window.__examData={"exam":"rbi","name":"RBI Grade B","total":738,"sections":[{"name":"General Awareness","count":584,"questions":[{"id":486,"text":"In the recently published Global Innovation Index (GII), India’s rank has improved to 48th in the year 2020. Its rank in the year 2019 was _________","options":[{"label":"A","text":"50th"},{"label":"B","text":"54th"},{"label":"C","text":"56th"},{"label":"D","text":"52nd"},{"label":"E","text":"58th"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":487,"text":"The International  Energy Agency has recently published the report “India Energy Outlook” for the year 2021. As per this report, at present, India is the _______ largest global energy consumer.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1st"},{"label":"B","text":"3rd"},{"label":"C","text":"4th"},{"label":"D","text":"8th"},{"label":"E","text":"10th"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":488,"text":"Ministry of Labour and Employment has published 4 labour codes in the year 2020. These codes are aimed at protecting the interest of workers and will provide them social security, protection, safe working  environment and effective conciliation, mechanism for their grievances. Which one of the following is not one these four labour codes published by the Labour Ministry?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Code on Wages, 2019"},{"label":"B","text":"Code on Migrant Laborers , 2020"},{"label":"C","text":"Industrial Relations Code, 2020"},{"label":"D","text":"Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code, 2020"},{"label":"E","text":"Code on Social Security, 2020"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":489,"text":"An integrated logistics and hyperscale data centre park called Green base and Yotta is going to be set up by Hiranandani Group companies, in which one of the following states?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"West Bengal"},{"label":"B","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"C","text":"Kerala"},{"label":"D","text":"Karnataka"},{"label":"E","text":"Haryana"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":490,"text":"India -Maldives joint military exercise ‘Ex EKUVERIN – 2019’ was held in which place?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Jodhpur"},{"label":"B","text":"Visakhapatnam"},{"label":"C","text":"Pune"},{"label":"D","text":"Dehradun"},{"label":"E","text":"Balasore"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":491,"text":"Amazon’s market value was $250 billion in the year 2015, two decades after its founding in the year 1995. This major e -commerce company was started as which of the following in its earliest days?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pantry"},{"label":"B","text":"Apparel store"},{"label":"C","text":"Courier store"},{"label":"D","text":"Book store"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":492,"text":"Union Minister of State for Agriculture Shri Parshottam Rupala has recently introduced AYUSHMAN SAHAKAR. It is a unique scheme to assist cooperatives play an important role in the creation of ___________ infrastructure in the country, under National Coop erative Development Cooperation (NCDC).","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Education"},{"label":"B","text":"Healthcare"},{"label":"C","text":"Employment"},{"label":"D","text":"Banking"},{"label":"E","text":"All of these"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":493,"text":"Indian Finance Minister Arun Jaitley introduced a GIS -based Mobile App for financial inclusion in the year 2018 during Annual Public Sector Banks meeting. This App assists  the common people in finding a financial service touch point at any location in the country. What is the name of this mobile app?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"CSC"},{"label":"B","text":"UMANG"},{"label":"C","text":"BHIM"},{"label":"D","text":"Jan Dhan Darshak"},{"label":"E","text":"Aaykar Setu"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":494,"text":"___________ was the first microlending bank in India to win a banking license from the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) in April 2014.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Equitas Bank"},{"label":"B","text":"Bandhan Bank"},{"label":"C","text":"Ashirvad Bank"},{"label":"D","text":"Aarohan Bank"},{"label":"E","text":"IDFC First Bank"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":495,"text":"Ranthambore National Park is located near which one of the following cities of Rajasthan?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Jaipur"},{"label":"B","text":"Udaipur"},{"label":"C","text":"Sikar"},{"label":"D","text":"Sawai Madhopur"},{"label":"E","text":"Bhilwara"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":496,"text":"The Union budget for the year 2021 -22 has allocated ₹1.1 trillion for the Indian Railways, out of this amount how much will  be utilized for capital expenditure for 2021 -22 to expand rail infrastructure in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹1.07 trillion"},{"label":"B","text":"₹1.02 trillion"},{"label":"C","text":"₹0.95 trillion"},{"label":"D","text":"₹1.04 trillion"},{"label":"E","text":"₹1.09 trillion"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":497,"text":"Denmark has decided to build the world’s first artificial island with the aim to provide clean energy. The island will be located in the North Sea (located between England and Scotland). Power will be generated from which of the following energies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Solar"},{"label":"B","text":"Tidal"},{"label":"C","text":"Wind"},{"label":"D","text":"Geothermal"},{"label":"E","text":"Biomass"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":498,"text":"Identify which among the following festivals is celebrated by the Apatani, or Tanw, also known by Apa, the tribal group living in the Ziro valley in the Lower Subansiri district of Arunachal Pradesh in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Myoko"},{"label":"B","text":"Gauchar Mela"},{"label":"C","text":"Thisam Phanit"},{"label":"D","text":"Tsukhenyie"},{"label":"E","text":"None of these"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":499,"text":"Identify which among the following PSUs has featured on top of the list among “Indian PSUs” in 'World's Best Employer 2020' Report, published by Forbes in the month of October 2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"ONGC"},{"label":"B","text":"BHEL"},{"label":"C","text":"NTPC"},{"label":"D","text":"SAIL"},{"label":"E","text":"IOCL"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":500,"text":"National Cadet Corps (NCC) of India, which is the largest uniformed youth organisation in the world, has celebrated its 72nd Raising Day on which of the following dates, in the year 2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"22nd December"},{"label":"B","text":"24th December"},{"label":"C","text":"25th October"},{"label":"D","text":"24th November"},{"label":"E","text":"22nd November"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":501,"text":"Identify the bank that has introduced “Gram Sampark Abhiyan”, a nation -wide Financial Inclusion and Literacy Campaign on the occasion of the 151st birth anniversary of Mahatma Gandhi, in the year 2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"SBI"},{"label":"B","text":"PNB"},{"label":"C","text":"HDFC"},{"label":"D","text":"BoI"},{"label":"E","text":"BoB"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":502,"text":"CRA is an agency registered under Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority (PFRDA) to perform functions of record -keeping, accounting, administration, and customer service to Pension scheme subscribers. What does “R” stand for in CRA?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Registry"},{"label":"B","text":"Record Keeping"},{"label":"C","text":"Resolution"},{"label":"D","text":"Real -Time"},{"label":"E","text":"Regulation"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":503,"text":"Real Time Gross Settlement (RTGS) system is primarily meant for large value transactions. The minimum amount to initiate a transaction through RTGS is ________ with no upper or maximum ceiling.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 2 lakhs"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 3 lakhs"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 5 lakhs"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 4 lakhs"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs. 1 lakh"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":504,"text":"The Ministry  of New and Renewable Energy (MNRE) has introduced the scheme PM KUSUM for farmers with the aim to add solar and other renewable capacity of 25,750 MW by 2022. Consider the following  given statements regarding this scheme and identify the one which is not a feature of the same?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Subsidy would be provided on diesel for running diesel pumps  and thus provide the"},{"label":"B","text":"Individual farmers will be supported to install standalone solar Agriculture pumps"},{"label":"C","text":"The farmer will be able to use the generated solar power to meet the irrigation needs and"},{"label":"D","text":"In case cultivated fields are chosen for setting up solar power projects , the farmers could"},{"label":"E","text":"The scheme would ensure that sufficient local solar/ other renewable energy -based"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":505,"text":"Cyclone Nivar made a landfall near which one of the following places, recently in the month of November 2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mumbai"},{"label":"B","text":"Puducherry"},{"label":"C","text":"Hyderabad"},{"label":"D","text":"Mysuru"},{"label":"E","text":"Kochi"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":506,"text":"In recent news, in the month of October 2020, World Economic Forum (WEF) has declared to set up India’s first Advanced Manufacturing HUB or AMHUB in w hich of the foll owing states?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Tamil Nadu"},{"label":"B","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"C","text":"Chhattisgarh"},{"label":"D","text":"Odisha"},{"label":"E","text":"Jharkhand"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":507,"text":"PM Kisan is a Central Sector scheme with 100% funding from Government of India. Who among the following are not eligible to avail the benefit of PM Kisan scheme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Large landholding farmer families"},{"label":"B","text":"Former and present holders of constitutional posts"},{"label":"C","text":"All eligible landholding farmer families"},{"label":"D","text":"Both A & B"},{"label":"E","text":"None of these"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":508,"text":"In the recently published Union Budget 2021 -22, what amount of funds  has been allocated under the revamped Post Matric Scholarship Scheme (PMSS) for the welfare of Scheduled Castes for 6 years, to benefit 4 crore SC students?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹35,219 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"₹25,219 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"₹32,117 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"₹22,117 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"₹27,115 crore"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":509,"text":"In recent news, in the month of February 2021, Puducherry Chief Minister V. Narayanasamy has submitted his resignation to Lieutenant Governor Tamilisai Soundararajan, after losing a confidence  vote in the Legislative  Assembly . The Puducherry Legislative Assembly has _________ seats.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"27"},{"label":"B","text":"35"},{"label":"C","text":"28"},{"label":"D","text":"33"},{"label":"E","text":"39"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":510,"text":"In Feb 2021, Ngozi Okonjo -Iweala was appointed as the seventh Director -General of the World Trade Organization, becoming the first woman head of the body. She belongs to which of the following countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ethiopia"},{"label":"B","text":"Nigeria"},{"label":"C","text":"Kenya"},{"label":"D","text":"Eritrea"},{"label":"E","text":"Algeria"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":511,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India has constructed a composite Digital Payments Index (DPI) to capture the extent of digitisation of payments across the country. Which one of the following is not a parameter that enables the measurement of deepening and penetr ation of digital payments in the country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Payment Enabler"},{"label":"B","text":"Payment Infrastructure"},{"label":"C","text":"Payment Analysis"},{"label":"D","text":"Payment Performance"},{"label":"E","text":"Consumer Centricity"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":512,"text":"__________ is the art and science of making maps and charts.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Demography"},{"label":"B","text":"Calligraphy"},{"label":"C","text":"Cartography"},{"label":"D","text":"Orthography"},{"label":"E","text":"Cacography"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":513,"text":"HCL Technologies has declared to roll out a one -time special bonus of Rs 700 crore to its employees globally, in recognition of its recent milestone of crossing the _________ mark in revenue for 2020.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"$15 billion"},{"label":"B","text":"$10 billion"},{"label":"C","text":"$50 billion"},{"label":"D","text":"$25 billion"},{"label":"E","text":"$30 billion"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":514,"text":"What is the current ceiling of Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR) set by the Reserve Bank of India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5%"},{"label":"B","text":"3%"},{"label":"C","text":"6%"},{"label":"D","text":"2.5%"},{"label":"E","text":"None of these"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":515,"text":"In recent news, in the month of Jan 2021, a certification course “NAVRITIH” was introduced by Prime Minister Narendra Modi. It is related to which of the following sectors?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Education Technology"},{"label":"B","text":"Construction Technology"},{"label":"C","text":"Food Processing and Technology"},{"label":"D","text":"Financial Technology"},{"label":"E","text":"None of these"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":516,"text":"In recent news, in the month of December 2020, Government of India has declared to set up a Multi -Modal Logistics Hub & Multi -Modal Transport Hub (MMTH), with the aim of making India a strong part of the Global  Value Chain. In which of the following  states will it be set up?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Uttar Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"C","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"E","text":"Tamil Nadu"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":517,"text":"In recent news, in the month of February 2021, ____ INS Karanj - a Scorpene class submarine has been handed over to the Indian  Navy by Mazagon Dock Limited.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"First"},{"label":"B","text":"Sixth"},{"label":"C","text":"Third"},{"label":"D","text":"Fourth"},{"label":"E","text":"Fifth"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":518,"text":"Identify which among the following Small Finance Banks has got the permission from SEBI to launch its IPO in the month of December 2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ujjivan Small Finance Bank"},{"label":"B","text":"Janalakshmi Small Finance Bank"},{"label":"C","text":"Capital Small Finance Bank."},{"label":"D","text":"Equitas Small Finance Bank"},{"label":"E","text":"Suryodaya Small Finance Bank"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":519,"text":"ATMs that are owned and operated by non -bank entities are called as _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Blue Label ATMs"},{"label":"B","text":"White Label ATMs"},{"label":"C","text":"Brown Label ATMs"},{"label":"D","text":"Black Label ATMs"},{"label":"E","text":"Red Label ATMs"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":520,"text":"Good Governance Day in India is observed on December 25th. This day is observed to commemorate the birth anniversary of which of the following Indian personalities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sardar Vallabh Bhai Patel"},{"label":"B","text":"Atal Bihari Vajpayee"},{"label":"C","text":"Swami Vivekananda"},{"label":"D","text":"Madan Mohan Malviya"},{"label":"E","text":"Pt. Deen Dayal Upadhyaya"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":521,"text":"Identify which among the following is NOT a policy rate that is changed by the Reserve  Bank of India (RBI) from time to time?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Repo Rate"},{"label":"B","text":"Reverse Repo Rate"},{"label":"C","text":"Statutory Liquidity Ratio"},{"label":"D","text":"Marginal Standing Facility Rate"},{"label":"E","text":"Bank Rate"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":522,"text":"In recent news, in the month of December 2020, “iMobile app” was introduced by ICICI Bank with the aim to strengthen the financial  ecosystem of the country. Read the below given statements and determine which is NOT correct regarding the features of this","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It enables users to pre -set limits on their credit and debit cards for domestic as well as"},{"label":"B","text":"It allows customers to link multiple bank accounts."},{"label":"C","text":"It can be used only by the customers of ICICI Bank."},{"label":"D","text":"It allows customers to scan a QR Code of any payment app and send money  to any UPI ID,"},{"label":"E","text":"It lets its customers open (and renew) Life Insurance and General Insurance policies, directly"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":523,"text":"The Government  has introduced the New  National Education Policy 2020 . As per it ______% is the target Gross enrolment ratio  (GER) for pre -school to secondary level by the year 2030 and _____% is the target GER of higher education by 2035.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"100, 50"},{"label":"B","text":"75, 50"},{"label":"C","text":"50, 100"},{"label":"D","text":"50, 75"},{"label":"E","text":"100, 75"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":524,"text":"The state of Maharashtra has topped the list of states in terms  of MSME registration in Udyam Portal. Identify which among the following states is second after Maharashtra as per a newspaper report, published recently in February 2021?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"B","text":"Kerala"},{"label":"C","text":"Tamil Nadu"},{"label":"D","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"E","text":"Haryana"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":525,"text":"In recent news, in the month of October 2020, the Government has notified that a “National Authority of Ship Recycling” will be set up to look after the sustainable development of the Ship Recycling industry, monitoring the compliance to environment -friendly  norms. In which of the following states will it be located?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"B","text":"Andhra Pradesh"},{"label":"C","text":"Kerala"},{"label":"D","text":"Maharashtra"},{"label":"E","text":"Goa"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":526,"text":"As per the recently published guidelines by RBI in October 2020, Non -deposit - taking HFCs with an asset size of ₹5,000 crore and above, but less than ₹10,000 crore will have to reach a minimum LCR of _____ by December 1, 2021 and _______ by Decemb er 1, 2025.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"20%, 40%"},{"label":"B","text":"30%, 60%"},{"label":"C","text":"30%, 100%"},{"label":"D","text":"50%, 100%"},{"label":"E","text":"25%, 50%"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":527,"text":"Identify which among the following states  is set to be home to the country’s first sand dune park under a project funded by the World Bank, which has accepted the proposal of the Biodiversity Board of the state, recently in October 2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Maharashtra"},{"label":"B","text":"Goa"},{"label":"C","text":"Kerala"},{"label":"D","text":"Odisha"},{"label":"E","text":"Gujarat"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":528,"text":"What is the current Marginal Standing Facility Rate, in the month of February 2021?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"4.75%"},{"label":"B","text":"3.50%"},{"label":"C","text":"3.25%"},{"label":"D","text":"4.50%"},{"label":"E","text":"4.25%"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":529,"text":"A women’s Self -Help Group (SHG), coming together on the basis of mutual affinity, is the primary building block of community institutional design of which of the schemes, being run by the  Government of India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"MGNREGA"},{"label":"B","text":"DAY - NRLM"},{"label":"C","text":"PMGSY"},{"label":"D","text":"Gram Swaraj Abhiyan"},{"label":"E","text":"None of these"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":530,"text":"India’s First Fire Park has been opened in which of the following states in the month of January 2021?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Assam"},{"label":"B","text":"Haryana"},{"label":"C","text":"Karnataka"},{"label":"D","text":"Odisha"},{"label":"E","text":"Kerala"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":531,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India has proposed to increase the minimum Net Owned Fund (NOF) for Housing Finance Companies (HFCs) from the current requirement of Rs ________to Rs 20 crore.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"15 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"10 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"8 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"12 crore"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":532,"text":"The year 2021 commemorates ________anniversary of the signing of the Ramsar Convention on Wetlands on 2nd February in Ramsar, Iran, celebrated annually as World Wetlands Day.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"45th"},{"label":"B","text":"70th"},{"label":"C","text":"50th"},{"label":"D","text":"75th"},{"label":"E","text":"100th"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":533,"text":"The world’s longest highway tunnel named as “Atal Tunnel” has been opened  by Prime Minister Narendra Modi in the month of October 2020 . It connects which of the following two places?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Manali -Leh"},{"label":"B","text":"Jammu -Baramulla"},{"label":"C","text":"Srinagar -Jammu"},{"label":"D","text":"Srinagar -Kargil"},{"label":"E","text":"Kullu -Manali"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":534,"text":"In recent news, in the month February 2020, which of the following companies has declared plans to launch  online engineering courses that will focus on three areas — employability assessment and recruitment, reinforced learning, reskilling and vocational skills training?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Larson & Toubro"},{"label":"B","text":"Bharti Airtel"},{"label":"C","text":"Reliance"},{"label":"D","text":"Infosys"},{"label":"E","text":"Wipro"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":535,"text":"In recent news, (September 2020), Bayer’s Better Life Farming initiative has declared partnership with which of the following banks in India to provide holistic financial solutions to smallholder farmers and rural farming communities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Axis Bank"},{"label":"B","text":"HDFC Bank"},{"label":"C","text":"ICICI Bank"},{"label":"D","text":"IDBI Bank"},{"label":"E","text":"IDFC First Bank"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":536,"text":"What is the Bank Credit to GDP ratio in India, as of March  2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"75%"},{"label":"B","text":"100%"},{"label":"C","text":"50%"},{"label":"D","text":"60%"},{"label":"E","text":"85%"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":537,"text":"The WHO Foundation has appointed Indian -origin global health expert Anil Soni as its first ____________ in the month of January 2021.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chief Medical Advisor"},{"label":"B","text":"Chief Executive Officer"},{"label":"C","text":"Chief Health Expert"},{"label":"D","text":"Chief Operations Officer"},{"label":"E","text":"Chief Research Scientist"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":538,"text":"Tata Steel has recently (in February 20201) declared the plans to double its steel producing capacity from the current to _______ million tonnes, in consideration of the expanding steel demand.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"20"},{"label":"B","text":"40"},{"label":"C","text":"60"},{"label":"D","text":"50"},{"label":"E","text":"25"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":539,"text":"India’s largest Public Sector Bank SBI is expecting its home loan portfolio to touch Rs 7 lakh crore by the year_______, where demand is being driven by an increased desire among the youth to own homes early in life, rising incomes, and government pol icies like the cuts in stamp duty and subsidy.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2020 -23"},{"label":"B","text":"2029 -30"},{"label":"C","text":"2030 -31"},{"label":"D","text":"2023 -24"},{"label":"E","text":"2021 -22"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":540,"text":"In the month of February 2021, West Indies has recently defeated Bangladesh in a test match after chasing a target of 395 runs. This was ______ highest run chase in the history of test matches.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1st"},{"label":"B","text":"2nd"},{"label":"C","text":"5th"},{"label":"D","text":"4th"},{"label":"E","text":"6th"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":541,"text":"The Japanese  government is going to join the ‘Five Eyes’ intelligence -sharing alliance. The island nation is on its way to become the ‘sixth eye’. Which one of the following countries is not a part of the ‘Five Eyes’ group?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"China"},{"label":"B","text":"Australia"},{"label":"C","text":"Britain"},{"label":"D","text":"Canada"},{"label":"E","text":"New Zealand"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":542,"text":"In the month of December 2020, The Olympic Council of Asia has declared that Doha, Qatar will host the 2030 Asian Games while _________ will host the 2034 edition.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Beijing, China"},{"label":"B","text":"Tokyo, Japan"},{"label":"C","text":"Riyadh, Saudi Arabia"},{"label":"D","text":"Abu Dhabi, UAE"},{"label":"E","text":"New Delhi, India"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":543,"text":"India's first digital asset management platform called __________, has been formally introduced in Tamil Nadu under Centre's ambitious ''Atmanirbhar\" initiative, in December 2020.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Assetboxx"},{"label":"B","text":"DigiPal"},{"label":"C","text":"SUVIDHA"},{"label":"D","text":"Digiboxx"},{"label":"E","text":"SUNIDHI"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":544,"text":"The RBI has published the Annual Report “Ombudsman Schemes of the Reserve Bank for the year 2019 -20”, in the month of February 2021. The Banking Ombudsman Scheme (BOS) was first notified by the Reserve Bank in the year _____ under Section 35A of the Banking Regulation Act, 1949.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1948"},{"label":"B","text":"2005"},{"label":"C","text":"2010"},{"label":"D","text":"1995"},{"label":"E","text":"2000"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":545,"text":"Identify which among the following banks has emerged as the top player among the 100 Banking, Financial Services and Insurance (BFSI) companies in India, as per the recently published report in the month of December 2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Axis Bank"},{"label":"B","text":"Bandhan Bank"},{"label":"C","text":"HDFC Bank"},{"label":"D","text":"ICICI Bank"},{"label":"E","text":"Yes Bank"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":546,"text":"The Government of India has decided to extend the benefit of the Scheme for “Remission of Duties and Taxes on Exported Products” (RoDTEP) to all export goods with effect from 1st January, 2021. This scheme will replace ______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Export Promotion Capital Goods Schemes"},{"label":"B","text":"Service Exports From India Scheme (SEIS)"},{"label":"C","text":"Merchandise Exports From India Scheme (MEIS)"},{"label":"D","text":"Both B & C"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":547,"text":"Cairn  Energy, a _______ firm has filed a case in a district court of USA (in Feb 2021) to enforce a $1.2  billion arbitration award that was by it in a tax dispute against India.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"British"},{"label":"B","text":"Russia"},{"label":"C","text":"Swedish"},{"label":"D","text":"Chinese"},{"label":"E","text":"Canadian"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":548,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India had constituted an Internal Working Group (IWG) in June 2020 to review the extant ownership guidelines and corporate structure for Indian private sector banks. Refer to the statements given below and identify which of the  following is/are the recommendation(s) of this IWG, as per its report submitted in Nov 2020. i. Large corporate/industrial houses May be allowed as promoters of banks only after necessary amendments to the Banking Regulation Act, 1949 and strengthening of the supervisory mechanism for large conglomerates, including consolidated supervision. ii. For Payments Banks intending to convert to a Small Finance Bank, track record of 3 years of experience as Payments Bank May be considered as sufficient. iii. The cap on promoters’ stake in the long run (15 years) May be raised from the current level of 15 percent to 26 percent of the paid -up voting equity share capital of the bank.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only i & ii"},{"label":"B","text":"Only ii & iii"},{"label":"C","text":"All of the above"},{"label":"D","text":"Only i & iii"},{"label":"E","text":"Only i"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":549,"text":"Consider the following statements regarding the features of Senior Citizen Saving Scheme (SCSS) and identify the correct answer out of the options given below :","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Deposits in SCSS qualify for deduction u/s 80C of Income Tax Act."},{"label":"B","text":"A retired personnel of Defence Services ( excluding civilian defence employees), who has"},{"label":"C","text":"A depositor May open an account individually or jointly with a spouse ."},{"label":"D","text":"Both A & B"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":550,"text":"The Tso Kar is a Salt Lake which is also a high -altitude wetland complex . It is situated in the Rupshu plateau located in which of the following places?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sikkim"},{"label":"B","text":"Himachal Pradesh"},{"label":"C","text":"Manipur"},{"label":"D","text":"Ladakh"},{"label":"E","text":"Arunachal Pradesh"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":551,"text":"In recent news, in the month of December 2020, the cabinet has cleared the PM -WANI scheme. It aims to provide which of the following services?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mobile Banking"},{"label":"B","text":"Radio"},{"label":"C","text":"Wi -Fi"},{"label":"D","text":"Digital Education"},{"label":"E","text":"Mobile Networks"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":552,"text":"Jigmet Dolma, an SPO of Ladakh Police has recently secured __________ position in the Dhaka Marathon 2021, organised in the month of January 2021.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"second"},{"label":"B","text":"first"},{"label":"C","text":"third"},{"label":"D","text":"fourth"},{"label":"E","text":"fifth"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":553,"text":"The Spices Board of India has set an ambitious target, in the month of February 2021, of achieving an export value of $5 billion by 2025 and $_____ billion by the year 2030.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10"},{"label":"B","text":"15"},{"label":"D","text":"50"},{"label":"E","text":"20"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":554,"text":"In the month of February 2021, Seychelles has become the first country to welcome the tourists that have been vaccinated against COVID -19. Seychelles is located in the Indian Ocean, nearest to which of the following countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"label":"B","text":"Maldives"},{"label":"C","text":"Malaysia"},{"label":"D","text":"Madagascar"},{"label":"E","text":"South Africa"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":555,"text":"International Tea Day is observed globally on which of the following dates?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"25th Jan"},{"label":"B","text":"21st May"},{"label":"C","text":"21st Jan"},{"label":"D","text":"25th May"},{"label":"E","text":"28th June"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":556,"text":"UNDP has notified 17 Sustainable Goals (SDGs) to be attained by the year 2030. SDG 5 is related to which of the following?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"No Poverty"},{"label":"B","text":"Zero Hunger"},{"label":"C","text":"Quality Education"},{"label":"D","text":"Gender Equality"},{"label":"E","text":"Clean Water and Sanitation"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":557,"text":"The International Olympic Committee (IOC) has its headquarters located in which of the following places?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rome, Italy"},{"label":"B","text":"Paris, France"},{"label":"C","text":"Geneva, Switzerland"},{"label":"D","text":"Lausanne, Switzerland"},{"label":"E","text":"Bern, Switzerland"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":558,"text":"In recent news, in the month of Jan 2021, NITI Aayog has published the second edition of India Innovation Index. Identify which among the following has topped in the category of major states?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Himachal Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Karnataka"},{"label":"C","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"D","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"E","text":"None of these"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":559,"text":"Where is the headquarters of the International Olympic Committee located?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Italy"},{"label":"B","text":"Switzerland"},{"label":"C","text":"Belgium"},{"label":"D","text":"France"},{"label":"E","text":"UK"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":560,"text":"Section 80C of the Income Tax Act allows a maximum deduction of Rs _________every year from the taxpayer’s total income. The benefit of this deduction can be availed by Individuals and HUFs. Companies, partnership firms, LLPs cannot avail the benefit of this deduction.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 1 lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 2.5 lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 5 lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 1.5 lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs. 3.5 lakh"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":561,"text":"The Government  of India has decided to celebrate Subhash Chandra Bose’s birthday on the _________ every year as “PARAKRAM DIWAS”, starting from the year 2021.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"25th day of February"},{"label":"B","text":"23rd day of February"},{"label":"C","text":"25th day of January"},{"label":"D","text":"23rd day of January"},{"label":"E","text":"2nd day of March"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":562,"text":"In recent news, in the month of Oct 2020, Andorra has become _________ member of the International  Monetary Fund.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"190th"},{"label":"B","text":"185th"},{"label":"C","text":"195th"},{"label":"D","text":"191st"},{"label":"E","text":"193rd"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":563,"text":"In recent news, the Reserve Bank has come out with a five -pillared strategic approach 'GUARD' to deal with cybersecurity threats being faced by urban cooperative banks (UCBs). What does A in GUARD stands for?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Automatic regulation"},{"label":"B","text":"Agency"},{"label":"C","text":"Appropriate Regulation"},{"label":"D","text":"Authorisation"},{"label":"E","text":"Autonomous"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":564,"text":"Kasturba Gandhi Balika Vidyalaya is a scheme introduced by the Government of India for  the school girls of SC, ST, OBC and minority communities , from the classes of __________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1st to 5th"},{"label":"B","text":"6th to 10th"},{"label":"C","text":"6th to 12th"},{"label":"D","text":"11th & 12th"},{"label":"E","text":"9th to 12th"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":565,"text":"The Finance Ministry has extended the ‘Emergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme’ (ECLGS) to support  MSMEs  engaged in travel, tourism and hospitality sectors to overcome the impact of the COVID -19 pandemic impact. The scheme will be expanded by  _______ to ₹5 lakh crore.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹25,000 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"₹30,000 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"₹35,000 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"₹45,000 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"₹50,000 crore"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":566,"text":"The Reserve Bank has declared a hike in cash reserve ratio (CRR) by 50 basis points to 4.5 per cent. It has been effective from _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"May 05, 2022"},{"label":"B","text":"May 14, 2022"},{"label":"C","text":"May 18, 2022"},{"label":"D","text":"May 21, 2022"},{"label":"E","text":"May 23, 2022"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":567,"text":"National Coal Miner’s Day is observed on which date in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"May 2nd"},{"label":"B","text":"May 4th"},{"label":"C","text":"May 9th"},{"label":"D","text":"May 12th"},{"label":"E","text":"May 15th"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":568,"text":"As per the National Education Policy 2020, government aims to increase the public investment in the education sector from the current 4.3 per cent to reach ____ per cent of GDP at the earliest.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5.2"},{"label":"B","text":"5.5"},{"label":"C","text":"6.0"},{"label":"D","text":"6.5"},{"label":"E","text":"7.0"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":569,"text":"The Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA) has tightened the rules for Nidhi Companies, according to which company needs to have atleast 200 members and should have a net owned fund (NOF) of Rs _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"15 lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"18 lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"20 lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"25 lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"30 lakh"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":570,"text":"Where is Louvre Museum located?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"France"},{"label":"B","text":"Italy"},{"label":"C","text":"Germany"},{"label":"D","text":"Netherlands"},{"label":"E","text":"Spain"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":571,"text":"How many member countries are there in the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"36"},{"label":"B","text":"37"},{"label":"C","text":"38"},{"label":"D","text":"39"},{"label":"E","text":"40"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":572,"text":"ISRO has declared to launch a spacecraft to orbit Venus, which is scheduled by _______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"December 2023"},{"label":"B","text":"November 2024"},{"label":"C","text":"September 2023"},{"label":"D","text":"August 2024"},{"label":"E","text":"December 2024"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":573,"text":"Interest rate on employees' provident fund deposits was cut to a four -decade low of ____ per cent for the 2021 -22 fiscal from 8.5 per cent in the previous year.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"8.4%"},{"label":"B","text":"8.3%"},{"label":"C","text":"8.2%"},{"label":"D","text":"8.1%"},{"label":"E","text":"8.0%"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":574,"text":"Presently, ______ Debt Recovery Tribunals and 5 Debts Recovery Appellate Tribunals are functioning across the country.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"33"},{"label":"B","text":"36"},{"label":"C","text":"39"},{"label":"D","text":"41"},{"label":"E","text":"47"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":575,"text":"As per data published by the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (IRDAI), ______ insurance company consolidated its position as the second -largest general insurance company with an 11% market share, up from 10% last year.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"HDFC Life"},{"label":"B","text":"ICICI Lombard"},{"label":"C","text":"Max Life Insurance"},{"label":"D","text":"PNB Metlife"},{"label":"E","text":"Reliance General Insurance"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":576,"text":"Ministry of Social Justice has recently introduced the DACE Scheme from BHU, Uttar Pradesh. What does ‘E’ stand for in the acronym DACE?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Excellence"},{"label":"B","text":"Empowerment"},{"label":"C","text":"Encouragement"},{"label":"D","text":"Entrepreneurship"},{"label":"E","text":"Employment"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":577,"text":"Dabang Delhi KC beat ____ to win the Pro Kabaddi League Season 8 Champions.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Telugu Titans"},{"label":"B","text":"Patna Pirates"},{"label":"C","text":"Puneri Paltan"},{"label":"D","text":"Bengaluru Bulls"},{"label":"E","text":"Bengal Warriors"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":578,"text":"The Singareni  Collieries Company Limited (SCCL) is a Government coal mining company jointly owned by the  Government of ________ and Government of India  on a 51:49 equity basis.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Andhra Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Karnataka"},{"label":"C","text":"Odisha"},{"label":"D","text":"Telangana"},{"label":"E","text":"Maharashtra"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":579,"text":"The Union Cabinet approved an additional subsidy of  Rs. _____ crore  for phosphate - based fertilisers for the upcoming kharif season (April -September), seeking to shield farmers from any additional burden due to a sharp increase in input costs globally.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 35,935"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 38,938"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 69,939"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 45,945"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs. 50,955"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":580,"text":"India’s monthly merchandise exports remained above US$ _____ billion for the first time, during FY 2021 – 2022.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"38"},{"label":"B","text":"40"},{"label":"C","text":"43"},{"label":"D","text":"47"},{"label":"E","text":"49"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":581,"text":"Centre has recently (April 2022) introduced “Azadi Se Antyodaya Tak campaign”, which is a _____ day campaign,  with a mission to saturate 75 districts.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"75"},{"label":"B","text":"90"},{"label":"C","text":"120"},{"label":"D","text":"130"},{"label":"E","text":"150"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":582,"text":"Monthly Premium made by India citizen at 18 years of age, under Atal Pension Yojana, opting for Rs. 5000 monthly pension after attaining 60 years of age,  is Rs. ______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"185"},{"label":"B","text":"210"},{"label":"C","text":"225"},{"label":"D","text":"305"},{"label":"E","text":"324"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":583,"text":"Which airport has bagged the 'Covid champion' award at Wings India 2022, which is Asia's largest event on civil aviation jointly organised by the Ministry of Civil Aviation and FICCI?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Delhi International Airport Limited (DIAL)"},{"label":"B","text":"Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel International Airport"},{"label":"C","text":"Lokpriya Gopinath Bordoloi International Airport"},{"label":"D","text":"Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj International Airport"},{"label":"E","text":"Cochin International Airport Limited (CIAL)"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":584,"text":"Which state won the final match of “Santosh Trophy”, one of India's oldest football tournaments, held recently at the Manjeri Payyanad Stadium?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Kerala"},{"label":"B","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"C","text":"Tamil Nadu"},{"label":"D","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"E","text":"Meghalaya"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":585,"text":"As per the National Family Health Survey (NFHS) conducted in 2019 -21, India's sex ratio in urban areas is _____ females per every 1,000 males and  ______ females per every 1,000 males in rural areas.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"958, 984"},{"label":"B","text":"967, 997"},{"label":"C","text":"985, 1037"},{"label":"D","text":"979, 1019"},{"label":"E","text":"972, 1026"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":586,"text":"In recent news, the State of the World's Forests 2022 (SOFO 2022) was published by the   _______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP)"},{"label":"B","text":"United Nations Development Programme (UNDP)"},{"label":"C","text":"United Nations Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)"},{"label":"D","text":"International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN)"},{"label":"E","text":"Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC)"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":587,"text":"The Geological Survey of India (GSI) has approved the setting up of the country's first geo park at  Lamheta village, in which state of India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"B","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"C","text":"Jharkhand"},{"label":"D","text":"Uttar Pradesh"},{"label":"E","text":"West Bengal"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":588,"text":"India's wave of unicorns reaches an all -time high with Open – a  _____ becoming the 100th unicorn in the country.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"e-Commerce Platform"},{"label":"B","text":"Fintech Neobank"},{"label":"C","text":"Social Startup"},{"label":"D","text":"Lifestyle brand"},{"label":"E","text":"Online fashion brand"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":589,"text":"Federal Reserves  System, also known as FED has recently got new chair of the Board of Governors for a term ending May 15, 2026. Federal Reserve was created in the year ____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1905"},{"label":"B","text":"1908"},{"label":"C","text":"1913"},{"label":"D","text":"1919"},{"label":"E","text":"1929"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":590,"text":"_______ has recently expanded its strategic partnership with SBI Cards and Payments Services Ltd to power the company's next leg of digital transformation.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Infosys Ltd"},{"label":"B","text":"Wipro Ltd"},{"label":"C","text":"Tata Consultancy Services (TCS)"},{"label":"D","text":"HCL Technologies"},{"label":"E","text":"Tech Mahindra"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":591,"text":"Consider the following statements about the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBS) 2016, and find out the correct statement – 1. These Regulations shall apply to the corporate insolvency resolution process. 2. An insolvency professional shall be eligible to be appointed as a resolution professional for a corporate insolvency resolution process of a corporate debtor. 3. A resolution professional shall make disclosures at the time of his appointment and thereafter in accordance with the Code of Conduct.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 2"},{"label":"B","text":"2 and 3"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 2"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":592,"text":"Germany has recently committed to provide additional support worth Euro 10 billion to India by the year _______ to support green growth initiatives.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2026"},{"label":"B","text":"2027"},{"label":"C","text":"2028"},{"label":"D","text":"2029"},{"label":"E","text":"2030"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":593,"text":"RBI has recently  decided  to increase the  repo rate  by 40 basis points (bps) in an off - cycle meeting in May 2022, citing  inflation  concerns. This is followed by a reduction in the policy  repo rate  by _____ basis points in March 2020, followed by reduction of 40 basis points in ___ ___.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"50, May 2020"},{"label":"B","text":"75, July 2020"},{"label":"C","text":"75, May 2020"},{"label":"D","text":"45, September 2020"},{"label":"E","text":"50, July 2020"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":594,"text":"Consider the following statements about PMJDY, and find out the correct one – 1. Overdraft limit doubled from Rs 5,000/ - to Rs 10,000/ 2. Free accidental insurance cover on RuPay cards increased from Rs. 1 lakh to Rs. 2 lakh for PMJDY accounts. 3. The person should normally be head of the family or an earning member of the family and should be in the age group of  18 to 70.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 2 and 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 1 and 2"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":595,"text":"What is the theme of World Water Day 2022?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nature for Water"},{"label":"B","text":"Leaving No One Behind"},{"label":"C","text":"Water and Climate Change"},{"label":"D","text":"Valuing Water"},{"label":"E","text":"Groundwater: making the invisible visible"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":596,"text":"City of Guadalajara has been named World Book Capital for the year 2022. It belongs to which country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Taiwan"},{"label":"B","text":"Mexico"},{"label":"C","text":"Brazil"},{"label":"D","text":"Morocco"},{"label":"E","text":"Indonesia"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":597,"text":"India's only BIS -approved national flag manufacturing unit is located in which of the following state?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Telangana"},{"label":"B","text":"Karnataka"},{"label":"C","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"D","text":"Kerala"},{"label":"E","text":"Tamil Nadu"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":598,"text":"The Regional Rural Banks Act, 1976 mainly provides for the incorporation, regulation and winding up of Regional Rural Banks (RRBs). The Act mandates that of the capital issued by a RRB, ___% shall be held by the central government, ___% by the concerned st ate government and ___% by the sponsor bank.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"35:50:15"},{"label":"B","text":"35:15:50"},{"label":"C","text":"50:35:15"},{"label":"D","text":"50:15:35"},{"label":"E","text":"15:35:50"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":599,"text":"What is the full form of UNCED?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United Nations Conference on Environment and Development"},{"label":"B","text":"United Nations Convention on Environment and Development"},{"label":"C","text":"United Nations Conference on Employment and Demographics"},{"label":"D","text":"United Nations Convention on Empowerment and Development"},{"label":"E","text":"United Nations Conference on Energy and Development"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":600,"text":"The government has allocated Rs ______ for Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM -Kisan) in the Union Budget 2022 -23, which is _____ higher than the Budget Estimates of Rs 65,000 crore for 2021 -22?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"60,000 crore, 4.2%"},{"label":"B","text":"55,000 crore, 7.3%"},{"label":"C","text":"68,000 crore, 4.6%"},{"label":"D","text":"72,000 crore, 5.4%"},{"label":"E","text":"80,000 crore, 8.9%"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":601,"text":"Who among the following has recently been appointed as (May 2022) the Google Policy Head in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Avinash Saha"},{"label":"B","text":"Rajeev Kumar"},{"label":"C","text":"Archana Gulati"},{"label":"D","text":"Sundar Arora"},{"label":"E","text":"Girish Mathur"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":602,"text":"Identify which among the following statements are correct with respect to National Apprenticeship Training Scheme. 1. It was introduced in 2016. 2. It has been extended till 2026. 3. It comes under Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship. 4. It provides Rs 9000 per month allowance to graduates and diploma holders in engineering, science and business.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 1, 2 and 4"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 2, 3 and 4"},{"label":"D","text":"Only 1, 3 and 4"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":603,"text":"Delimitation Commission for which of the following States/UTs has submitted its final report in May 2022?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ladakh"},{"label":"B","text":"Uttarakhand"},{"label":"C","text":"Jammu and Kashmir"},{"label":"D","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"E","text":"Arunachal Pradesh"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":604,"text":"Which of these statement is/are correct about the PM SVANidhi scheme? 1. The Scheme has been extended till 2024. 2. The approval is expected to benefit nearly 1.2 crore citizens of Urban India. 3. The loan amount under the scheme has increased the loan amount to Rs. 10000 crore","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 2 only"},{"label":"B","text":"1 and 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":605,"text":"Identify which among the following Oil and Marketing Companies (OMC) has recently (May, 2022) introduced M15 petrol?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"IOCL"},{"label":"B","text":"BPCL"},{"label":"C","text":"HPCL"},{"label":"D","text":"Nayara Energy"},{"label":"E","text":"Reliance Petroleum"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":606,"text":"In recent news, (April 2022), Indian Air Force in collaboration with which of the following companies has taken a leap forward in fuel supply chain management by introducing a ‘Fleet Card - Fuel on Move' for its varied fleet of vehicles?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bharat Petroleum"},{"label":"B","text":"Hindustan Petroleum"},{"label":"C","text":"Indian Oil Corporation"},{"label":"D","text":"Oil and Natural Gas Corporation"},{"label":"E","text":"Oil India Limited"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":607,"text":"Which of these country will host World Environment Day 2022 in June 2022?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Switzerland"},{"label":"B","text":"Sweden"},{"label":"C","text":"Finland"},{"label":"D","text":"Norway"},{"label":"E","text":"Italy"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":608,"text":"Nand Mulchandani has been appointed as Chief Technology Officer of _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI)"},{"label":"B","text":"European Space Agency"},{"label":"C","text":"National Investigation Agency (NIA)"},{"label":"D","text":"Central Investigation Agency (CIA)"},{"label":"E","text":"Interpol"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":609,"text":"As per Gold Monetization Schemes 2015, the Medium -Term Government Deposit (MTGD) can be withdrawn after _____ years.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"3 years"},{"label":"B","text":"4 years"},{"label":"C","text":"5 years"},{"label":"D","text":"6 years"},{"label":"E","text":"7 years"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":610,"text":"Which of these state has opened the country's first Greenfield grain -based ethanol plant?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bihar"},{"label":"B","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"C","text":"Odisha"},{"label":"D","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"E","text":"Telangana"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":611,"text":"“My Country My Life ”  is an autobiography of _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sheela Dixit"},{"label":"B","text":"Atal Bihari Vajpayee"},{"label":"C","text":"Lal Krishna Advani"},{"label":"D","text":"Jaswant Singh"},{"label":"E","text":"Manmohan Singh"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":612,"text":"Which of these is not among the top five sectors of National Monetization Pipeline?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Roads"},{"label":"B","text":"Railways"},{"label":"C","text":"Power"},{"label":"D","text":"Telecom"},{"label":"E","text":"Solar Energy"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":613,"text":"As per National Infrastructure Pipeline, which among the following sector is not among the top 4 sectors as per the sector -wise annual projected capital expenditure?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Energy"},{"label":"B","text":"Urban"},{"label":"C","text":"Social Infrastructure"},{"label":"D","text":"Railways"},{"label":"E","text":"Roads"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":614,"text":"GST Revenue collection has crossed 1.5 lakh crore for the first time in _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"March 2022"},{"label":"B","text":"April 2022"},{"label":"C","text":"May 2022"},{"label":"D","text":"January 2022"},{"label":"E","text":"February 2022"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":615,"text":"In recent news, (March 2022), which among the following Automatic Train Protection (ATP) System has been developed by Indian Railway on its own?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"KAVACH"},{"label":"B","text":"Trishool"},{"label":"C","text":"Dhaal"},{"label":"D","text":"PRAHAR"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":616,"text":"ASEEM Portal is related to_____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Livelihood and Employment"},{"label":"B","text":"Prevention of Human Trafficking"},{"label":"C","text":"Bootstrap startups"},{"label":"D","text":"Rural Development"},{"label":"E","text":"Promotion of MSMEs"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":617,"text":"The main objective of DESH Stack e Portal is to provide skilling, upskilling and reskilling opportunities through API -based platforms. In DESH what does ‘E’ stands for?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Employment"},{"label":"B","text":"Encouragement"},{"label":"C","text":"Empowerment"},{"label":"D","text":"Ecosystem"},{"label":"E","text":"Enlightenment"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":618,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India and _____ have declared the project to link Unified Payments Interface and PayNow for faster transactions. The UPI -PayNow linkage is targeted for operationalisation by July 2022.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Myanmar"},{"label":"B","text":"Maldives"},{"label":"C","text":"Germany"},{"label":"D","text":"Singapore"},{"label":"E","text":"Vietnam"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":619,"text":"National Forensic Science University has been set up under which among the following ministry?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ministry of Science and Technology"},{"label":"B","text":"Ministry of Home Affairs"},{"label":"C","text":"Ministry of Finance"},{"label":"D","text":"Ministry of Health and Family Welfare"},{"label":"E","text":"Prime Minister's Office"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":620,"text":"Cyclone Asani, which developed over southeast regions of Bay of Bengal and intensified into a 'severe cyclone' was named by _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bangladesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Myanmar"},{"label":"C","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"label":"D","text":"Thailand"},{"label":"E","text":"Indonesia"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":621,"text":"Financial Stability Board represents which of the following organization?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"SCO"},{"label":"B","text":"G-7"},{"label":"C","text":"G-20"},{"label":"D","text":"ASEAN"},{"label":"E","text":"BIMSTEC"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":622,"text":"Identify which among the following statement is/are correct about interest rate and bond price? 1. Interest rate is negatively related to bond prices. 2. If interest rate and yield is rising bond prices will fall. 3. Interest rate positively related to bond prices.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 1 and 2"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 2 and 3"},{"label":"D","text":"All 1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":623,"text":"India has recently become the only country to adopt the T+1 settlement system after ________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"China"},{"label":"B","text":"Russia"},{"label":"C","text":"United States of America"},{"label":"D","text":"Germany"},{"label":"E","text":"Canada"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":624,"text":"T Raja Kumar, a senior advisor at MHA, has been appointed as the president of the Financial Action Task Force (FATF), the global money laundering and terrorism financing watchdog. He is from which country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nepal"},{"label":"B","text":"Bhutan"},{"label":"C","text":"Singapore"},{"label":"D","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"label":"E","text":"Thailand"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":625,"text":"The Sagarmala programme is the flagship programme of the Ministry of Shipping to promote port -led development in the country through _____ of potentially navigable waterways maritime trade routes.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"7500 km"},{"label":"B","text":"8600 km"},{"label":"C","text":"12300 km"},{"label":"D","text":"13750 km"},{"label":"E","text":"14500 km"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":626,"text":"What is India’s Rank in Global Fisheries Protection?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1st"},{"label":"B","text":"2nd"},{"label":"C","text":"3rd"},{"label":"D","text":"4th"},{"label":"E","text":"5th"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":627,"text":"Identify which among the following has won the ‘Khelo India University Games 2021’?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"JAIN University"},{"label":"B","text":"Lovely Professional University"},{"label":"C","text":"Punjab University"},{"label":"D","text":"Shivaji University"},{"label":"E","text":"University of Calicut"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":628,"text":"The World Forestry Congress (WFC) is held every six years since 1926 under the auspices of the _______, in association with the government of the host country.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO)"},{"label":"B","text":"United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP)"},{"label":"C","text":"Conservation International"},{"label":"D","text":"Worldwide fund for Nature (WWF)"},{"label":"E","text":"Greenpeace"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":629,"text":"When was BIMSTEC formed?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1991"},{"label":"B","text":"1995"},{"label":"C","text":"1997"},{"label":"D","text":"2001"},{"label":"E","text":"2004"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":630,"text":"In India, the second largest provider of employment after agriculture is:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Textile Sector"},{"label":"B","text":"Real Estate"},{"label":"C","text":"Manufacturing"},{"label":"D","text":"Services Sector"},{"label":"E","text":"Railways"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":631,"text":"Ministry of Culture has organised PAN India Programme “Jharokha” in how many States?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10"},{"label":"B","text":"11"},{"label":"C","text":"12"},{"label":"D","text":"13"},{"label":"E","text":"15"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":632,"text":"Identify which among the following has introduced the first Exchange Traded ‘Bharat Bond’?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"ICICI Prudential"},{"label":"B","text":"Adtiya Birla Capital"},{"label":"C","text":"Edelweiss"},{"label":"D","text":"HDFC Capital"},{"label":"E","text":"National Stock Exchang e"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":633,"text":"As per Union Budget 2022 -23, how much amount of Fund has been allocated for Jal Jeevan Mission?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 40,000 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 50,000 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 35,000 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 60,000 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs. 68,000 crore"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":634,"text":"Identify which among the following is part of the Memorandum of Company Act? 1. The objective of the Company 2. State in which the company is located 3. This clause states the liability of the members of the company. The Liability can be limited or unlimited 4. The name of the company should be stated in this clause.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"1, 2 and 4"},{"label":"C","text":"2, 3 and 4"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 3 and 4"},{"label":"E","text":"1, 2, 3 and 4"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":635,"text":"Under which of the following conditions does the DICGC give money to the liquidator? 1. If a bank goes into liquidation. 2. If a bank is reconstructed or amalgamated/merged with another bank 3. If the bank wishes to withdraw from the DICGC","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1 and 2"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 2 and 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 1 and 3"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":636,"text":"An exchange rate system got implemented after World War 2. This system was accepted on the basis of which declaration?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bretton Woods"},{"label":"B","text":"Marrakesh Agreement"},{"label":"C","text":"International Finance Agreement"},{"label":"D","text":"Foreign Account Tax Compliance"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":637,"text":"Identify which among the following is not among the baseline assumptions of the monetary policy committee of April 2022? 1. Normal monsoon in 2022 2. Average crude oil price (Indian basket) of US$ 95 per barrel 3. Inflation at 5.7% in 2022 -23","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 2"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 3"},{"label":"D","text":"1 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"2 and 3"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":638,"text":"Indian peacekeepers has  been awarded UN medals for outstanding performance, for serving in which of the following country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ghana"},{"label":"B","text":"Caribbean Island"},{"label":"C","text":"South Sudan"},{"label":"D","text":"Syria"},{"label":"E","text":"Mongolia"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":639,"text":"National Centre for Financial Education (NCFE), a non profit  organization was set up under which section of the company act 2013?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Section 5"},{"label":"B","text":"Section 6"},{"label":"C","text":"Section 7"},{"label":"D","text":"Section 8"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":640,"text":"Government of India is selling 100% stake in AI, ____% stake in AI Express Limited (AIXL) and all of the government’s ____% stake in AI -SATS, which is a joint venture with Singapore -based ground handling company SATS Limited.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"75, 50"},{"label":"B","text":"75, 75"},{"label":"C","text":"100, 50"},{"label":"D","text":"100, 75"},{"label":"E","text":"100, 100"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":641,"text":"Which of these telecommunication company has joined the SEA -ME-WE- 6 undersea cable consortium to scale up its high -speed global network capacity and serve India’s fast growing digital economy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Reliance Jio"},{"label":"B","text":"Bharti Airtel"},{"label":"C","text":"Vodafone -Idea"},{"label":"D","text":"BSNL"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":642,"text":"As per State of World's Forests (SOFO) 2022, forests cover ___% of the global land area.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"29%"},{"label":"B","text":"31%"},{"label":"C","text":"33%"},{"label":"D","text":"27%"},{"label":"E","text":"26%"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":643,"text":"In recent news, a declaration has been adopted that aims to boost industry ties on defense and renewable energy, in the face of growing competition from the other emerging countries . The  above -mentioned Atlantic Declaration was  signed between which of the following two  countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United States and United Kingdom"},{"label":"B","text":"Australia & United Kingdom"},{"label":"C","text":"France and United States"},{"label":"D","text":"Australia and United Kingdom"},{"label":"E","text":"Australia and France"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":644,"text":"The United  States will rejoin an organization in July, four years after it left it in 2019, alleging that it was biased against Israel. The move to rejoin will face a vote by the organisation's  member states and is expected to pass easily. Identify which among the following organisations is the  US  about to re -join?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"UNICEF"},{"label":"B","text":"WHO"},{"label":"C","text":"UNESCO"},{"label":"D","text":"UNCTAD"},{"label":"E","text":"SCO"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":645,"text":"What is the objective of the \"Antardrishti  Dashboard\" which was introduced recently by the RBI ?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It will provide the required insight to assess and monitor the progress of grievance"},{"label":"B","text":"It will provide the required insight to assess and monitor the progress of financial"},{"label":"C","text":"It will provide the required insight to assess and monitor the progress of reducing NPAs."},{"label":"D","text":"It will provide the required insight to assess and monitor the progress of strengthening"},{"label":"E","text":"It will provide the required insight to assess and monitor the progress of digital banking."}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":646,"text":"In recent news, Indian -origin Climate Change researcher ______ has been picked for the Spinoza Prize 2023, which is the highest scientific honour in the Netherlands  and has a prize money of _______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sheo Kumar, 1.5 million euros"},{"label":"B","text":"Rajkumar Upadhyay, 2.5 million euros"},{"label":"C","text":"Joyeeta Gupta, 1.5 million euros"},{"label":"D","text":"K Rajaraman, 3.5 million euros"},{"label":"E","text":"Navtej Bal, 1.5 million euros"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":647,"text":"Which country has achieved gender  parity according to the latest Global Gender Gap Index?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Iceland"},{"label":"B","text":"Finland"},{"label":"C","text":"Denmark"},{"label":"D","text":"Sweden"},{"label":"E","text":"None"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":648,"text":"Comptroller and Auditor General of India Girish Chandra Murmu has been re -elected as the external auditor of ______ for a  four -year term from____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"WHO, 2024 to 2027"},{"label":"B","text":"UNICEF, 2023 to 2026"},{"label":"C","text":"UNESCO, 2024 to 2027"},{"label":"D","text":"WTO, 2023 to 2026"},{"label":"E","text":"UNCTAD, 2024 to 2027"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":649,"text":"The tropical cyclones forming over different ocean basins are named by the concerned regional specialised meteorological centres (RSMCs) and regional Tropical Cyclone Warning Centres (TCWCs). As per the 'List of North Indian Ocean Tropical Cyclone Names', what is the name of the next cyclone aft er cyclone 'Biparjoy' and the name has been recommended by which country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prahar, Bangladesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Akhand, India"},{"label":"C","text":"Tej, India"},{"label":"D","text":"Bhanwar, Nepal"},{"label":"E","text":"Prachand, Sri Lanka"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":650,"text":"Foreign Trade Policy (2023) is a policy document which is based on continuity of time - tested schemes facilitating exports as well as a document which is nimble and responsive to the requirements of trade. Which of these is not part of the fo ur key pillars of the Foreign Trade Policy 2023 declared recently?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Incentive to Remission"},{"label":"B","text":"Export promotion through collaboration - Exporters, States, Districts, Indian Missions"},{"label":"C","text":"Ease of doing business, reduction in transaction cost and e -initiatives"},{"label":"D","text":"Emerging Areas – E-Commerce Developing Districts as Export Hubs and streamlining"},{"label":"E","text":"E-Governance"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":651,"text":"The Union government, in consultation with the RBI, fixes the inflation target for the central bank every five years. The Upper Tolerance level of Inflation is ____________ and in case of breach of the upper tolerance for ___________ quarters the repor t has to be submitted by RBI.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"4.0%, three consecutive quarters"},{"label":"B","text":"5.0%, two consecutive quarters"},{"label":"C","text":"6.0%, two consecutive quarters"},{"label":"D","text":"6.0%, three consecutive quarters"},{"label":"E","text":"5.0%, three consecutive quarters"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":652,"text":"As per the survey of professional forecasters (SPF) by RBI, the real gross domestic product (GDP) growth forecast for 2023 -24 has been retained at _____ , while it is expected to grow by ____ in 2024 -25.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5.7 per cent, 6.1 per cent"},{"label":"B","text":"5.9 per cent, 6.3 per cent"},{"label":"C","text":"6.0 per cent, 6.4 per cent"},{"label":"D","text":"6.1 per cent, 6.4 per cent"},{"label":"E","text":"6.2 per cent, 6.3 per cent"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":653,"text":"As per Annual Report of RBI, Commercial banks remained the largest holders of government securities  [including T -Bills and state government securities (SGSs)] accounting for __________ at end -March 2023.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"27.5%"},{"label":"B","text":"37.5%"},{"label":"C","text":"25.5%"},{"label":"D","text":"31.5%"},{"label":"E","text":"28.5%"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":654,"text":"Identify which among the following States are among the top 3 States with highest mangrove cover in India? 1. West Bengal 2. Gujarat 3. Andaman Nicobar 4. Tamil Nadu","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1, 2 & 3"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 2 & 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 1 & 4"},{"label":"D","text":"Only 3 & 4"},{"label":"E","text":"2, 3 & 4"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":655,"text":"Group of Twenty (G20) is an intergovernmental forum comprising 19 countries and the European Union. India holds the Presidency of the G20 from December 1, 2022 to November 30, 2023. Which  of the following is not one of the guest countries invited to the G20 summit under India’s presidency?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bangladesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Philippines"},{"label":"C","text":"Mauritius"},{"label":"D","text":"Netherlands"},{"label":"E","text":"Nigeria"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":656,"text":"India  is NOT a member of which of the following organizations?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"SCO"},{"label":"B","text":"ADB"},{"label":"C","text":"World Trade Organisation"},{"label":"D","text":"OECD"},{"label":"E","text":"World Bank"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":657,"text":"As per RBI Annual Report 2022 -23, India has remained among the fastest growing major economies of the world, contributing more than ___________ to global growth on average during the last five years.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5.5%"},{"label":"B","text":"7.5%"},{"label":"C","text":"12%"},{"label":"D","text":"6.8%"},{"label":"E","text":"10.5%"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":658,"text":"As per the Financial Stability Report, SCBs’ gross non -performing assets (GNPA) ratio continued  its downtrend and fell to a __________ year low to 3.9% in March 2023 and the net non -performing assets (NNPA) ratio declined to __________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"8, 0.5%"},{"label":"B","text":"10, 1%"},{"label":"C","text":"13, 1.5%"},{"label":"D","text":"10, 1.5%"},{"label":"E","text":"8, 1%"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":659,"text":"Despite prolonged geopolitical tensions and slowing global trade, India’s merchandise exports touched US$ 450.4 billion during 2022 - 23, which is 6.7 percent above the previous year’s record level. Which  of the following sectors contributed the largest share in the merchandise exports from India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Electronic Goods"},{"label":"B","text":"Petroleum Products"},{"label":"C","text":"Rice"},{"label":"D","text":"Organic and Inorganic Chemicals"},{"label":"E","text":"Iron Ore"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":660,"text":"The core theme of the 2025 Payments Vision document is E -Payments for Everyone ______________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"E-Payments for Elder"},{"label":"B","text":"Everywhere, Everytime"},{"label":"C","text":"Everywhere, Everything"},{"label":"D","text":"Everything, Everytime"},{"label":"E","text":"Everyone, Everything"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":661,"text":"Which of these ASEAN countries are also the members of BIMSTEC? 1.Thailand 2. Singapore 3. Myanmar 4. Indonesia 5. Vietnam","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1, 2 and 3 only"},{"label":"B","text":"3 and 4 only"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 4 and 5"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":662,"text":"There has been great excitement and a rush of positive sentiment among members of the fintech community (digital lenders), regulated lenders, and investors about the recently (June 2023) published Guidelines on Default Loss Guarantee (DLG) in Digital L ending  which were issued by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI). The Guidelines on Default Loss Guarantee (DLG) in Digital Lending is not applicable on which of the following  entities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Payment Banks"},{"label":"B","text":"Small Finance Banks"},{"label":"C","text":"State Co -operative Banks"},{"label":"D","text":"NBFC"},{"label":"E","text":"Commercial Banks"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":663,"text":"The term of State Legislative Assemblies of which of the following states will not end till Jan 2024?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"C","text":"Haryana"},{"label":"D","text":"Chhattisgarh"},{"label":"E","text":"Telangana"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":664,"text":"Which of these small saving schemes will provide highest return in July - September  2023?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Kisan Vikas Patra"},{"label":"B","text":"National Savings Certificate (NSC)"},{"label":"C","text":"Senior citizen savings Scheme"},{"label":"D","text":"Sukanya Samriddhi"},{"label":"E","text":"Monthly Income Scheme"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":665,"text":"HS Prannoy  ended a six -year long title drought with a three -game win over China's Weng Hong Yang in a pulsating men's singles finals at the Malaysia Masters. This title is known as _________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Super 1000 title"},{"label":"B","text":"Super 500 title"},{"label":"C","text":"Super 300 title"},{"label":"D","text":"Super 200 title"},{"label":"E","text":"Super 100 title"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":666,"text":"For the first time in India, the share price of a company crossed the Rs 1 lakh mark. With this, __________ became the first stock in India to cross the Rs 1 lakh mark per share in intra -day trade after its share jumped  1.07 per cent in early trade recently in June 2023.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Honeywell"},{"label":"B","text":"MRF Ltd."},{"label":"C","text":"Page Industries"},{"label":"D","text":"3M India"},{"label":"E","text":"Shree Cement"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":667,"text":"With  classification of UCBs into four tiers, the prudential exposure limits for UCBs to a group of connected borrowers/parties will be how much of their tier -I capital?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹150 lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"₹120 lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"₹60 lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"₹50 lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"₹70 lakh"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":668,"text":"As per the recent (June 2023) data of Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT), United Arab Emirates (UAE), with which India implemented a comprehensive free trade agreement in May last year, has emerged as the fourth largest investor in India during 2022 -23. Which  among the following countries are among the top 3 sources of FDI into India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"UAE, Mauritius, US"},{"label":"B","text":"Netherlands, Mauritius, US"},{"label":"C","text":"Singapore, Mauritius, US"},{"label":"D","text":"Singapore, Netherlands, US"},{"label":"E","text":"Singapore, Mauritius, Australia"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":669,"text":"India’s overall exports (Merchandise and Services combined) in April 2023 is estimated to be USD 65.02 Billion, exhibiting a positive growth of 2 percent over April 2022.  Which one of the following  key sectors under merchandise exports exhibited the highest positive growth in April 2023 as compared to the same period last year (April 2022)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Oil Meals"},{"label":"B","text":"Electronic Goods"},{"label":"C","text":"Ceramic Products & Glassware"},{"label":"D","text":"Drugs & Pharmaceuticals"},{"label":"E","text":"Cereal Preparations & Miscellaneous Processed Items"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":670,"text":"Which  of the following States are among the top 3 destination states for FDI in India? 1. Maharashtra 2. Karnataka 3. Gujarat 4. Delhi 5. Tamil Nadu","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Both 2 & 3"},{"label":"C","text":"1, 3 and 5"},{"label":"D","text":"2, 4 and 5"},{"label":"E","text":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":671,"text":"Dr. Mansukh Mandaviya  unveiled the 5th State Food Safety Index (SFSI), which evaluates the performance of states and union territories across six different aspects of food safety. Which one of the following are the top -3 states in the large state category of the State Food Saf ety Index ?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Kerala, Punjab and Uttar Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Andhra Pradesh, Kerala and Punjab"},{"label":"C","text":"Kerala, Punjab and Tamil Nadu"},{"label":"D","text":"Haryana, Kerala and Telangana"},{"label":"E","text":"Haryana, Punjab and Tamil Nadu"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":672,"text":"Who has been recently appointed as the chair of B20 India which represents the entire G20 business  community?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ajay Bhalla"},{"label":"B","text":"Gautam Adani"},{"label":"C","text":"N. Chandrasekaran"},{"label":"D","text":"Ratan Tata"},{"label":"E","text":"Ravneet Kaur"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":673,"text":"The headquarters of the European Central Bank is located in ____and was established in ______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"London, 1998"},{"label":"B","text":"Brussels , 2002"},{"label":"C","text":"Paris, 2000"},{"label":"D","text":"Rome, 1998"},{"label":"E","text":"Frankfurt, 1998"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":674,"text":"Identify which among the following statements is true regarding Call Money, Notice Money and Term Money?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Scheduled commercial banks (including Small Finance Banks) cannot set their own limits"},{"label":"B","text":"Scheduled commercial banks (excluding Small Finance Banks) can set their own limits for"},{"label":"C","text":"Scheduled commercial banks (excluding Small Finance Banks) can set their own limits for"},{"label":"D","text":"Scheduled commercial banks (including Small Finance Banks) can set their own limits for"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":675,"text":"50 years after the launch of Project Tiger on April 1, 1973, India's tiger population today ranges from 2,500 to 3,000. When Project Tiger started, we had ___ tiger reserves. In 2023, we have ___.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"9, 47"},{"label":"B","text":"9, 53"},{"label":"C","text":"9, 48"},{"label":"D","text":"9, 55"},{"label":"E","text":"9, 67"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":676,"text":"Identify which among the following statements is incorrect regarding Sovereign Gold Bonds?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Investment limit per fiscal year is 4 kg for individuals and Hindu Undivided Family (HUF)"},{"label":"B","text":"Investment limit per fiscal year is 20 Kg for Trusts and similar entities notified by the"},{"label":"C","text":"Bond is available both in demat and paper form"},{"label":"D","text":"Total limit is excluding purchase from secondary market"},{"label":"E","text":"Bond can be used as collateral for loans"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":677,"text":"Which of these banks has introduced corporate customer  platform  \"fyn\"?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Kotak Mahindra Bank"},{"label":"B","text":"IndusInd Bank"},{"label":"C","text":"HDFC Bank"},{"label":"D","text":"RBL Bank"},{"label":"E","text":"Federal Bank"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":678,"text":"Identify which among the following is one of the Payment System Operators in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Clearing Corporation of India"},{"label":"B","text":"National Payments Corporation of India"},{"label":"C","text":"Scheduled Commercial Banks"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":679,"text":"In recent news, 40 years have been completed for the historic win of India in the 1983 Cricket World Cup final. India scored 183 runs batting first, what was the score of West Indies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"128"},{"label":"B","text":"133"},{"label":"C","text":"110"},{"label":"D","text":"125"},{"label":"E","text":"140"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":680,"text":"The Union Minister of Ports, Shipping & Waterways and Ayush, Shri Sarbananda Sonowal flagged off the maiden International Cruise Vessel \"_______\", India’s first international cruise vessel, from Chennai to _______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"MV Empress, Bangladesh"},{"label":"B","text":"MV Ganga Vilas, Bhutan"},{"label":"C","text":"MV Empress, Sri Lanka"},{"label":"D","text":"MV Ganga Vilas, Sri Lanka"},{"label":"E","text":"MV Emperor, Sri Lanka"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":681,"text":"Identify which among the following institutes celebrates their foundation day on 1st July?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Indian Space Research Organisation"},{"label":"B","text":"Institute of Chartered Accountants of India"},{"label":"C","text":"Defence Research and Development Organisation"},{"label":"D","text":"Border Roads Organisation"},{"label":"E","text":"NITI Aayog"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":682,"text":"Brand Finance evaluates and values over 5,000 brands every year, across all sectors and geographies to get instant access to the world's largest brand database, including brand value, brand strength, research and competitive ranking data. As per  brand finance India, which among the following is not among the top 5 Indian brands?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Tata"},{"label":"B","text":"Infosys"},{"label":"C","text":"HDFC Bank"},{"label":"D","text":"LIC"},{"label":"E","text":"Reliance"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":683,"text":"The National Institutional Ranking Framework (NIRF) was approved by the MHRD and introduced by the Honourable Minister of Human Resource Development on 29th September 2015. As per the NIRF's \"India Rankings 2023\", which one of the following has been mat ched incorrectly: 1. Top performing University: IISc Bengaluru 2. Top performing College: St. Stephens 3. Top performing institute in Overall Category: IIT Madras","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2 only"},{"label":"B","text":"1 and 2 only"},{"label":"C","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":684,"text":"El Nino is a cyclical environmental condition that occurs across the Equatorial Pacific Ocean and is triggered by natural interactions between the ocean and atmosphere with the driving factors being the sea surface temperature, rainfall, air pressure,  and atmospheric and ocean circulations. It occurs when the surface water in the equatorial Pacific becomes warmer than average and east winds blow weaker than normal. The phenomenon is similar to which of the following climatic anomalies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Indian Ocean Dipole"},{"label":"B","text":"Maven  Oscillation"},{"label":"C","text":"Madden Jullian Oscillation"},{"label":"D","text":"Western Disturbances"},{"label":"E","text":"Monsoon"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":685,"text":"Identify which among the following is the mascot introduced by RBI as a part of its financial Awareness  campaign?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ms Money"},{"label":"B","text":"Mr Money"},{"label":"C","text":"Money Kumar"},{"label":"D","text":"Mr Kumar"},{"label":"E","text":"Money Raja"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":686,"text":"Identify which among the following is the initiative supported by NITI Aayog, aimed to finance 50,000 electric vehicles for MSMEs?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"ELECTRO"},{"label":"B","text":"EVOLVE"},{"label":"C","text":"EVPURE"},{"label":"D","text":"EVWORLD"},{"label":"E","text":"EVNITI"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":687,"text":"The World Bank has scrapped Ease of Doing Business and declared a new replacement annual series which will reflect a more balanced and transparent approach toward evaluating a country's business and investment climate. What is the name of the new rep lacement annual series?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ease Business"},{"label":"B","text":"Business PRO"},{"label":"C","text":"Easy Business"},{"label":"D","text":"Business Ready"},{"label":"E","text":"Business PORT"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":688,"text":"Food and Consumer Affairs Minister Piyush Goyal has declared that India will achieve its target of ____ ethanol blending with petrol by ______ instead of 2030. He also maintained that the maize crop will play an important role in implementation of th e programme.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"20%, 2024"},{"label":"B","text":"25%, 2025"},{"label":"C","text":"20%, 2025"},{"label":"D","text":"30%, 2030"},{"label":"E","text":"25%, 2023"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":689,"text":"In recent news, the Union Minister of Road Transport and Highway has informed about the ambitious India -Myanmar -Thailand Trilateral Highway which connects Kolkata to Bangkok. It belongs to which of which of the following  organization?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"BIMSTEC"},{"label":"B","text":"ASEAN"},{"label":"C","text":"SCO"},{"label":"D","text":"G-7"},{"label":"E","text":"G20"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":690,"text":"Prime Minister Narendra Modi introduced three flagship schemes for urban revamp, including smart cities and housing for all on 25th June 2015, ensuring better quality of life for 40% of the country’s population that either live in urban areas or depend  on them for livelihood. Which one of the following are the 3 -schemes introduced? 1. Smart Cities Mission 2. Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation (AMRUT) 3. Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana - Urban (PMAY -U)","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Both 2 & 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 3"},{"label":"D","text":"Both 1 & 2"},{"label":"E","text":"All 1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":691,"text":"As per the Union Budget 2023, Government has decided to continue the 50 -year interest free loan to state governments for one more year to spur capital investment and, with a significantly enhanced outlay of Rs 1.3 lakh crore, from ___________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2021 -22"},{"label":"B","text":"2025 -26"},{"label":"C","text":"2024 -25"},{"label":"D","text":"2022 -23"},{"label":"E","text":"2023 -24"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":692,"text":"Which one of the following statements are correct with respect to the Mission for Integrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH) scheme? 1. It is a Central  Sector Scheme introduced in 2015. 2. It provides financial assistance @35% of the project cost in general areas for setting up post harvest management infrastructure. 3. It provides technical advice and administrative support to state governments/state horticulture missions for the saffron mission.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Both 2 & 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 2"},{"label":"D","text":"Both 1 & 3"},{"label":"E","text":"All 1, 2 & 3"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":693,"text":"Progress has been sluggish in six sectors under Production -Linked Incentive (PLI) schemes. A detailed analysis is being conducted by relevant ministries. Which of these is not under the non -performing sectors of the scheme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Information technology (IT) hardware"},{"label":"B","text":"White Goods"},{"label":"C","text":"ACC Battery"},{"label":"D","text":"Textile"},{"label":"E","text":"Speciality Steel"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":694,"text":"Which one of the following states was among the top -3 states in terms of highest GST revenues in June 2023? 1. Haryana 2. Karnataka 3. Gujarat 4. Uttar Pradesh 5. Maharashtra","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 2, 3 and 5"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 1, 3 & 4"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 1, 2 & 5"},{"label":"D","text":"Only 3, 4 & 5"},{"label":"E","text":"Only 2, 3 & 4"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":695,"text":"E -way bill is a document required to be carried by a person in charge of the conveyance carrying any consignment of goods of value exceeding ______ as mandated by the Government in terms of section 68 of the Goods and Services Tax Act read with rule 1 38 of the rules framed thereunder.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 50,000"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 40,000"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 65,000"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 1,00,000"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 75,000"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":696,"text":"Name the country that conferred its highest civilian honour to President Droupadi Murmu - The Grand Order of the Chain of Yellow Star?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sudan"},{"label":"B","text":"South Africa"},{"label":"C","text":"Uganda"},{"label":"D","text":"Suriname"},{"label":"E","text":"Serbia"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":697,"text":"The Union Cabinet chaired by the Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi, approved the constitution and empowerment of an Inter Ministerial Committee (IMC) for facilitation of the “World’s Largest Grain Storage Plan in Cooperative Sector” by convergence of various schemes of ministries. Which ministry does not belong to that group?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare"},{"label":"B","text":"Ministry of Cooperation"},{"label":"C","text":"Ministry of Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution"},{"label":"D","text":"Ministry of Food Processing Industries"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":698,"text":"The Reserve Bank releases a quarterly house price index (HPI) based on transaction - level data received from housing registration authorities in ten major cities. The cities are: 1. Bengaluru 2. Delhi 3. Jaipur 4. Kanpur 5. Kolkata 6. Mumbai Remaining cities are :","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Chandigarh, Kochi, Lucknow, Ahmedabad"},{"label":"B","text":"Chennai, Shimla, Lucknow, Ahmedabad"},{"label":"C","text":"Chennai, Kochi, Lucknow, Agra"},{"label":"D","text":"Chennai, Surat, Lucknow, Ahmedabad"},{"label":"E","text":"Chennai, Kochi, Lucknow, Ahmedabad"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":699,"text":"Which of these is/are the dimensions across which the states and districts have been assessed under the Social Progress Index (SPI) for States and Districts made by the Institute for Competitiveness and Social Progress Imperative? 1. Basic Human Needs 2. Innovation 3. Foundations of Wellbeing 4. Opportunity 5. Foundations of Healthy life","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1, 3 and 4"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 2, 3 and 4"},{"label":"D","text":"Only 1 and 2"},{"label":"E","text":"Only 2 and 3"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":700,"text":"NASA's MAVEN mission has published some new, mind -blowing images captivating an array of ultraviolet views of the red planet. What does \"V\" stand for in MAVEN Mission?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Velocity"},{"label":"B","text":"Vacuum"},{"label":"C","text":"Volatile"},{"label":"D","text":"Valence"},{"label":"E","text":"Vector"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":701,"text":"The Basic Statistical Returns (BSR) Code is a seven -digit code that is provided to the registered banks by the RBI. The first three digits in the code identify the bank, while the following four digits identify the bank branch. India’s Basic Statistic al Returns (BSR) system recently completed _________ since its inception.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10 years"},{"label":"B","text":"20 years"},{"label":"C","text":"50 years"},{"label":"D","text":"25 years"},{"label":"E","text":"75 years"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":702,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) has fixed the minimum Net Owned Fund (NOF) size for housing finance companies at _________. The housing finance companies (HFCs) holding a Certificate of Registration (CoR) and having an NOF of less than ______  will be  required to achieve NOF of Rs 15 crore by March 31, 2022 and ________ by March 31, 2023.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 5 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 15 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 25 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 20 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 35 crore"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":703,"text":"As per Foreign Trade Policy 2023, towns that produce goods worth at least ______ can be recognized as towns of export excellence, based on their growth potential for exports.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 850 Crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 750 Crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 650 Crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 550 Crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 450 Crore"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":704,"text":"NTPC Limited, India's largest power generation company, has climbed 52 positions to secure the 433rd rank in Forbes' “The Global 2000” List for 2023. Which of these is/are not the parameters taken into account for determining Forbes 2000 ranking of the top public companies in the world?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Goodwill"},{"label":"B","text":"Sales"},{"label":"C","text":"Profits"},{"label":"D","text":"Assets"},{"label":"E","text":"Market value"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":705,"text":"In recent news, (June 2023), Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR), New Delhi has signed a MoU with _______ Kisan to combine strengths and create synergy between the two organizations for guiding the farmers on scientific cultivation of different cr ops for optimum yield and income.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Snapdeal"},{"label":"B","text":"Meesho"},{"label":"C","text":"Amazon"},{"label":"D","text":"Flipkart"},{"label":"E","text":"CRED"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":706,"text":"In recent news, SEBI has proposed to tweak the definition of unpublished price sensitive information (UPSI). It proposed changing the definition of UPSI as it currently stands and bringing Regulation 30 of LODR, according to which the listed firms must noti fy stock exchanges after the occurrence of any events or facts that are material. Identify which among the following occurrences are included? 1. Any modification to securities 2. Revision to ratings 3. Initiation of CSR activities 4. Change in director 5. Fraud or default by promoters or key managerial people","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both 2 & 3"},{"label":"B","text":"1, 3, 4 and 5"},{"label":"C","text":"Both 1 & 5"},{"label":"D","text":"3, 4 and 5"},{"label":"E","text":"1,2,4 and 5"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":707,"text":"As per data from the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation published under “Twenty Point Programme”, of the 14 parameters tracked quarterly, the Indian Government achieved a more than ____ target completion (\"very good\") in six parameters .","options":[{"label":"A","text":"80%"},{"label":"B","text":"90%"},{"label":"C","text":"75%"},{"label":"D","text":"60%"},{"label":"E","text":"40%"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":708,"text":"Household financial savings refer to currency, bank deposits, debt securities, mutual funds, pension funds, insurance, and investments in small savings schemes. The total of these savings is referred to as gross household financial savings. Once finan cial liabilities, including loans from banks, non -banking financial companies (NBFCs), and housing finance companies, are subtracted from gross savings, what remains is referred to as net household financial savings. As per the RBI Annual Report 2022 -23, w hich one of the following Financial Saving of the Household Sector has the highest share in 2021 -22?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Deposits"},{"label":"B","text":"Currency"},{"label":"C","text":"Shares and Debentures"},{"label":"D","text":"Insurance Funds"},{"label":"E","text":"Provident and Pension Funds"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":709,"text":"TRAI in its endeavor to curb menace of spams through Unsolicited Commercial Communication (UCC) has taken various measures in the recent past. In recent news, (June 2023), TRAI has now issued a Direction to all the Access Providers to develop and deploy the DCA facility for creating a unified platform and process to register customers consent digitally across all service providers and Principal Entities. What does “DCA” stand for?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Digital Consent Acquisition"},{"label":"B","text":"Data Consent Acquisition"},{"label":"C","text":"Digital Content Acquisition"},{"label":"D","text":"Data Content Acquisition"},{"label":"E","text":"Digital Communication Acquisition"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":710,"text":"Taking forward digitization efforts declared in the Union Budget 2022 -23, the Reserve Bank introduced its Central Bank Digital Currency (CBDC) in phases during the year, with the launch of pilots for Digital Rupee (e`) in ____________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Wholesale segments only on December 1, 2022"},{"label":"B","text":"Retail segments only November 1, 2022."},{"label":"C","text":"Wholesale and retail segments on December 1, 2022, and November 1, 2022 respectively."},{"label":"D","text":"Wholesale and retail segments on January 1, 2022, and December 1, 2022 respectively."},{"label":"E","text":"Wholesale and retail segments on November 1, 2022, and December 1, 2022 respectively."}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":711,"text":"As per the recent advance estimates of production of major crops for agricultural year 2022 -23 published by the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, the production of which one of the following crops did not increase from the previous year?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Jawar"},{"label":"B","text":"Rice"},{"label":"C","text":"Wheat"},{"label":"D","text":"Bajra"},{"label":"E","text":"Maize"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":712,"text":"Identify which among the following Scheduled Commercial Banks have recorded the highest number of new branch additions  in the financial year ended on 31st March 2023?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Yes Bank"},{"label":"B","text":"Axis Bank"},{"label":"C","text":"Bank of Baroda"},{"label":"D","text":"HDFC Bank"},{"label":"E","text":"ICICI Bank"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":713,"text":"Under SEBI (Mutual Funds) Regulations, 1996, Mutual Funds are permitted to charge certain operating expenses for managing a mutual fund scheme. All such costs for running and managing a mutual fund scheme are collectively referred to as ‘Total Expense  Ratio’ (TER).  TER is calculated as a percentage of the Scheme’s average _________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Net Asset Value (NAV)"},{"label":"B","text":"Absolute Returns"},{"label":"C","text":"Simple Annualised Return"},{"label":"D","text":"Total Investments"},{"label":"E","text":"Redemption Amount"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":714,"text":"Which of these metals was not used to make the commemorative '75 Rupee Coin' which was introduced during the inauguration of the new Parliament?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Silver"},{"label":"B","text":"Copper"},{"label":"C","text":"Nickel"},{"label":"D","text":"Gold"},{"label":"E","text":"Zinc"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":715,"text":"As per IRDAI, which among the following is a criteria  used to identify the Domestic - Systemically Important Insurers?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Number of Branches"},{"label":"B","text":"Market Share"},{"label":"C","text":"Domestic and global interconnectedness"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":716,"text":"In recent news, the Prime Minister of India attended the 3rd Summit of the Forum for India - Pacific Islands Cooperation (FIPIC) held at which of the following locations?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fiji"},{"label":"B","text":"Papua New Guinea"},{"label":"C","text":"Samoa"},{"label":"D","text":"Solomon Islands"},{"label":"E","text":"Niue"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":717,"text":"In recent news, Indian security forces have been trained in _________ “Krav Maga” to counter China's People Liberation Army (PLA) during patrolling along the Line of Actual Control (LAC).","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Russia"},{"label":"B","text":"Caribbean Island"},{"label":"C","text":"Israel"},{"label":"D","text":"France"},{"label":"E","text":"USA"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":718,"text":"The Centre has revised the threshold for GST e -invoicing, and has declared that it will be mandatory for all businesses with annual turnover of over _____to move to e - invoicing for business to business transactions under goods and services tax (GST) from _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 2 crore, Rs 10 Crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 3.5 crore, Rs 10 Crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 5 crore, Rs 10 Crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 10 crore, Rs 20 Crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 15 crore, Rs 20 Crore"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":719,"text":"As per the Union Budget 2023 -24, the highest surcharge rate in personal income tax has been reduced from 37% to _____ in the new tax regime for income above ₹2 crore.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"15%"},{"label":"B","text":"36%"},{"label":"C","text":"17%"},{"label":"D","text":"25%"},{"label":"E","text":"30%"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":720,"text":"Which of these players has courted controversy when he wrote “Kosovo is the heart of Serbia”, depicting the ethnic tensions flared in the  Balkan  nation?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Casper Ruud"},{"label":"B","text":"Carlos Alcaraz"},{"label":"C","text":"Novak Djokovic"},{"label":"D","text":"Rafael Nadal"},{"label":"E","text":"Andrey Rublev"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":721,"text":"The Government of India through Indian Strategic Petroleum Reserve Ltd. (ISPRL) under Phase –1 has set up Strategic Petroleum Reserves (SPR) at three locations namely Visakhapatnam, Mangalore and ________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Varanasi"},{"label":"B","text":"Padur"},{"label":"C","text":"Raipur"},{"label":"D","text":"Kolkata"},{"label":"E","text":"Ranchi"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":722,"text":"Which one of the following statements is/are correct regarding the PM KUSUM Scheme? 1. It seeks to increase the farmers’ income 2. The scheme comprises 3 - components. 3. It works towards decreasing environmental pollution.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Both 2 & 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 3"},{"label":"D","text":"Both 1 & 2"},{"label":"E","text":"All 1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":723,"text":"Spanish tennis sensation Carlos Alcaraz has not won which of the following grand slams?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"US Open"},{"label":"B","text":"Wimbledon"},{"label":"C","text":"French Open"},{"label":"D","text":"Australian Open"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":724,"text":"To boost participation of small investors in the securities market, Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) has increased the threshold for the basic service demat account to __________ from the current Rs 2 lakh.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 25 lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 20 lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 15 lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 10 lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 5 lakh"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":725,"text":"Identify which among the following parameters has the highest weightage in the ‘Digital Payments Index (DPI)’ published biannually by Reserve Bank of India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Demand -side factors"},{"label":"B","text":"Payment Infrastructure"},{"label":"C","text":"Supply -side factors"},{"label":"D","text":"Payment Performance"},{"label":"E","text":"Consumer Centricity"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":726,"text":"India has not signed the Free Trade Agreement (FTA) with which of the following countries in recent  times?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mauritius"},{"label":"B","text":"Brazil"},{"label":"C","text":"South Korea"},{"label":"D","text":"UAE"},{"label":"E","text":"Australia"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":727,"text":"RBI has published a bulk  deposit limit for scheduled commercial banks, regional rural banks, small finance banks and local area banks. What is the minimum limit of the bulk deposit for the local area banks?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 5 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 4 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 3 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 2 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 1 crore"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":728,"text":"In recent news, Indian shooting icon Abhinav Bindra has been awarded the prestigious Olympic Order in recognition of his \"distinguished contribution\" to the Olympic movement. Bindra, became India's first -ever Olympic individual gold medallist in the ________  with his top finish in 10m air rifle event.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2008 Beijing Olympics"},{"label":"B","text":"2012 London Olympics"},{"label":"C","text":"2014 Sochi Olympics"},{"label":"D","text":"2016 Rio Olympics"},{"label":"E","text":"2010 Vancouver Olympics"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":729,"text":"In recent news, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) has tightened norms related to public deposit acceptance by housing finance companies (HFCs). What is the maximum deposit duration for the housing finance companies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"60 months"},{"label":"B","text":"50 months"},{"label":"C","text":"40 months"},{"label":"D","text":"30 months"},{"label":"E","text":"20 months"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":730,"text":"Mark Rutte has recently been appointed the NATO Chief amid concerns over Russia - Ukraine conflict. He has served as the Prime Minister of which country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Denmark"},{"label":"B","text":"Ireland"},{"label":"C","text":"Netherlands"},{"label":"D","text":"Scotland"},{"label":"E","text":"France"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":731,"text":"Identify which among the following insurers has introduced the AI -powered health insurance plan ‘Elevate’?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Aditya Birla Health Insurance Co. Ltd."},{"label":"B","text":"ICICI Lombard"},{"label":"C","text":"V Care Health Insurance Ltd."},{"label":"D","text":"Galaxy Health and Allied Insurance Co."},{"label":"E","text":"Manipal Cigna Health Insurance Company Limited"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":732,"text":"The Union Cabinet, chaired by Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi, has approved the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana -Urban (PMAY -U) 2.0. This ambitious scheme aims to construct 1 crore houses for urban poor and middle -class families over the next five years, with an investment of ₹10 lakh crore and a government subsidy of __________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹ 2.30 lakh crore"},{"label":"B","text":"₹ 2.50 lakh crore"},{"label":"C","text":"₹ 2.70 lakh crore"},{"label":"D","text":"₹ 2.90 lakh crore"},{"label":"E","text":"₹ 3.10 lakh crore"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":733,"text":"Identify which among the following countries is not a member of the Columbo Security Conclave?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"India"},{"label":"B","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"label":"C","text":"Maldives"},{"label":"D","text":"Thailand"},{"label":"E","text":"Mauritius"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":734,"text":"Identify which among the following companies have emerged as India’s top 3 'attractive employer brands’ according to the Randstad Employer Brand Research (REBR) 2024? 1. Microsoft 2. TCS 3. Amazon 4. Google India 5. Reliance","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1, 2 & 3"},{"label":"B","text":"1, 3 & 4"},{"label":"C","text":"2, 4 & 5"},{"label":"D","text":"3, 4 & 5"},{"label":"E","text":"1, 4 & 5"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":735,"text":"What is the asset size for the NBFC -NDs to appoint an internal  ombudsman as per the RBI Internal Ombudsman Scheme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 5,000 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 4,000 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 3,000 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 2,000 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 1,000 crore"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":736,"text":"Identify which among the following government initiatives has been introduced for reducing NPAs in India? Identify the incorrect statement mentioned below along with their launch years?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Debt Recovery Tribunal - 1993"},{"label":"B","text":"National Asset Reconstruction Company Ltd - 2021"},{"label":"C","text":"SARFAESI Act - 2005"},{"label":"D","text":"Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code - 2016"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":737,"text":"In recent news, (July 2024), two MLAs from Jharkhand State Assembly have been disqualified under the anti -defection law under the ____ schedule of the Indian Constitution.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10th"},{"label":"B","text":"9th"},{"label":"C","text":"8th"},{"label":"D","text":"7th"},{"label":"E","text":"6th"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":738,"text":"Indian government bonds have been included in JP Morgan's emerging markets index. Foreign Portfolio Investor (FPI) holdings of outstanding FAR bonds could rise to ____ by 2025.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2.4%"},{"label":"B","text":"3.4%"},{"label":"C","text":"2.9%"},{"label":"D","text":"3.9%"},{"label":"E","text":"5.0%"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":739,"text":"Under the Sovereign Gold Bond scheme, premature redemption can be done after how many years from issuance?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5 years"},{"label":"B","text":"7 years"},{"label":"C","text":"2 years"},{"label":"D","text":"3 years"},{"label":"E","text":"9 years"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":740,"text":"As per the RBI’s report on Currency and Finance, which one of the following is/are the outcomes of increase in digital payments?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Better targeting of government schemes"},{"label":"B","text":"Higher financial inclusion and inclusive growth"},{"label":"C","text":"Better credit assessment and credit availability"},{"label":"D","text":"Higher demand for money"},{"label":"E","text":"All the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":741,"text":"As per Union Budget 2024, it has been decided to remove the penalty of Rs 10 lakh under Sections 42 and 43 of the Black Money Act (applicable till now) if you fail to report any foreign assets (other than immovable property) where the aggregate value does not exceed ____________. This amendment will take effect from October 1, 2024.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹35 lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"₹30 lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"₹25 lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"₹20 lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"₹15 lakh"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":742,"text":"As per the National Pension System (NPS) scheme, partial withdrawal can happen maximum of 3 times during entire tenure of subscription if the subscriber has completed at least 3 years from the date of joining where a beneficiary can withdraw up to ___ % of contribution at any time.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"25%"},{"label":"B","text":"20%"},{"label":"C","text":"15%"},{"label":"D","text":"10%"},{"label":"E","text":"12.5%"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":743,"text":"The Financial Inclusion Index captures information on various aspects of financial inclusion in a single value ranging between 0 and 100, where 0 represents complete financial exclusion and 100 indicates full financial inclusion. Which parameter broug ht maximum increase in the FI Index March 2024?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Quality"},{"label":"B","text":"Access"},{"label":"C","text":"Usage"},{"label":"D","text":"All the above"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":744,"text":"In recent news, the Parliament of India has passed the ‘Public Examinations (Prevention of Unfair Means) Act, 2024’. As per this Act, the service provider shall be liable to be punished with imposition of a fine up to ____ rupees.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"One crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Two crores"},{"label":"C","text":"Three crores"},{"label":"D","text":"Four crores"},{"label":"E","text":"Five crores"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":745,"text":"__________ Trade Receivables Discounting System (TReDS) platform has achieved a significant milestone, facilitating financing of over 50 lac invoices worth ₹1,00,000 crore since its inception providing accessible working capital financing solutions to  Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) in India.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Receivables Employment Exchange of India Limited"},{"label":"B","text":"Remittance Exchange of India Limited"},{"label":"C","text":"Exchange Rate of India Limited"},{"label":"D","text":"Receivables Exchange of India Limited"},{"label":"E","text":"Revenue Exchange of India Limited"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":746,"text":"Identify which among the following was/were the top three count ry/countries in the 2024 International Mathematical Olympiad (IMO)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United States"},{"label":"B","text":"China"},{"label":"C","text":"South Korea"},{"label":"D","text":"All the above"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":747,"text":"In the Union Budget 2024 -25, the TReDS onboarding turnover threshold has been reduced from Rs 500 Crore to ____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 450 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 400 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 350 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 300 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 250 crore"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":748,"text":"As per the Global Peace Index 2024, which region remains the least peaceful region?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Middle East and North Africa (MENA) region"},{"label":"B","text":"South Asia"},{"label":"C","text":"South America"},{"label":"D","text":"North America"},{"label":"E","text":"Europe"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":749,"text":"As per a recent RBI report, India's foreign exchange reserves are now sufficient to cover over ____ of projected imports.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"11 months"},{"label":"B","text":"10 months"},{"label":"C","text":"9 months"},{"label":"D","text":"8 months"},{"label":"E","text":"7 months"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":750,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India published the final guidelines for setting up a self -regulatory organisation (SRO) for the fintech sector. To be eligible, the applicant should have a minimum net worth of _________ within a period of one year after recognitio n as an SRO - FT by RBI, or before commencement of operations as an SRO -FT, whichever is earlier.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rupees one crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rupees two crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rupees three crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rupees four crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rupees five crore"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":751,"text":"As per the recent Monetary Policy Committee meeting of August 2024, the limit for the UPI for the tax payments has been increased from Rs 1 lakh to ____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 10 lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 5 lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 15 lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 3 lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 2 lakh"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":752,"text":"Identify which among the following statements is incorrect regarding the Environmental Performance Index?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has been released by Yale Center for Environmental Law and Policy and the Columbia"},{"label":"B","text":"Estonia is the top performing nation in the Environmental Performance Index."},{"label":"C","text":"The index analyses 180 countries across the world."},{"label":"D","text":"Vietnam is the worst performer of the index at 180th position."},{"label":"E","text":"There are 3 countries which have performed worse than India in the Environmental"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":753,"text":"How many days did Aditya -L1 spacecraft  take  to complete its first halo orbit around the Sun -Earth L1 point after its launch on September 2, 2023 ?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"158 days"},{"label":"B","text":"168 days"},{"label":"C","text":"188 days"},{"label":"D","text":"178 days"},{"label":"E","text":"208 days"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":754,"text":"In recent news, a drone attack was introduced on Israel and the group responsible for the attack was the Houthi group. The Houthi group belongs to which country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pakistan"},{"label":"B","text":"Syria"},{"label":"C","text":"Iran"},{"label":"D","text":"Yemen"},{"label":"E","text":"Afghanistan"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":755,"text":"As per International Energy Agency, which one of the following countries is the largest and the second largest consumer of coal? 1. China 2. India 3. South Africa 4. Brazil","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both 1 & 2"},{"label":"B","text":"Both 2 & 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Both 3 & 4"},{"label":"D","text":"Both 1 & 4"},{"label":"E","text":"Both 2 & 4"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":756,"text":"As per the MPC of August 2024, from May 2022 to Feb 2023 what was the change in the policy repo rate?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"300 basis points"},{"label":"B","text":"250 basis points"},{"label":"C","text":"200 basis points"},{"label":"D","text":"150 basis points"},{"label":"E","text":"100 basis points"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":757,"text":"SDG India Index 2023 -24, the fourth edition of the country’s principal tool for measuring national and subnational progress on the Sustainable Development Goals (SDG) was published by NITI Aayog. The overall SDG score for the country improved from 57 i n __________ to 71 in 2023 -24.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2018"},{"label":"B","text":"2017"},{"label":"C","text":"2012"},{"label":"D","text":"2014"},{"label":"E","text":"2013"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":758,"text":"Identify which among the following parameters has/have increased in the ASUSE Report published recently? 1. Number of establishments 2. Number of workers 3. GVA added","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both 1 & 2"},{"label":"B","text":"2 only"},{"label":"C","text":"3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"Both 1 & 3 only"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":759,"text":"As per the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) notification on Depositor Education Awareness Fund (DEA Fund),  funds in accounts/deposits that are inoperative/unclaimed for _________ or more are transferred to the RBI DEA Fund Scheme along with interest.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10 years"},{"label":"B","text":"9 years"},{"label":"C","text":"8 years"},{"label":"D","text":"7 years"},{"label":"E","text":"6 years"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":760,"text":"The Department of Regulation is one of the departments at the Reserve Bank of India. Identify which among the following entity (s) is/are being regulated by the above mentioned department?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Commercial Banks"},{"label":"B","text":"Co-operative Banks"},{"label":"C","text":"Non-Banking Financial Companies"},{"label":"D","text":"All India Financial Institutions"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":761,"text":"The Union Cabinet, chaired by Prime Minister Narendra Modi, has approved India signing the Biodiversity Beyond National Jurisdiction (BBNJ) agreement. The BBNJ agreement is also known as ____________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Big Seas Treaty"},{"label":"B","text":"Small Seas Treaty"},{"label":"C","text":"Deep Seas Treaty"},{"label":"D","text":"High Seas Treaty"},{"label":"E","text":"Largest Seas Treaty"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":762,"text":"In recent news, (August 2024), the Indian government has reinstated interest subsidy under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban) 2.0 and allocated _____________ for the Credit Linked Subsidy Scheme (CLSS). The scheme, which provides subsidized home loans ba sed on income, is being implemented through three verticals: Beneficiary Led Construction/Enhancement, Affordable Housing in Partnership, and In -situ Slum Redevelopment.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 3,000 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 5,000 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 6,000 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 7,000 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 4,000 crore"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":763,"text":"In the United Kingdom, the business of Parliament takes place in two Houses. Identify which among the following are the two houses in the parliament of the UK ? 1. House of King 2. House of Commons 3. House of Lords 4. House of Public","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 2"},{"label":"B","text":"1 and 3"},{"label":"C","text":"2 and 3"},{"label":"D","text":"2 and 4"},{"label":"E","text":"1 and 4"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":764,"text":"In India, the South -West Monsoon is a major seasonal wind system that brings substantial rainfall to the Indian subcontinent from June to September.  Which one of the following is responsible for the same? 1. La Nina 2. El Nino 3. Indian Ocean Dipole","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 2 only"},{"label":"B","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":765,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) came out with guidelines for the voluntary conversion of small finance banks (SFBs) into universal banks. Those intending to convert must have a minimum net worth of ________ and a satisfactory track record of at least _________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 500 crore; three years"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 1,000 crore; five years"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 1,500 crore; five years"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 2,000 crore; three years"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 2,500 crore; five years"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":766,"text":"Who is presently serving as the G -20 Sherpa for India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sitaram Yechury"},{"label":"B","text":"Sharad Powar"},{"label":"C","text":"Amit Shah"},{"label":"D","text":"Nirmala Sitharaman"},{"label":"E","text":"Amitabh Kant"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":767,"text":"Which one of the following statements is/are correct about the Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation (DICGC)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"All commercial banks including branches of foreign banks functioning in India, local area"},{"label":"B","text":"At present all co -operative banks are covered by the DICGC, while the Primary cooperative"},{"label":"C","text":"DICGC insures all deposits such as savings, fixed, current, recurring, etc."},{"label":"D","text":"DICGC insures principal and interest up to a maximum amount of ₹ 5 lakhs."},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":768,"text":"Piyush Gupta, the Indian origin Chief Executive of Singapore's largest bank ___________, will step down in March 2025. He will be succeeded by Tan Su Shan, who was appointed as deputy CEO.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"DBS Bank"},{"label":"B","text":"OCBC Bank"},{"label":"C","text":"United Overseas Bank"},{"label":"D","text":"Bank of Singapore"},{"label":"E","text":"Trust Bank"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":769,"text":"The startups that have the potential to enter the unicorn club soon are also called “___________”. These startups are often backed by angel investors or financial speculators based on future projections or apparent valuations.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lovecorn"},{"label":"B","text":"Billioncorn"},{"label":"C","text":"Soonicorns"},{"label":"D","text":"Decacorn"},{"label":"E","text":"Rushcorn"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":770,"text":"As per Economic Survey 2023 -24, the Foreign Exchange Reserves of India stood at $653.7 billion on June 21, 2024, enough to cover more than _______ of imports projected for FY25 and more than 98 per cent of total external debt outstanding at the end of  March 2024.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"9 months"},{"label":"B","text":"10 months"},{"label":"C","text":"11 months"},{"label":"D","text":"8 months"},{"label":"E","text":"7 months"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":771,"text":"Which one of the following institutions is not All India Financial Institutions?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"NABARD"},{"label":"B","text":"NHB"},{"label":"C","text":"SIDBI"},{"label":"D","text":"DICGC"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":772,"text":"As per Union Budget, the Mudra loan limit will be enhanced to _______ from the current Rs. 10 lakhs for those who have availed and successfully repaid loans previously taken under the Tarun category.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 15 lakhs"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 25 lakhs"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 30 lakhs"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 20 lakhs"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs. 35 lakhs"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":773,"text":"To standardize the opening price discovery/ equilibrium price across exchanges during special pre -open session for initial public offer (IPO) for the SME platform, the National Stock Exchange (NSE) has decided to put an overall capping up to ______ ov er the Issue price for SME IPOs.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"50%"},{"label":"B","text":"60%"},{"label":"C","text":"75%"},{"label":"D","text":"90%"},{"label":"E","text":"25%"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":774,"text":"Kantar published the 12th edition of its annual Brand Footprint India report. The report ranks the Most Chosen (in -home & out -of-home) FMCG Brands based on Consumer Reach Points (CRP’s). Identify which among the following are the top -3 most -chosen FMCG brands of I ndia? 1. Parle Products 2. Amul 3. Britannia 4. Clinic Plus","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"2, 3 and 4"},{"label":"C","text":"1, 2 and 4"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 3 and 4"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":775,"text":"Under RBI’s Fully Accessible Route (FAR), certain specified categories of Central Government securities were opened fully for non -resident investors without any restrictions, apart from being available to domestic investors as well. It has been decided to exclude all new securities of ___________ tenors from FAR.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10-year and 15 -year"},{"label":"B","text":"14-year and 30 -year"},{"label":"C","text":"10-year and 30 -year"},{"label":"D","text":"14-year and 20 -year"},{"label":"E","text":"10-year and 20 -year"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":776,"text":"CERT -In and ____________ India sign MoU for collaboration in cyber security to enhance India’s cyber -resilience in the financial  sector.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mastercard"},{"label":"B","text":"VISA"},{"label":"C","text":"RazorPay"},{"label":"D","text":"Rupay"},{"label":"E","text":"Amazon"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":777,"text":"The Presidencies of the 2023, 2024, and 2025 UN Climate Change Conferences have formed the COP Presidencies Troika and introduced the ‘Roadmap to Mission 1.5°C,’ to “significantly enhance international cooperation and the international enabling environm ent to stimulate ambition in the next round of nationally determined contributions. Identify which among the following countries are a part of this troika?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"France, Azerbaijan, and Germany"},{"label":"B","text":"United Arab Emirates (UAE), Azerbaijan, and Brazil"},{"label":"C","text":"United State of America (USA), Azerbaijan, and Brazil"},{"label":"D","text":"United Arab Emirates (UAE), India, and Brazil"},{"label":"E","text":"United Arab Emirates (UAE), Indonesia, and Brazil"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":778,"text":"As per a new report by UN body World Intellectual Property Organisation (WIPO), which one of the following countries has filed the maximum number of GenAI patents?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"China"},{"label":"B","text":"South Korea"},{"label":"C","text":"Thailand"},{"label":"D","text":"Nepal"},{"label":"E","text":"South Africa"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":779,"text":"Which organisation has signed up as the official kit sponsor of sports body, Athletics Federation of India (AFI) under which the sports brand will exclusively supply performance kits, speed suits and travel gear to all athletes under AFI?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Puma India"},{"label":"B","text":"Adidas"},{"label":"C","text":"Nike"},{"label":"D","text":"Skechers"},{"label":"E","text":"Asics"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":780,"text":"India has signed an agreement to acquire five lithium mines with a country which is also a part of the “Lithium Triangle”. The group together holds more than half of the world’s total lithium resources. Identify which among the following countries is/are a part o f the “Lithium Triangle”?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Argentina"},{"label":"B","text":"Bolivia"},{"label":"C","text":"Chile"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":781,"text":"Identify which among the following taxes have been subsumed under GST in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Central Sales Tax"},{"label":"B","text":"Central Excise Duty"},{"label":"C","text":"Service Tax"},{"label":"D","text":"OCTROI"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":782,"text":"What is the amount of out -of-pocket allowance which is given to core group athletes under Target Olympic Podium Scheme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 10,000"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 20,000"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 30,000"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 40,000"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 50,000"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":783,"text":"Identify which among the following ministries was the top achiever in achieving the targets of the National  Monetization Pipeline?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ministry of Commerce"},{"label":"B","text":"Ministry of Defence"},{"label":"C","text":"Ministry of Road Transport and Highways"},{"label":"D","text":"Ministry of Home Affairs"},{"label":"E","text":"Ministry of Finance"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":784,"text":"In which of the following sports did India not participate in the recently held Paris Olympics?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Javelin Throw"},{"label":"B","text":"Hockey"},{"label":"C","text":"Rowing"},{"label":"D","text":"Table Tennis"},{"label":"E","text":"Fencing"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":785,"text":"Identify which among the following statements is not correct with respect to IFSCA? 1. It was established in 2010, under International Financial Services Centres Authority Act, 2009. 2. It serves as a unified authority for the development and regulation of financial products, services and institutions in the International Financial Services Centre (IFSC) in India. 3. International Financial Services Centres Authority (IFSCA) has established an expert committee to position GIFTIFSC as a global trading hub.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both 1 & 2"},{"label":"B","text":"Both 2 & 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Both 1 & 3"},{"label":"D","text":"Only 2"},{"label":"E","text":"Only 1"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":786,"text":"As per Financial Stability Report, the CRAR declined for _____ that had higher shares of certain categories of loans for which risk weights were increased under regulatory measures.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"PVBs"},{"label":"B","text":"FBs"},{"label":"C","text":"PSBs"},{"label":"D","text":"Both A & B"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":787,"text":"How many information commissioners are there in the Central  Information Commission?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":788,"text":"Indian Financial Network (INFINET) is a membership -only Closed User Group (CUG) Network that comprises the Reserve Bank of India, Member Banks and Financial Institutions. As the network platform for the National Payments System, mostly catering to interbank applications _______ and ______. INFINET is also used by member banks to access RBI ______, CCIL systems, and other RBI mandated systems.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"NEFT, RTGS, and e -Kuber"},{"label":"B","text":"NEFT, UPI, and e -Kuber"},{"label":"C","text":"UPI, RTGS, and e -Kuber"},{"label":"D","text":"NEFT, RTGS, and UPI"},{"label":"E","text":"NEFT, RTGS, and CTS"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":789,"text":"Through which of the following formats, the state and UT governments borrow from","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Special Drawing Facility"},{"label":"B","text":"Ways and Means Advances"},{"label":"C","text":"Overdraft"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":790,"text":"As per the RBI Guidelines, Banks can reckon outstanding deposits with NABARD under Agriculture and overall PSL achievement, while deposits with SIDBI, MUDRA and NHB can be reckoned only for overall PSL achievement. However, the deposits with which one  of the following entities cannot be reckoned for sub -target achievement viz. SMF, NCF, Micro and weaker sections?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Deposits from NHB"},{"label":"B","text":"Deposits from SIDBI"},{"label":"C","text":"Deposits from MUDRA"},{"label":"D","text":"Deposits from NABARD"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":791,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India set up various notable committees on customer service over the years. Identify which among the following committees is incorrectly matched with its year of setting up?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Talwar Committee on Customer Service 1975"},{"label":"B","text":"Goiporia Committee 1990"},{"label":"C","text":"Tarapore Committee on Procedures and Performance Audit on Public Services 2004"},{"label":"D","text":"Damodaran Committee on Customer Service 2010"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":792,"text":"The Securities and Exchange Board of India has proposed that the government should allow tax benefits to companies investing in zero coupon zero principal bonds issued by non-profit organisations listed on the Social Stock Exchange. Under this, the in vestors or donors purchasing these bonds will receive tax benefits under Section _____ of Income Tax rules.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"80D"},{"label":"B","text":"80E"},{"label":"C","text":"80F"},{"label":"D","text":"80G"},{"label":"E","text":"80H"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":793,"text":"As per the Migration & Development brief Report, in the fourth quarter of 2023, the global average costs of sending USD 200 continued to be high at 6.4 per cent, 0.2 percentage points higher than the previous year. SDG 10.C underscores the commitment of countries to reducing the transaction costs associated with migrant remittances to less than _____. This target aims to establish a global average for sending USD 200.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5%"},{"label":"B","text":"3.5%"},{"label":"C","text":"3%"},{"label":"D","text":"2.5%"},{"label":"E","text":"1%"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":794,"text":"The maximum limit of Retirement gratuity and death gratuity shall be increased to _______ from existing Rs 20 Lakh on account of revision of Dearness Allowance payable to Central Government Employees.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 21 Lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 22 Lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 23 Lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 24 Lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs. 25 Lakh"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":795,"text":"Identify which among the following bank(s) do/does not use subsidiaries for their credit card issuance?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"State Bank of India"},{"label":"B","text":"Punjab National Bank"},{"label":"C","text":"Bank of Baroda"},{"label":"D","text":"Canara Bank"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":796,"text":"Union Home Minister Amit Shah introduced the MANAS (Madak Padarth Nisedh Asuchna  Kendra) Portal with a toll -free number _____ to seek advice on de -addiction and rehabilitation and share information on drug trafficking.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1933"},{"label":"B","text":"1911"},{"label":"C","text":"1801"},{"label":"D","text":"9011"},{"label":"E","text":"9013"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":797,"text":"The Indo -Nepal Remittance Facility (INRF, Scheme) is a cross -border remittance scheme to transfer funds from India to Nepal (one -way only), enabled under the NEFT ecosystem. One can remit up to _________ per transaction to the beneficiary residing in Nepal, provided the sender maintains an account  with any NEFT enabled bank branch in India.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹1 lakhs"},{"label":"B","text":"₹2 lakhs"},{"label":"C","text":"₹3 lakhs"},{"label":"D","text":"₹4 lakhs"},{"label":"E","text":"₹5 lakhs"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":798,"text":"With which country has India signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU), aimed at enabling Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) from both countries to participate more effectively in global markets and foster trade?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"U.S."},{"label":"B","text":"South Korea"},{"label":"C","text":"Thailand"},{"label":"D","text":"Nepal"},{"label":"E","text":"South Africa"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":799,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India has recently (November 2023) decided to directly regulate all entities facilitating cross -border payment transactions for the import and export of goods and services. In respect of import and export transactions processed by PA-CBs, the maximum value per unit of goods / services sold / purchased shall be __________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹5,00,000"},{"label":"B","text":"₹10,00,000"},{"label":"C","text":"₹15,00,000"},{"label":"D","text":"₹20,00,000"},{"label":"E","text":"₹25,00,000"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":800,"text":"Which one of the following statements is/are incorrect with respect to the Beti Bachao Beti Padhao (BBBP) scheme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The scheme was launched in 2015 under the Ministry of Women and Child Development"},{"label":"B","text":"The Pan India Expansion of the scheme covering all districts of the country was launched"},{"label":"C","text":"It aims to improve the Sex Ratio at Birth (SRB) by 2 points every year."},{"label":"D","text":"The scheme has been subsumed into Mission Shakti - Sambal sub -scheme from 2021 -"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":801,"text":"What is the name of India’s first all -in-one payment product that integrates Point of sale (POS), Quick Response (QR), and speaker into one device?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"BharatPe One"},{"label":"B","text":"PayTm One"},{"label":"C","text":"PhonePe One"},{"label":"D","text":"AmazonPay One"},{"label":"E","text":"NPCI one"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":802,"text":"The Pulitzer Prize, established in 1917, is among the world’s most prestigious honours in journalism and literature. Who was the first Indian recipient of this award, winning it in 1937 for his outstanding work in science reporting?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"R. K. Narayan"},{"label":"B","text":"Gobind Behari Lal"},{"label":"C","text":"K. K. Menon"},{"label":"D","text":"Khushwant Singh"},{"label":"E","text":"V. S. Naipaul"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":803,"text":"The Exercise Sea Dragon, a multinational anti -submarine warfare (ASW) drill hosted by the United States Navy’s 7th Fleet at Guam, is conducted with what frequency to enhance Indo -Pacific maritime security and coordination?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Quarterly"},{"label":"B","text":"Biennially"},{"label":"C","text":"Annually"},{"label":"D","text":"Once every three years"},{"label":"E","text":"Semi -annually"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":804,"text":"Who won the FIDE Women’s Grand Swiss 2025, held in Samarkand, Uzbekistan, becoming the first -ever player to win the event twice in a row?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Kateryna Lagno"},{"label":"B","text":"Koneru Humpy"},{"label":"C","text":"Vaishali Rameshbabu"},{"label":"D","text":"Divya Deshmukh"},{"label":"E","text":"Tan Zhongyi"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":805,"text":"As part of India’s effort to promote cooperative federalism and evidence -based policymaking, the NITI Aayog was established by replacing the Planning Commission in which year?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2014"},{"label":"B","text":"2015"},{"label":"C","text":"2016"},{"label":"D","text":"2017"},{"label":"E","text":"2018"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":806,"text":"Who holds the record for the most Australian Open men’s singles titles, with 10 championship wins to his name?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Roger Federer"},{"label":"B","text":"Rafael Nadal"},{"label":"C","text":"Novak Djokovic"},{"label":"D","text":"Andy Murray"},{"label":"E","text":"Pete Sampras"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":807,"text":"Who is the current President of the Confederation of Indian Industry (CII) for the 2025 –26 term?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sanjiv Puri"},{"label":"B","text":"Rajiv Memani"},{"label":"C","text":"Uday Kotak"},{"label":"D","text":"R. Dinesh"},{"label":"E","text":"Pawan Munjal"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":808,"text":"Who serves as the Ex -officio President of the Council of Scientific & Industrial Research (CSIR), India’s premier national R&D organization established in 1942?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Union Minister of Science and Technology"},{"label":"B","text":"Cabinet Secretary of India"},{"label":"C","text":"Prime Minister of India"},{"label":"D","text":"Finance Secretary (Expenditure)"},{"label":"E","text":"Director -General of CSIR"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":809,"text":"In which year did the Indian Air Force (IAF) first commission the MiG -21 aircraft, marking the beginning of India’s supersonic aviation era?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1959"},{"label":"B","text":"1960"},{"label":"C","text":"1963"},{"label":"D","text":"1965"},{"label":"E","text":"1971"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":810,"text":"What was the theme of World Population Day 2025, observed annually on July 11?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"“Ensuring Reproductive Rights and Choices for All”"},{"label":"B","text":"“Empowering young people to create the families they want in a fair and hopeful world”"},{"label":"C","text":"“Building a Sustainable Future through Family Planning”"},{"label":"D","text":"“Investing in Women for a Resilient Future”"},{"label":"E","text":"“Population and Development: Balancing People and Planet”"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":811,"text":"The International Day for the Elimination of Violence Against Women is observed annually on which date to raise awareness about gender -based violence worldwide?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"November 20"},{"label":"B","text":"November 25"},{"label":"C","text":"December 1"},{"label":"D","text":"December 10"},{"label":"E","text":"October 11"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":812,"text":"Who is the author of the novel “The Loneliness of Sonia and Sunny,” recently shortlisted for the Booker Prize?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Arundhati Roy"},{"label":"B","text":"Jhumpa Lahiri"},{"label":"C","text":"Kiran Desai"},{"label":"D","text":"Anita Desai"},{"label":"E","text":"Salman Rushdie"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":813,"text":"Identify which among the following countries are members of the European Free Trade Association (EFTA)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Iceland"},{"label":"B","text":"Liechtenstein"},{"label":"C","text":"Norway"},{"label":"D","text":"Switzerland"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":814,"text":"Infosys signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with which global financial technology company to enhance cross -border payment solutions for financial institutions?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Visa"},{"label":"B","text":"PayPal"},{"label":"C","text":"Mastercard"},{"label":"D","text":"American Express"},{"label":"E","text":"Ripple Labs"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":815,"text":"On which of the following daily consumption articles was the GST rate reduced to NIL, effective 22nd September 2025, as per the recommendations of the 56th GST Council Meeting?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pre -packaged paneer"},{"label":"B","text":"Cheese & Dairy Spreads"},{"label":"C","text":"Pre -packaged Namkeens, Bhujia & Mixtures"},{"label":"D","text":"Butter and Ghee"},{"label":"E","text":"Juice -based  drinks"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":816,"text":"India's  agreement  for the supply  of fortified  rice primarily  caters  to which  of the following  Sustainable  Development  Goals  (SDGs )? 1. By 2030, ensure sustainable food production systems and implement resilient agricultural practices that increase productivity and production. 2. By 2030, end hunger and ensure access by all people, in particular the poor and people in vulnerable situations, including infants, to safe, nutritious and sufficient food all year round. 3. By 2030, end all forms of malnutrition, including achieving, by 2025, the internationally agreed targets on stunting and wasting in children under 5 years of age.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 only"},{"label":"B","text":"2 only"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 2 only"},{"label":"D","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"E","text":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":817,"text":"Which  state  became  the first in India  to issue  identity  cards  for women  Self-Help Group  (SHG)  members?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Kerala"},{"label":"B","text":"Tamil  Nadu"},{"label":"C","text":"Andhra  Pradesh"},{"label":"D","text":"Karnataka"},{"label":"E","text":"Maharashtra"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":818,"text":"Which organisation  earned the Guinness World Record for issuing the most life insurance policies in a single day, with over 5.88 lakh policies sold across India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"HDFC Life Insurance"},{"label":"B","text":"ICICI Prudential Life Insurance"},{"label":"C","text":"Life Insurance Corporation of India (LIC)"},{"label":"D","text":"SBI Life Insurance"},{"label":"E","text":"Max Life Insurance"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":819,"text":"Which fintech platform became one of the first non -banking entities to offer Central Bank Digital Currency (CBDC) e₹ wallets in collaboration with the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) and Yes Bank?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Paytm"},{"label":"B","text":"PhonePe"},{"label":"C","text":"MobiKwik"},{"label":"D","text":"Razorpay"},{"label":"E","text":"Google Pay"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":820,"text":"Which regulatory body is responsible for overseeing and regulating Venture Capital Funds (VCFs) in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Reserve Bank of India (RBI)"},{"label":"B","text":"Ministry of Finance"},{"label":"C","text":"Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI)"},{"label":"D","text":"Small Industries Development Bank of India (SIDBI)"},{"label":"E","text":"NITI Aayog"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":821,"text":"Which country hosted the Women’s Hockey Asia Cup 2025?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"India"},{"label":"B","text":"Japan"},{"label":"C","text":"South Korea"},{"label":"D","text":"China"},{"label":"E","text":"Malaysia"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":822,"text":"Which international financial institution has introduced the India Green Finance Facility (IGFF) in partnership with the Green Climate Fund (GCF) to boost clean energy investments in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"World Bank"},{"label":"B","text":"Asian Development Bank (ADB)"},{"label":"C","text":"International Monetary Fund (IMF)"},{"label":"D","text":"Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB)"},{"label":"E","text":"International Finance Corporation (IFC)"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":823,"text":"As per the revised guidelines declared by the National Payments Corporation of India (NPCI), effective September 15, 2025, what is the new maximum UPI transaction limit for Person -to-Merchant (P2M) payments in sectors such as Capital Markets, Insuran ce, Government e -Marketplace, and Travel?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹2 lakh per transaction"},{"label":"B","text":"₹3 lakh per transaction"},{"label":"C","text":"₹4 lakh per transaction"},{"label":"D","text":"₹5 lakh per transaction"},{"label":"E","text":"₹10 lakh per transaction"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":824,"text":"The headquarters of the Geological Survey of India (GSI), which celebrated its 175th Foundation Day in 2025, is located in which Indian city?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"New Delhi"},{"label":"B","text":"Hyderabad"},{"label":"C","text":"Kolkata"},{"label":"D","text":"Bengaluru"},{"label":"E","text":"Pune"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":825,"text":"In the abbreviation AERB, which word does the letter ‘E’ stand for?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Environment"},{"label":"B","text":"Electricity"},{"label":"C","text":"Energy"},{"label":"D","text":"Engineering"},{"label":"E","text":"Establishment"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":826,"text":"Which additional Nobel Prize was introduced in 1968 by the Central Bank of Sweden (Sveriges Riksbank ) to commemorate its 300th anniversary?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nobel Prize in Peace"},{"label":"B","text":"Nobel Prize in Literature"},{"label":"C","text":"Nobel Prize in Economic Sciences"},{"label":"D","text":"Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine"},{"label":"E","text":"Nobel Prize in Chemistry"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":827,"text":"India’s first bamboo -based ethanol plant, also recognised  as the world’s first green bamboo bioethanol plant, has been set up in which Indian state?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Arunachal Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Meghalaya"},{"label":"C","text":"Assam"},{"label":"D","text":"Tripura"},{"label":"E","text":"Manipur"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":828,"text":"What is the name of the world’s first tri -services all -women circumnavigation sailing expedition, flagged off from the Gateway of India, Mumbai?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sagarika"},{"label":"B","text":"Samudra Pradakshina"},{"label":"C","text":"Triveni Shakti"},{"label":"D","text":"Nari Shakti Sagar Parikrama"},{"label":"E","text":"Vayu -Nari Mission"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":829,"text":"As per the Constitution of India, what happens when the office of the Vice President of India becomes vacant due to resignation or any other reason?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The President nominates an interim Vice President until elections are held."},{"label":"B","text":"The Prime Minister temporarily assumes the duties of the Vice President."},{"label":"C","text":"The Deputy Chairman of the Rajya Sabha presides over the Upper House until a new Vice"},{"label":"D","text":"The Chief Justice of India acts as the Vice President until Parliament meets."},{"label":"E","text":"The Election Commission directly appoints a new Vice President."}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":830,"text":"Who is the current Director General of the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR), who also serves as the Secretary of the Department of Health Research?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Dr. Soumya Swaminathan"},{"label":"B","text":"Dr. Rajiv Bahl"},{"label":"C","text":"Dr. Balram Bhargava"},{"label":"D","text":"Dr. Randeep Guleria"},{"label":"E","text":"Dr. V.K. Paul"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":831,"text":"The Image (Nano Banana), recently introduced as an advanced image editing AI model, has been based on which model?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bloom"},{"label":"B","text":"Llama 3.1"},{"label":"C","text":"Gemini 2.5 Flash"},{"label":"D","text":"Claude 3.7 Sonnet"},{"label":"E","text":"Grok"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":832,"text":"What is the name of the newly commissioned Indian Navy establishment in Gurugram, serving as a hub for Command, Control, and Maritime Domain Awareness (MDA) operations?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"INS Vikrant"},{"label":"B","text":"INS Aravali"},{"label":"C","text":"INS Hansa"},{"label":"D","text":"INS Shivaji"},{"label":"E","text":"INS Kalinga"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":833,"text":"What is the authorised capital of the India Infrastructure Finance Company Ltd (IIFCL) as on 31st March 2025?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹5,000 Crore"},{"label":"B","text":"₹8,000 Crore"},{"label":"C","text":"₹10,000 Crore"},{"label":"D","text":"₹15,000 Crore"},{"label":"E","text":"₹12,000 Crore"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":834,"text":"As per the latest update, how many Maharatna Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs) are there in India after Hindustan Aeronautics Limited (HAL) was upgraded to Maharatna status?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"12"},{"label":"B","text":"13"},{"label":"C","text":"14"},{"label":"D","text":"15"},{"label":"E","text":"16"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":835,"text":"Thewa Art, a traditional form of jewellery -making  that fuses intricately worked gold foil onto colored glass, originated in which Indian state?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"B","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"C","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"D","text":"Uttar Pradesh"},{"label":"E","text":"Maharashtra"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":836,"text":"Identify which among the following is NOT a subsidiary of IFCI Limited?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"IFCI Venture Capital Fund Ltd. (IVCF)"},{"label":"B","text":"IFCI MPCON Ltd."},{"label":"C","text":"IFCI Infrastructure Development Ltd. (IIDL)"},{"label":"D","text":"India Infrastructure Finance Company Ltd. (IIFCL)"},{"label":"E","text":"Stock Holding Corporation of India Ltd. (SHCIL)"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":837,"text":"Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel earned the title “Sardar” (leader) for his leadership during which major event of India’s freedom struggle?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Kheda Satyagraha"},{"label":"B","text":"Champaran Movement"},{"label":"C","text":"Bardoli Satyagraha"},{"label":"D","text":"Non -Cooperation Movement"},{"label":"E","text":"Quit India Movement"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":838,"text":"Based on the Top 10 Largest Countries by Area (2025), which of the following statements is not correct?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"China – 3rd Largest Country"},{"label":"B","text":"Brazil – 5th Largest Country"},{"label":"C","text":"USA – Largest Country"},{"label":"D","text":"Canada – 2nd Largest Country"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":839,"text":"Identify which among the following banks are members of the Partnership for Carbon Accounting Financials (PCAF)? 1. Union Bank of India (UBI) 2. Indian Overseas Bank (IOB) 3. Punjab National Bank (PNB) 4. IDFC FIRST Bank Select the correct answer using the code given below:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 2 only"},{"label":"B","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 4 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 4"},{"label":"E","text":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":840,"text":"Identify which among the following initiatives has been introduced by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare (MoHFW) and the Ministry of Women and Child Development (MoWCD) to empower women and families for a healthier India through comprehensive health screening s and community -driven support systems?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nari Shakti Swasthya Abhiyaan"},{"label":"B","text":"Swasthya Samriddhi Pariwar Yojana"},{"label":"C","text":"SwasthyaSarthi Mission"},{"label":"D","text":"Swasth Nari Sashakt Parivar Abhiyaan"},{"label":"E","text":"Samagra Aarogya Sashakt Pariwar  Programme"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":841,"text":"From which date was the Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) framework formally implemented in India under the Companies Act, 2013?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"January 1, 2013"},{"label":"B","text":"April 1, 2014"},{"label":"C","text":"March 31, 2015"},{"label":"D","text":"July 1, 2016"},{"label":"E","text":"October 1, 2017"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":842,"text":"Identify which among the following organisations is responsible for conducting the All India Debt and Investment Survey (AIDIS)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"NITI Aayog"},{"label":"B","text":"Reserve Bank of India (RBI)"},{"label":"C","text":"National Statistics Office (NSO) under the Ministry of Statistics and Programme"},{"label":"D","text":"Ministry of Finance"},{"label":"E","text":"Indian Statistical Institute (ISI)"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":843,"text":"As per the Report of the Committee to develop a Framework for Responsible and Ethical Enablement of Artificial Intelligence (FREE -AI) in the Financial Sector, the framework is structured around how many strategic pillars?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Four"},{"label":"B","text":"Five"},{"label":"C","text":"Six"},{"label":"D","text":"Seven"},{"label":"E","text":"Eight"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":844,"text":"Identify which among the following is not a parameter under the Quality Dimension of the Reserve Bank of India’s Financial Inclusion Index (FI -Index)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Financial Literacy"},{"label":"B","text":"Consumer Protection"},{"label":"C","text":"Inequalities and Deficiencies in Services"},{"label":"D","text":"Credit Accessibility and Outreach"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":845,"text":"Under the Reserve Bank of India’s Integrated Ombudsman Scheme, 2021 , an Ombudsman can be appointed for a maximum period of how many years at a time?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Two years"},{"label":"B","text":"Three years"},{"label":"C","text":"Four years"},{"label":"D","text":"Five years"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":846,"text":"The 11th World Green Economy Summit (WGES) was held, focusing on positioning itself as a global hub for sustainable development and climate action. The summit was organised by the DSCE, DEWA, and the World Green Economy Organization (WGEO). The event took place in _______ and was co -hosted with _______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Abu Dhabi; Expo 2025"},{"label":"B","text":"Riyadh; World Energy Forum 2025"},{"label":"C","text":"Dubai; WETEX 2025"},{"label":"D","text":"Doha; Green Future Summit 2025"},{"label":"E","text":"Muscat; Global Sustainability Meet 2025"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":847,"text":"As per the Reserve Bank of India (Regulation of Payment Aggregators) Directions, 2025, for an entity seeking to become a Payment Aggregator (PA), what is the minimum net worth requirement at the time of registration?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹10 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"₹15 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"₹20 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"₹25 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":848,"text":"Identify which among the following schemes implemented by the Government of India are aimed at promoting Skill Development and Vocational Training across various sectors of the economy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Jan Shikshan Sansthan (JSS)"},{"label":"B","text":"Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY)"},{"label":"C","text":"National Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme (NAPS)"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":849,"text":"Which one of the following categories of people is not targeted under the Financial Education Programme for Adults (FEPA) introduced to promote financial literacy among financially excluded sections?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Farmers"},{"label":"B","text":"Anganwadi and ASHA Workers"},{"label":"C","text":"Self -Help Groups and Skill -Development Trainees"},{"label":"D","text":"Government School Students"},{"label":"E","text":"Women’s Groups"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":850,"text":"Identify which among the following is a Kharif forage crop?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Egyptian clover"},{"label":"B","text":"Oat"},{"label":"C","text":"Cluster bean"},{"label":"D","text":"Lucerne/Alfalfa"},{"label":"E","text":"Perennial ryegrass"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":851,"text":"As per the Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare Annual Report 2024 -25, which of the following statements is/are correct? 1. Net sown area in India is more than half of the total geographical area. 2. Sugarcane occupies a significant area among commercial crops. 3. A major share of irrigation in India is done using tubewells.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1 and 2"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 2 and 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 1 and 3"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":852,"text":"Identify which among the following is not a quantitative tool used by the Reserve Bank of India to control the money supply?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Open Market Operations (OMO)"},{"label":"B","text":"Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR)"},{"label":"C","text":"Statutory Liquidity Ratio (SLR)"},{"label":"D","text":"Credit Rationing"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":853,"text":"Basel III norms are applicable to which of the following?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Private Banks"},{"label":"B","text":"Regional Rural Banks"},{"label":"C","text":"Local Area Banks"},{"label":"D","text":"Cooperative Banks"},{"label":"E","text":"Payment Banks"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":854,"text":"Identify which among the following is updated daily on the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) website?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Liquidity Adjustment Facility"},{"label":"B","text":"Exchange Rates"},{"label":"C","text":"Money Market Operations"},{"label":"D","text":"Government Securities Market Data"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":855,"text":"As per the Master Direction – Reserve Bank of India (Interest Rate on Deposits), interest on domestic rupee savings deposits shall be calculated on a daily product basis, with a uniform rate applicable on balances up to what amount?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹50,000"},{"label":"B","text":"₹75,000"},{"label":"C","text":"₹1,00,000"},{"label":"D","text":"₹1,50,000"},{"label":"E","text":"₹2,00,000"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":856,"text":"The World Mental Health Day is observed every year to raise awareness about mental health issues and to mobilize global efforts in support of mental well -being. On which date is this day celebrated annually across the world?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"7th October"},{"label":"B","text":"8th October"},{"label":"C","text":"9th October"},{"label":"D","text":"10th October"},{"label":"E","text":"11th October"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":857,"text":"In the QS World University Rankings 2026, which among the following Indian institutions has been placed within the top 500 universities globally, reflecting its strong academic and research performance?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Jawaharlal Nehru University"},{"label":"B","text":"Indian Institute of Technology Delhi (IITD)"},{"label":"C","text":"Indian Institute of Technology BHU Varanasi"},{"label":"D","text":"Jadavpur University"},{"label":"E","text":"Birla Institute of Technology and Science"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":858,"text":"Identify which among the following states represent the top three rice -producing states in India in 2023 –24 according to the Economic Survey 2024 –25? 1. Telangana 2. Uttar Pradesh 3. Punjab","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2 only"},{"label":"B","text":"1 only"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 2"},{"label":"D","text":"2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":859,"text":"With reference to the findings of the Global Innovation Index (GII) 2025: Innovation at a Crossroads, consider the following statements regarding India’s performance: 1. India’s Input Rank in the Global Innovation Index 2025 is 44. 2. India’s Output Rank in the same index is 32. 3. India ranks at par with its development level.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 only"},{"label":"B","text":"1 and 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"2 only"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":860,"text":"Which of these countries is NOT included in the top 5 most competitive economies globally as per the International Institute for Management Development (IMD) World Competitiveness Ranking 2025?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Switzerland"},{"label":"B","text":"Singapore"},{"label":"C","text":"Hong Kong"},{"label":"D","text":"Norway"},{"label":"E","text":"UAE"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":861,"text":"Identify which among the following components of the Human Development Index (HDI) has shown improvement in India since the 1990s, according to the Human Development Report 2025? 1. Longevity (Life expectancy at birth) 2. Education/Knowledge 3. Income per capita","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 only"},{"label":"B","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"2 only"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":862,"text":"Rating and Investment Information, Inc. (R&I) recently upgraded India’s long -term sovereign credit rating to ‘BBB+’ from ‘BBB’, while maintaining a Stable outlook. The R&I rating agency belongs to which of the following countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United States of America"},{"label":"B","text":"Japan"},{"label":"C","text":"United Kingdom"},{"label":"D","text":"France"},{"label":"E","text":"Germany"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":863,"text":"Which fintech company has recently introduced India’s first fully UPI -powered physical bank branch, offering digital -first banking services such as instant account opening and seamless UPI transactions?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"PhonePe"},{"label":"B","text":"Google Pay (GPay)"},{"label":"C","text":"Paytm"},{"label":"D","text":"slice"},{"label":"E","text":"BharatPe"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":864,"text":"With reference to important international declarations and organizations completing milestone years in 2025, consider the following statements: 1. The Beijing Declaration and Platform for Action completes 30 years in 2025. 2. The Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) celebrates its 80th anniversary in 2025. 3. The UN Security Council Resolution 1325 on Women, Peace and Security completes 25 years in 2025. Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 2"},{"label":"D","text":"2 only"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":865,"text":"The Citizen’s Charter of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) aims to enhance transparency, accountability, and efficiency in the delivery of public services to citizens. The Charter is currently being implemented in _____ departments of the RBI.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"15"},{"label":"B","text":"18"},{"label":"C","text":"11"},{"label":"D","text":"20"},{"label":"E","text":"23"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":866,"text":"India is planning to establish a small nuclear reactor programme as part of its clean energy transition. Identify which among the following pairs of countries already have operational or grid-connected small nuclear reactors (SMRs)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Russia, Japan"},{"label":"B","text":"Japan, China"},{"label":"C","text":"Russia, China"},{"label":"D","text":"China, South Korea"},{"label":"E","text":"Japan, South Korea"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":867,"text":"Identify which among the following statements regarding the conditions under which a payment bank can be upgraded to a small finance bank is correct?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A payment bank can apply for conversion into an SFB immediately after it starts operations,"},{"label":"B","text":"Conversion is permitted only if the payment bank has a satisfactory track record of"},{"label":"C","text":"The payment bank must have already obtained scheduled bank status before applying for"},{"label":"D","text":"There is no minimum paid -up capital requirement for a payment bank to convert into an"},{"label":"E","text":"The payment bank must first convert to a universal bank before becoming an SFB."}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":868,"text":"Identify which among the following statements regarding the features of a BSBDA (Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account) under Reserve Bank of India guidelines is correct?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The account holder is required to maintain a minimum balance of ₹1,000 every month."},{"label":"B","text":"The account holder is eligible to open multiple BSBDA accounts in the same bank"},{"label":"C","text":"The account can be opened by any individual —there are no age or income criteria set for"},{"label":"D","text":"A BSBDA account permits unlimited free withdrawals from ATMs every month."},{"label":"E","text":"A BSBDA -Small Account variant allows total credits of up to ₹5 lakh in a year."}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":869,"text":"Since 2004 –05, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) has suspended the issuance of new licences for which category of banks as part of its sector -consolidation measures?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Regional Rural Banks (RRBs)"},{"label":"B","text":"Urban Co -operative Banks (UCBs)"},{"label":"C","text":"Local Area Banks (LABs)"},{"label":"D","text":"Private Sector Banks (PSBs)"},{"label":"E","text":"Small Finance Banks (SFBs)"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":870,"text":"In several countries across the world, the administrative, legislative, and judicial functions are distributed among different capital cities instead of being concentrated in a single city. With reference to this, consider the following countries and identify which among them have more than one capital city officially designated for different branches of governance: 1. South Africa 2. Singapore 3. Bolivia Select the correct combination using the code given below:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"1 only"},{"label":"C","text":"3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":871,"text":"The UNESCO World Heritage List includes several Indian sites recognized for their cultural, historical, and architectural significance. With reference to this, consider the following sites: 1. Elephanta Caves 2. Chhatrapati Shivaji Terminus (formerly Victoria Terminus) 3. Fatehpur Sikri 4. Shantiniketan Which of the above sites are included in the UNESCO World Heritage List?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"2, 3 and 4"},{"label":"C","text":"1, 3 and 4"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2, 3 and 4"},{"label":"E","text":"1 and 4"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":872,"text":"The Government of India’s S3WAAS platform, developed by the National Informatics Centre (NIC), enables the creation of secure and accessible websites for district administrations across the country. With reference to this initiative, which of the following words does NOT represent the letter ‘S’ in S3WAAS?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Smart"},{"label":"B","text":"Scalable"},{"label":"C","text":"Sugamya"},{"label":"D","text":"Secure"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":873,"text":"Four of the following mountain peaks belong to the same country. Which one does not belong to that category?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Anamudi"},{"label":"B","text":"Mount Everest"},{"label":"C","text":"Mount Kamet"},{"label":"D","text":"Kanchenjunga"},{"label":"E","text":"Nanda Devi"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":874,"text":"NASA’s Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL) published a mosaic image captured by the Mars Odyssey’s THEMIS instrument, showing Olympus Mons, the largest volcano in the solar system. Olympus Mons is located on which planet?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Venus"},{"label":"B","text":"Jupiter"},{"label":"C","text":"Saturn"},{"label":"D","text":"Mercury"},{"label":"E","text":"Mars"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":875,"text":"Shri Piyush Goyal is a senior leader in the Union Cabinet who has been entrusted with several important economic and infrastructural portfolios over the years. With reference to his current responsibilities in the Union Government, consider the following ministries: 1. Ministry of Railways 2. Ministry of Commerce and Industry 3. Ministry of Coal Which of the above ministries has ever been served by Piyush Goyal?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 only"},{"label":"B","text":"2 only"},{"label":"C","text":"3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1 and 2"},{"label":"E","text":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":876,"text":"The Securitisation and Reconstruction of Financial Assets and Enforcement of Security Interest (SARFAESI) Act, 2002 provides for the establishment of a particular type of institution to acquire and manage non -performing assets (NPAs) of banks and finan cial institutions. Which one of the following types of entities has been established under the provisions of this Act?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Asset Reconstruction Company (ARC)"},{"label":"B","text":"Asset Management Company (AMC)"},{"label":"C","text":"Asset Securitisation Fund (ASF)"},{"label":"D","text":"Debt Recovery Tribunal (DRT)"},{"label":"E","text":"Credit Information Company (CIC)"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":877,"text":"Match the following major rivers with the continents on which they flow: Rivers                Continents","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nile                    1. South America"},{"label":"B","text":"Amazon      2. North America"},{"label":"C","text":"Yangtze      3. Asia"},{"label":"D","text":"Mississippi    4. Africa"},{"label":"A","text":"A-4, B-1, C-3, D-2"},{"label":"B","text":"A-1, B-2, C-4, D-3"},{"label":"C","text":"A-2, B-4, C-3, D-1"},{"label":"D","text":"A-4, B-3, C-1, D-2"},{"label":"E","text":"A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":878,"text":"The Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO) plays a vital role in advancing India’s space technology and promoting the peaceful use of outer space. Consider the following statements about ISRO: 1. Dr. Vikram Sarabhai was the first Chairman of ISRO. 2. ISRO was established in the year 1957 under the Department of Space. 3. The headquarters of ISRO is located in Chennai, Tamil Nadu. Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 only"},{"label":"B","text":"1 and 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"2 only"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":879,"text":"The Green National Highways Corridor Project (GNHCP) is being implemented by the Government of India in partnership with the World Bank to promote the development of safe, green, and climate -resilient highways. Under this project, in which of the following state/states are the highway corridors being developed?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Himachal Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"C","text":"Uttar Pradesh"},{"label":"D","text":"Andhra Pradesh"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":880,"text":"As per the recent RBI guidelines revising the prudential norms for Urban Cooperative Banks (UCBs), match the following tiers of UCBs with their corresponding maximum individual housing loan limits per dwelling unit: List I (Tier of UCBs)  List II (Loan Limit) 1. Tier –I UCBs  A. ₹1.40 crore 2. Tier –II UCBs  B. ₹2 crore 3. Tier –III UCBs  C. ₹3 crore 4. Tier –IV UCBs  D. ₹60 lakh Select the correct code:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1–D, 2–A, 3–B, 4–C"},{"label":"B","text":"1–A, 2–B, 3–C, 4–D"},{"label":"C","text":"1–C, 2–D, 3–A, 4–B"},{"label":"D","text":"1–B, 2–C, 3–D, 4–A"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":881,"text":"Minimum credit rating required for NBFCs is:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"BB+"},{"label":"B","text":"Aaa"},{"label":"C","text":"BBB -"},{"label":"D","text":"AA+"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":882,"text":"In recent news, in the month of October 2020, the Government has notified that a “National Authority of Ship Recycling” will be set up to look after the sustainable development of the Ship Recycling industry, monitoring the compliance to environment -friendly  norms. In which of the following states will it be located?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"B","text":"Andhra Pradesh"},{"label":"C","text":"Kerala"},{"label":"D","text":"Maharashtra"},{"label":"E","text":"Goa"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":883,"text":"ASEEM Portal is related to_____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Livelihood and Employment"},{"label":"B","text":"Prevention of Human Trafficking"},{"label":"C","text":"Bootstrap startups"},{"label":"D","text":"Rural Development"},{"label":"E","text":"Promotion of MSMEs"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":884,"text":"Which fintech company has recently introduced India’s first fully UPI -powered physical bank branch, offering digital -first banking services such as instant account opening and seamless UPI transactions?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"PhonePe"},{"label":"B","text":"Google Pay (GPay)"},{"label":"C","text":"Paytm"},{"label":"D","text":"slice"},{"label":"E","text":"BharatPe"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":887,"text":"In recent news, the State of the World&#39;s Forests 2022 (SOFO 2022) was published by the   _______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP)"},{"label":"B","text":"United Nations Development Programme (UNDP)"},{"label":"C","text":"United Nations Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)"},{"label":"D","text":"International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN)"},{"label":"E","text":"Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC)"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":889,"text":"The Union budget for the year 2021 -22 has allocated ₹1.1 trillion for the Indian Railways, out of this amount how much will  be utilized for capital expenditure for 2021 -22 to expand rail infrastructure in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹1.07 trillion"},{"label":"B","text":"₹1.02 trillion"},{"label":"C","text":"₹0.95 trillion"},{"label":"D","text":"₹1.04 trillion"},{"label":"E","text":"₹1.09 trillion"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":890,"text":"The Finance Ministry has extended the ‘Emergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme’ (ECLGS) to support  MSMEs  engaged in travel, tourism and hospitality sectors to overcome the impact of the COVID -19 pandemic impact. The scheme will be expanded by  _______ to ₹5 lakh crore.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹25,000 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"₹30,000 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"₹35,000 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"₹45,000 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"₹50,000 crore"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":891,"text":"In Feb 2021, Ngozi Okonjo -Iweala was appointed as the seventh Director -General of the World Trade Organization, becoming the first woman head of the body. She belongs to which of the following countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ethiopia"},{"label":"B","text":"Nigeria"},{"label":"C","text":"Kenya"},{"label":"D","text":"Eritrea"},{"label":"E","text":"Algeria"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":892,"text":"Which of these country will host World Environment Day 2022 in June 2022?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Switzerland"},{"label":"B","text":"Sweden"},{"label":"C","text":"Finland"},{"label":"D","text":"Norway"},{"label":"E","text":"Italy"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":894,"text":"How many information commissioners are there in the Central  Information Commission?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":895,"text":"The tropical cyclones forming over different ocean basins are named by the concerned regional specialised meteorological centres (RSMCs) and regional Tropical Cyclone Warning Centres (TCWCs). As per the &#39;List of North Indian Ocean Tropical Cyclone Names&#39;, what is the name of the next cyclone aft er cyclone &#39;Biparjoy&#39; and the name has been recommended by which country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Prahar, Bangladesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Akhand, India"},{"label":"C","text":"Tej, India"},{"label":"D","text":"Bhanwar, Nepal"},{"label":"E","text":"Prachand, Sri Lanka"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":896,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India has constructed a composite Digital Payments Index (DPI) to capture the extent of digitisation of payments across the country. Which one of the following is not a parameter that enables the measurement of deepening and penetr ation of digital payments in the country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Payment Enabler"},{"label":"B","text":"Payment Infrastructure"},{"label":"C","text":"Payment Analysis"},{"label":"D","text":"Payment Performance"},{"label":"E","text":"Consumer Centricity"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":897,"text":"Monthly Premium made by India citizen at 18 years of age, under Atal Pension Yojana, opting for Rs. 5000 monthly pension after attaining 60 years of age,  is Rs. ______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"185"},{"label":"B","text":"210"},{"label":"C","text":"225"},{"label":"D","text":"305"},{"label":"E","text":"324"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":899,"text":"Which one of the following states was among the top -3 states in terms of highest GST revenues in June 2023? 1. Haryana 2. Karnataka 3. Gujarat 4. Uttar Pradesh 5. Maharashtra","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 2, 3 and 5"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 1, 3 &amp; 4"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 1, 2 &amp; 5"},{"label":"D","text":"Only 3, 4 &amp; 5"},{"label":"E","text":"Only 2, 3 &amp; 4"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":900,"text":"HCL Technologies has declared to roll out a one -time special bonus of Rs 700 crore to its employees globally, in recognition of its recent milestone of crossing the _________ mark in revenue for 2020.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"$15 billion"},{"label":"B","text":"$10 billion"},{"label":"C","text":"$50 billion"},{"label":"D","text":"$25 billion"},{"label":"E","text":"$30 billion"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":901,"text":"Amazon’s market value was $250 billion in the year 2015, two decades after its founding in the year 1995. This major e -commerce company was started as which of the following in its earliest days?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pantry"},{"label":"B","text":"Apparel store"},{"label":"C","text":"Courier store"},{"label":"D","text":"Book store"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":902,"text":"Which country hosted the Women’s Hockey Asia Cup 2025?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"India"},{"label":"B","text":"Japan"},{"label":"C","text":"South Korea"},{"label":"D","text":"China"},{"label":"E","text":"Malaysia"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":903,"text":"In recent news, Indian security forces have been trained in _________ “Krav Maga” to counter China&#39;s People Liberation Army (PLA) during patrolling along the Line of Actual Control (LAC).","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Russia"},{"label":"B","text":"Caribbean Island"},{"label":"C","text":"Israel"},{"label":"D","text":"France"},{"label":"E","text":"USA"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":905,"text":"What is the name of the newly commissioned Indian Navy establishment in Gurugram, serving as a hub for Command, Control, and Maritime Domain Awareness (MDA) operations?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"INS Vikrant"},{"label":"B","text":"INS Aravali"},{"label":"C","text":"INS Hansa"},{"label":"D","text":"INS Shivaji"},{"label":"E","text":"INS Kalinga"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":906,"text":"As per the Union Budget 2023 -24, the highest surcharge rate in personal income tax has been reduced from 37% to _____ in the new tax regime for income above ₹2 crore.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"15%"},{"label":"B","text":"36%"},{"label":"C","text":"17%"},{"label":"D","text":"25%"},{"label":"E","text":"30%"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":907,"text":"Identify which among the following is NOT a subsidiary of IFCI Limited?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"IFCI Venture Capital Fund Ltd. (IVCF)"},{"label":"B","text":"IFCI MPCON Ltd."},{"label":"C","text":"IFCI Infrastructure Development Ltd. (IIDL)"},{"label":"D","text":"India Infrastructure Finance Company Ltd. (IIFCL)"},{"label":"E","text":"Stock Holding Corporation of India Ltd. (SHCIL)"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":908,"text":"In recent news, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) has tightened norms related to public deposit acceptance by housing finance companies (HFCs). What is the maximum deposit duration for the housing finance companies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"60 months"},{"label":"B","text":"50 months"},{"label":"C","text":"40 months"},{"label":"D","text":"30 months"},{"label":"E","text":"20 months"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":909,"text":"The Ministry  of New and Renewable Energy (MNRE) has introduced the scheme PM KUSUM for farmers with the aim to add solar and other renewable capacity of 25,750 MW by 2022. Consider the following  given statements regarding this scheme and identify the one which is not a feature of the same?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Subsidy would be provided on diesel for running diesel pumps  and thus provide the"},{"label":"B","text":"Individual farmers will be supported to install standalone solar Agriculture pumps"},{"label":"C","text":"The farmer will be able to use the generated solar power to meet the irrigation needs and"},{"label":"D","text":"In case cultivated fields are chosen for setting up solar power projects , the farmers could"},{"label":"E","text":"The scheme would ensure that sufficient local solar/ other renewable energy -based"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":910,"text":"The World Forestry Congress (WFC) is held every six years since 1926 under the auspices of the _______, in association with the government of the host country.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO)"},{"label":"B","text":"United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP)"},{"label":"C","text":"Conservation International"},{"label":"D","text":"Worldwide fund for Nature (WWF)"},{"label":"E","text":"Greenpeace"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":911,"text":"As per Foreign Trade Policy 2023, towns that produce goods worth at least ______ can be recognized as towns of export excellence, based on their growth potential for exports.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 850 Crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 750 Crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 650 Crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 550 Crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 450 Crore"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":912,"text":"Germany has recently committed to provide additional support worth Euro 10 billion to India by the year _______ to support green growth initiatives.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2026"},{"label":"B","text":"2027"},{"label":"C","text":"2028"},{"label":"D","text":"2029"},{"label":"E","text":"2030"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":913,"text":"What is the name of India’s first all -in-one payment product that integrates Point of sale (POS), Quick Response (QR), and speaker into one device?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"BharatPe One"},{"label":"B","text":"PayTm One"},{"label":"C","text":"PhonePe One"},{"label":"D","text":"AmazonPay One"},{"label":"E","text":"NPCI one"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":914,"text":"T Raja Kumar, a senior advisor at MHA, has been appointed as the president of the Financial Action Task Force (FATF), the global money laundering and terrorism financing watchdog. He is from which country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nepal"},{"label":"B","text":"Bhutan"},{"label":"C","text":"Singapore"},{"label":"D","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"label":"E","text":"Thailand"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":915,"text":"Which of these is/are the dimensions across which the states and districts have been assessed under the Social Progress Index (SPI) for States and Districts made by the Institute for Competitiveness and Social Progress Imperative? 1. Basic Human Needs 2. Innovation 3. Foundations of Wellbeing 4. Opportunity 5. Foundations of Healthy life","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1, 3 and 4"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 2, 3 and 4"},{"label":"D","text":"Only 1 and 2"},{"label":"E","text":"Only 2 and 3"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":916,"text":"ATMs that are owned and operated by non -bank entities are called as _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Blue Label ATMs"},{"label":"B","text":"White Label ATMs"},{"label":"C","text":"Brown Label ATMs"},{"label":"D","text":"Black Label ATMs"},{"label":"E","text":"Red Label ATMs"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":917,"text":"Which one of the following statements are correct with respect to the Mission for Integrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH) scheme? 1. It is a Central  Sector Scheme introduced in 2015. 2. It provides financial assistance @35% of the project cost in general areas for setting up post harvest management infrastructure. 3. It provides technical advice and administrative support to state governments/state horticulture missions for the saffron mission.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Both 2 &amp; 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 2"},{"label":"D","text":"Both 1 &amp; 3"},{"label":"E","text":"All 1, 2 &amp; 3"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":919,"text":"The term of State Legislative Assemblies of which of the following states will not end till Jan 2024?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"C","text":"Haryana"},{"label":"D","text":"Chhattisgarh"},{"label":"E","text":"Telangana"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":920,"text":"Which additional Nobel Prize was introduced in 1968 by the Central Bank of Sweden (Sveriges Riksbank ) to commemorate its 300th anniversary?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nobel Prize in Peace"},{"label":"B","text":"Nobel Prize in Literature"},{"label":"C","text":"Nobel Prize in Economic Sciences"},{"label":"D","text":"Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine"},{"label":"E","text":"Nobel Prize in Chemistry"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":921,"text":"When was BIMSTEC formed?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1991"},{"label":"B","text":"1995"},{"label":"C","text":"1997"},{"label":"D","text":"2001"},{"label":"E","text":"2004"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":922,"text":"As per the recent RBI guidelines revising the prudential norms for Urban Cooperative Banks (UCBs), match the following tiers of UCBs with their corresponding maximum individual housing loan limits per dwelling unit: List I (Tier of UCBs)  List II (Loan Limit) 1. Tier –I UCBs  A. ₹1.40 crore 2. Tier –II UCBs  B. ₹2 crore 3. Tier –III UCBs  C. ₹3 crore 4. Tier –IV UCBs  D. ₹60 lakh Select the correct code:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1–D, 2–A, 3–B, 4–C"},{"label":"B","text":"1–A, 2–B, 3–C, 4–D"},{"label":"C","text":"1–C, 2–D, 3–A, 4–B"},{"label":"D","text":"1–B, 2–C, 3–D, 4–A"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":923,"text":"The Union Cabinet chaired by the Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi, approved the constitution and empowerment of an Inter Ministerial Committee (IMC) for facilitation of the “World’s Largest Grain Storage Plan in Cooperative Sector” by convergence of various schemes of ministries. Which ministry does not belong to that group?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare"},{"label":"B","text":"Ministry of Cooperation"},{"label":"C","text":"Ministry of Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution"},{"label":"D","text":"Ministry of Food Processing Industries"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":925,"text":"Identify which among the following festivals is celebrated by the Apatani, or Tanw, also known by Apa, the tribal group living in the Ziro valley in the Lower Subansiri district of Arunachal Pradesh in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Myoko"},{"label":"B","text":"Gauchar Mela"},{"label":"C","text":"Thisam Phanit"},{"label":"D","text":"Tsukhenyie"},{"label":"E","text":"None of these"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":926,"text":"Which one of the following statements is/are correct regarding the PM KUSUM Scheme? 1. It seeks to increase the farmers’ income 2. The scheme comprises 3 - components. 3. It works towards decreasing environmental pollution.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Both 2 &amp; 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 3"},{"label":"D","text":"Both 1 &amp; 2"},{"label":"E","text":"All 1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":927,"text":"Infosys signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with which global financial technology company to enhance cross -border payment solutions for financial institutions?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Visa"},{"label":"B","text":"PayPal"},{"label":"C","text":"Mastercard"},{"label":"D","text":"American Express"},{"label":"E","text":"Ripple Labs"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":929,"text":"India has recently become the only country to adopt the T+1 settlement system after ________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"China"},{"label":"B","text":"Russia"},{"label":"C","text":"United States of America"},{"label":"D","text":"Germany"},{"label":"E","text":"Canada"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":930,"text":"The headquarters of the Geological Survey of India (GSI), which celebrated its 175th Foundation Day in 2025, is located in which Indian city?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"New Delhi"},{"label":"B","text":"Hyderabad"},{"label":"C","text":"Kolkata"},{"label":"D","text":"Bengaluru"},{"label":"E","text":"Pune"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":931,"text":"The Singareni  Collieries Company Limited (SCCL) is a Government coal mining company jointly owned by the  Government of ________ and Government of India  on a 51:49 equity basis.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Andhra Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Karnataka"},{"label":"C","text":"Odisha"},{"label":"D","text":"Telangana"},{"label":"E","text":"Maharashtra"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":932,"text":"What was the theme of World Population Day 2025, observed annually on July 11?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"“Ensuring Reproductive Rights and Choices for All”"},{"label":"B","text":"“Empowering young people to create the families they want in a fair and hopeful world”"},{"label":"C","text":"“Building a Sustainable Future through Family Planning”"},{"label":"D","text":"“Investing in Women for a Resilient Future”"},{"label":"E","text":"“Population and Development: Balancing People and Planet”"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":933,"text":"What is the current Marginal Standing Facility Rate, in the month of February 2021?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"4.75%"},{"label":"B","text":"3.50%"},{"label":"C","text":"3.25%"},{"label":"D","text":"4.50%"},{"label":"E","text":"4.25%"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":934,"text":"Spanish tennis sensation Carlos Alcaraz has not won which of the following grand slams?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"US Open"},{"label":"B","text":"Wimbledon"},{"label":"C","text":"French Open"},{"label":"D","text":"Australian Open"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":935,"text":"CRA is an agency registered under Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority (PFRDA) to perform functions of record -keeping, accounting, administration, and customer service to Pension scheme subscribers. What does “R” stand for in CRA?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Registry"},{"label":"B","text":"Record Keeping"},{"label":"C","text":"Resolution"},{"label":"D","text":"Real -Time"},{"label":"E","text":"Regulation"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":936,"text":"Identify which among the following statements are correct with respect to National Apprenticeship Training Scheme. 1. It was introduced in 2016. 2. It has been extended till 2026. 3. It comes under Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship. 4. It provides Rs 9000 per month allowance to graduates and diploma holders in engineering, science and business.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 1, 2 and 4"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 2, 3 and 4"},{"label":"D","text":"Only 1, 3 and 4"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":937,"text":"Name the country that conferred its highest civilian honour to President Droupadi Murmu - The Grand Order of the Chain of Yellow Star?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sudan"},{"label":"B","text":"South Africa"},{"label":"C","text":"Uganda"},{"label":"D","text":"Suriname"},{"label":"E","text":"Serbia"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":938,"text":"The RBI has published the Annual Report “Ombudsman Schemes of the Reserve Bank for the year 2019 -20”, in the month of February 2021. The Banking Ombudsman Scheme (BOS) was first notified by the Reserve Bank in the year _____ under Section 35A of the Banking Regulation Act, 1949.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1948"},{"label":"B","text":"2005"},{"label":"C","text":"2010"},{"label":"D","text":"1995"},{"label":"E","text":"2000"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":939,"text":"The Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA) has tightened the rules for Nidhi Companies, according to which company needs to have atleast 200 members and should have a net owned fund (NOF) of Rs _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"15 lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"18 lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"20 lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"25 lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"30 lakh"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":940,"text":"To boost participation of small investors in the securities market, Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) has increased the threshold for the basic service demat account to __________ from the current Rs 2 lakh.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 25 lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 20 lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 15 lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 10 lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 5 lakh"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":941,"text":"In the month of February 2021, Seychelles has become the first country to welcome the tourists that have been vaccinated against COVID -19. Seychelles is located in the Indian Ocean, nearest to which of the following countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"label":"B","text":"Maldives"},{"label":"C","text":"Malaysia"},{"label":"D","text":"Madagascar"},{"label":"E","text":"South Africa"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":942,"text":"What is the asset size for the NBFC -NDs to appoint an internal  ombudsman as per the RBI Internal Ombudsman Scheme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 5,000 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 4,000 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 3,000 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 2,000 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 1,000 crore"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":943,"text":"In recent news, in the month of October 2020, World Economic Forum (WEF) has declared to set up India’s first Advanced Manufacturing HUB or AMHUB in w hich of the foll owing states?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Tamil Nadu"},{"label":"B","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"C","text":"Chhattisgarh"},{"label":"D","text":"Odisha"},{"label":"E","text":"Jharkhand"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":944,"text":"As per Union Budget, the Mudra loan limit will be enhanced to _______ from the current Rs. 10 lakhs for those who have availed and successfully repaid loans previously taken under the Tarun category.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 15 lakhs"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 25 lakhs"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 30 lakhs"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 20 lakhs"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs. 35 lakhs"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":945,"text":"Denmark has decided to build the world’s first artificial island with the aim to provide clean energy. The island will be located in the North Sea (located between England and Scotland). Power will be generated from which of the following energies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Solar"},{"label":"B","text":"Tidal"},{"label":"C","text":"Wind"},{"label":"D","text":"Geothermal"},{"label":"E","text":"Biomass"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":946,"text":"In recent news, a declaration has been adopted that aims to boost industry ties on defense and renewable energy, in the face of growing competition from the other emerging countries . The  above -mentioned Atlantic Declaration was  signed between which of the following two  countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United States and United Kingdom"},{"label":"B","text":"Australia &amp; United Kingdom"},{"label":"C","text":"France and United States"},{"label":"D","text":"Australia and United Kingdom"},{"label":"E","text":"Australia and France"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":947,"text":"The Presidencies of the 2023, 2024, and 2025 UN Climate Change Conferences have formed the COP Presidencies Troika and introduced the ‘Roadmap to Mission 1.5°C,’ to “significantly enhance international cooperation and the international enabling environm ent to stimulate ambition in the next round of nationally determined contributions. Identify which among the following countries are a part of this troika?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"France, Azerbaijan, and Germany"},{"label":"B","text":"United Arab Emirates (UAE), Azerbaijan, and Brazil"},{"label":"C","text":"United State of America (USA), Azerbaijan, and Brazil"},{"label":"D","text":"United Arab Emirates (UAE), India, and Brazil"},{"label":"E","text":"United Arab Emirates (UAE), Indonesia, and Brazil"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":948,"text":"In recent news, in the month February 2020, which of the following companies has declared plans to launch  online engineering courses that will focus on three areas — employability assessment and recruitment, reinforced learning, reskilling and vocational skills training?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Larson &amp; Toubro"},{"label":"B","text":"Bharti Airtel"},{"label":"C","text":"Reliance"},{"label":"D","text":"Infosys"},{"label":"E","text":"Wipro"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":949,"text":"Identify which among the following is part of the Memorandum of Company Act? 1. The objective of the Company 2. State in which the company is located 3. This clause states the liability of the members of the company. The Liability can be limited or unlimited 4. The name of the company should be stated in this clause.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"1, 2 and 4"},{"label":"C","text":"2, 3 and 4"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 3 and 4"},{"label":"E","text":"1, 2, 3 and 4"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":950,"text":"__________ is the art and science of making maps and charts.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Demography"},{"label":"B","text":"Calligraphy"},{"label":"C","text":"Cartography"},{"label":"D","text":"Orthography"},{"label":"E","text":"Cacography"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":951,"text":"How many days did Aditya -L1 spacecraft  take  to complete its first halo orbit around the Sun -Earth L1 point after its launch on September 2, 2023 ?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"158 days"},{"label":"B","text":"168 days"},{"label":"C","text":"188 days"},{"label":"D","text":"178 days"},{"label":"E","text":"208 days"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":952,"text":"The startups that have the potential to enter the unicorn club soon are also called “___________”. These startups are often backed by angel investors or financial speculators based on future projections or apparent valuations.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lovecorn"},{"label":"B","text":"Billioncorn"},{"label":"C","text":"Soonicorns"},{"label":"D","text":"Decacorn"},{"label":"E","text":"Rushcorn"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":953,"text":"City of Guadalajara has been named World Book Capital for the year 2022. It belongs to which country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Taiwan"},{"label":"B","text":"Mexico"},{"label":"C","text":"Brazil"},{"label":"D","text":"Morocco"},{"label":"E","text":"Indonesia"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":954,"text":"Good Governance Day in India is observed on December 25th. This day is observed to commemorate the birth anniversary of which of the following Indian personalities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sardar Vallabh Bhai Patel"},{"label":"B","text":"Atal Bihari Vajpayee"},{"label":"C","text":"Swami Vivekananda"},{"label":"D","text":"Madan Mohan Malviya"},{"label":"E","text":"Pt. Deen Dayal Upadhyaya"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":955,"text":"Despite prolonged geopolitical tensions and slowing global trade, India’s merchandise exports touched US$ 450.4 billion during 2022 - 23, which is 6.7 percent above the previous year’s record level. Which  of the following sectors contributed the largest share in the merchandise exports from India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Electronic Goods"},{"label":"B","text":"Petroleum Products"},{"label":"C","text":"Rice"},{"label":"D","text":"Organic and Inorganic Chemicals"},{"label":"E","text":"Iron Ore"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":956,"text":"In recent news, in the month of December 2020, Government of India has declared to set up a Multi -Modal Logistics Hub &amp; Multi -Modal Transport Hub (MMTH), with the aim of making India a strong part of the Global  Value Chain. In which of the following  states will it be set up?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Uttar Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"C","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"E","text":"Tamil Nadu"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":958,"text":"The Reserve Bank of India has recently (November 2023) decided to directly regulate all entities facilitating cross -border payment transactions for the import and export of goods and services. In respect of import and export transactions processed by PA-CBs, the maximum value per unit of goods / services sold / purchased shall be __________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹5,00,000"},{"label":"B","text":"₹10,00,000"},{"label":"C","text":"₹15,00,000"},{"label":"D","text":"₹20,00,000"},{"label":"E","text":"₹25,00,000"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":959,"text":"To standardize the opening price discovery/ equilibrium price across exchanges during special pre -open session for initial public offer (IPO) for the SME platform, the National Stock Exchange (NSE) has decided to put an overall capping up to ______ ov er the Issue price for SME IPOs.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"50%"},{"label":"B","text":"60%"},{"label":"C","text":"75%"},{"label":"D","text":"90%"},{"label":"E","text":"25%"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":961,"text":"__________ Trade Receivables Discounting System (TReDS) platform has achieved a significant milestone, facilitating financing of over 50 lac invoices worth ₹1,00,000 crore since its inception providing accessible working capital financing solutions to  Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) in India.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Receivables Employment Exchange of India Limited"},{"label":"B","text":"Remittance Exchange of India Limited"},{"label":"C","text":"Exchange Rate of India Limited"},{"label":"D","text":"Receivables Exchange of India Limited"},{"label":"E","text":"Revenue Exchange of India Limited"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":962,"text":"Cyclone Asani, which developed over southeast regions of Bay of Bengal and intensified into a &#39;severe cyclone&#39; was named by _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bangladesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Myanmar"},{"label":"C","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"label":"D","text":"Thailand"},{"label":"E","text":"Indonesia"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":963,"text":"In recent news, a declaration has been adopted that aims to boost industry ties on defense and renewable energy, in the face of growing competition from the other emerging countries . The  above -mentioned Atlantic Declaration was  signed between which of the following two  countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United States and United Kingdom"},{"label":"B","text":"Australia &amp; United Kingdom"},{"label":"C","text":"France and United States"},{"label":"D","text":"Australia and United Kingdom"},{"label":"E","text":"Australia and France"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":964,"text":"In Feb 2021, Ngozi Okonjo -Iweala was appointed as the seventh Director -General of the World Trade Organization, becoming the first woman head of the body. She belongs to which of the following countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ethiopia"},{"label":"B","text":"Nigeria"},{"label":"C","text":"Kenya"},{"label":"D","text":"Eritrea"},{"label":"E","text":"Algeria"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":965,"text":"The Government of India through Indian Strategic Petroleum Reserve Ltd. (ISPRL) under Phase -1 has set up Strategic Petroleum Reserves (SPR) at three locations namely Visakhapatnam, Mangalore and ________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Varanasi"},{"label":"B","text":"Padur"},{"label":"C","text":"Raipur"},{"label":"D","text":"Kolkata"},{"label":"E","text":"Ranchi"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":966,"text":"To boost participation of small investors in the securities market, Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) has increased the threshold for the basic service demat account to __________ from the current Rs 2 lakh.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 25 lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 20 lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 15 lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 10 lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 5 lakh"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":969,"text":"India&#39;s overall exports (Merchandise and Services combined) in April 2023 is estimated to be USD 65.02 Billion, exhibiting a positive growth of 2 percent over April 2022.  Which one of the following  key sectors under merchandise exports exhibited the highest positive growth in April 2023 as compared to the same period last year (April 2022)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Oil Meals"},{"label":"B","text":"Electronic Goods"},{"label":"C","text":"Ceramic Products &amp; Glassware"},{"label":"D","text":"Drugs &amp; Pharmaceuticals"},{"label":"E","text":"Cereal Preparations &amp; Miscellaneous Processed Items"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":970,"text":"As per Annual Report of RBI, Commercial banks remained the largest holders of government securities  [including T -Bills and state government securities (SGSs)] accounting for __________ at end -March 2023.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"27.5%"},{"label":"B","text":"37.5%"},{"label":"C","text":"25.5%"},{"label":"D","text":"31.5%"},{"label":"E","text":"28.5%"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":972,"text":"Since 2004 -05, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) has suspended the issuance of new licences for which category of banks as part of its sector -consolidation measures?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Regional Rural Banks (RRBs)"},{"label":"B","text":"Urban Co -operative Banks (UCBs)"},{"label":"C","text":"Local Area Banks (LABs)"},{"label":"D","text":"Private Sector Banks (PSBs)"},{"label":"E","text":"Small Finance Banks (SFBs)"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":973,"text":"In several countries across the world, the administrative, legislative, and judicial functions are distributed among different capital cities instead of being concentrated in a single city. With reference to this, consider the following countries and identify which among them have more than one capital city officially designated for different branches of governance: 1. South Africa 2. Singapore 3. Bolivia Select the correct combination using the code given below:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"1 only"},{"label":"C","text":"3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":974,"text":"E -way bill is a document required to be carried by a person in charge of the conveyance carrying any consignment of goods of value exceeding ______ as mandated by the Government in terms of section 68 of the Goods and Services Tax Act read with rule 1 38 of the rules framed thereunder.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 50,000"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 40,000"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 65,000"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 1,00,000"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 75,000"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":976,"text":"How many member countries are there in the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"36"},{"label":"B","text":"37"},{"label":"C","text":"38"},{"label":"D","text":"39"},{"label":"E","text":"40"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":977,"text":"Kasturba Gandhi Balika Vidyalaya is a scheme introduced by the Government of India for  the school girls of SC, ST, OBC and minority communities , from the classes of __________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1st to 5th"},{"label":"B","text":"6th to 10th"},{"label":"C","text":"6th to 12th"},{"label":"D","text":"11th &amp; 12th"},{"label":"E","text":"9th to 12th"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":978,"text":"Consider the following statements regarding the features of Senior Citizen Saving Scheme (SCSS) and identify the correct answer out of the options given below :","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Deposits in SCSS qualify for deduction u/s 80C of Income Tax Act."},{"label":"B","text":"A retired personnel of Defence Services ( excluding civilian defence employees), who has"},{"label":"C","text":"A depositor May open an account individually or jointly with a spouse ."},{"label":"D","text":"Both A &amp; B"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":980,"text":"Shri Piyush Goyal is a senior leader in the Union Cabinet who has been entrusted with several important economic and infrastructural portfolios over the years. With reference to his current responsibilities in the Union Government, consider the following ministries: 1. Ministry of Railways 2. Ministry of Commerce and Industry 3. Ministry of Coal Which of the above ministries has ever been served by Piyush Goyal?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 only"},{"label":"B","text":"2 only"},{"label":"C","text":"3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1 and 2"},{"label":"E","text":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":981,"text":"The World Forestry Congress (WFC) is held every six years since 1926 under the auspices of the _______, in association with the government of the host country.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO)"},{"label":"B","text":"United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP)"},{"label":"C","text":"Conservation International"},{"label":"D","text":"Worldwide fund for Nature (WWF)"},{"label":"E","text":"Greenpeace"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":982,"text":"Progress has been sluggish in six sectors under Production -Linked Incentive (PLI) schemes. A detailed analysis is being conducted by relevant ministries. Which of these is not under the non -performing sectors of the scheme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Information technology (IT) hardware"},{"label":"B","text":"White Goods"},{"label":"C","text":"ACC Battery"},{"label":"D","text":"Textile"},{"label":"E","text":"Speciality Steel"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":983,"text":"What is the theme of World Water Day 2022?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nature for Water"},{"label":"B","text":"Leaving No One Behind"},{"label":"C","text":"Water and Climate Change"},{"label":"D","text":"Valuing Water"},{"label":"E","text":"Groundwater: making the invisible visible"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":985,"text":"In recent news, in the month of December 2020, Government of India has declared to set up a Multi -Modal Logistics Hub &amp; Multi -Modal Transport Hub (MMTH), with the aim of making India a strong part of the Global  Value Chain. In which of the following  states will it be set up?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Uttar Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Gujarat"},{"label":"C","text":"Madhya Pradesh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"E","text":"Tamil Nadu"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":986,"text":"Centre has recently (April 2022) introduced &quot;Azadi Se Antyodaya Tak campaign&quot;, which is a _____ day campaign,  with a mission to saturate 75 districts.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"75"},{"label":"B","text":"90"},{"label":"C","text":"120"},{"label":"D","text":"130"},{"label":"E","text":"150"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":988,"text":"_______ has recently expanded its strategic partnership with SBI Cards and Payments Services Ltd to power the company&#39;s next leg of digital transformation.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Infosys Ltd"},{"label":"B","text":"Wipro Ltd"},{"label":"C","text":"Tata Consultancy Services (TCS)"},{"label":"D","text":"HCL Technologies"},{"label":"E","text":"Tech Mahindra"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":989,"text":"Identify which among the following was/were the top three count ry/countries in the 2024 International Mathematical Olympiad (IMO)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United States"},{"label":"B","text":"China"},{"label":"C","text":"South Korea"},{"label":"D","text":"All the above"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":990,"text":"Identify which among the following taxes have been subsumed under GST in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Central Sales Tax"},{"label":"B","text":"Central Excise Duty"},{"label":"C","text":"Service Tax"},{"label":"D","text":"OCTROI"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":991,"text":"The Centre has revised the threshold for GST e -invoicing, and has declared that it will be mandatory for all businesses with annual turnover of over _____to move to e - invoicing for business to business transactions under goods and services tax (GST) from _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 2 crore, Rs 10 Crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 3.5 crore, Rs 10 Crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 5 crore, Rs 10 Crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 10 crore, Rs 20 Crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 15 crore, Rs 20 Crore"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":992,"text":"In recent news, in the month of February 2021, ____ INS Karanj - a Scorpene class submarine has been handed over to the Indian  Navy by Mazagon Dock Limited.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"First"},{"label":"B","text":"Sixth"},{"label":"C","text":"Third"},{"label":"D","text":"Fourth"},{"label":"E","text":"Fifth"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":993,"text":"India&#39;s First Fire Park has been opened in which of the following states in the month of January 2021?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Assam"},{"label":"B","text":"Haryana"},{"label":"C","text":"Karnataka"},{"label":"D","text":"Odisha"},{"label":"E","text":"Kerala"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":994,"text":"As per Annual Report of RBI, Commercial banks remained the largest holders of government securities  [including T -Bills and state government securities (SGSs)] accounting for __________ at end -March 2023.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"27.5%"},{"label":"B","text":"37.5%"},{"label":"C","text":"25.5%"},{"label":"D","text":"31.5%"},{"label":"E","text":"28.5%"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":995,"text":"Identify which among the following statements is true regarding Call Money, Notice Money and Term Money?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Scheduled commercial banks (including Small Finance Banks) cannot set their own limits"},{"label":"B","text":"Scheduled commercial banks (excluding Small Finance Banks) can set their own limits for"},{"label":"C","text":"Scheduled commercial banks (excluding Small Finance Banks) can set their own limits for"},{"label":"D","text":"Scheduled commercial banks (including Small Finance Banks) can set their own limits for"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":996,"text":"NASA&#39;s MAVEN mission has published some new, mind -blowing images captivating an array of ultraviolet views of the red planet. What does &quot;V&quot; stand for in MAVEN Mission?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Velocity"},{"label":"B","text":"Vacuum"},{"label":"C","text":"Volatile"},{"label":"D","text":"Valence"},{"label":"E","text":"Vector"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":997,"text":"Where is the headquarters of the International Olympic Committee located?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Italy"},{"label":"B","text":"Switzerland"},{"label":"C","text":"Belgium"},{"label":"D","text":"France"},{"label":"E","text":"UK"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":998,"text":"With reference to the findings of the Global Innovation Index (GII) 2025: Innovation at a Crossroads, consider the following statements regarding India&#39;s performance: 1. India&#39;s Input Rank in the Global Innovation Index 2025 is 44. 2. India&#39;s Output Rank in the same index is 32. 3. India ranks at par with its development level.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 only"},{"label":"B","text":"1 and 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"2 only"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1000,"text":"In the Union Budget 2024 -25, the TReDS onboarding turnover threshold has been reduced from Rs 500 Crore to ____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 450 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 400 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 350 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 300 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 250 crore"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1002,"text":"As per the Constitution of India, what happens when the office of the Vice President of India becomes vacant due to resignation or any other reason?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The President nominates an interim Vice President until elections are held."},{"label":"B","text":"The Prime Minister temporarily assumes the duties of the Vice President."},{"label":"C","text":"The Deputy Chairman of the Rajya Sabha presides over the Upper House until a new Vice"},{"label":"D","text":"The Chief Justice of India acts as the Vice President until Parliament meets."},{"label":"E","text":"The Election Commission directly appoints a new Vice President."}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1004,"text":"UNDP has notified 17 Sustainable Goals (SDGs) to be attained by the year 2030. SDG 5 is related to which of the following?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"No Poverty"},{"label":"B","text":"Zero Hunger"},{"label":"C","text":"Quality Education"},{"label":"D","text":"Gender Equality"},{"label":"E","text":"Clean Water and Sanitation"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1005,"text":"Indian Finance Minister Arun Jaitley introduced a GIS -based Mobile App for financial inclusion in the year 2018 during Annual Public Sector Banks meeting. This App assists  the common people in finding a financial service touch point at any location in the country. What is the name of this mobile app?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"CSC"},{"label":"B","text":"UMANG"},{"label":"C","text":"BHIM"},{"label":"D","text":"Jan Dhan Darshak"},{"label":"E","text":"Aaykar Setu"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1006,"text":"In the month of February 2021, West Indies has recently defeated Bangladesh in a test match after chasing a target of 395 runs. This was ______ highest run chase in the history of test matches.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1st"},{"label":"B","text":"2nd"},{"label":"C","text":"5th"},{"label":"D","text":"4th"},{"label":"E","text":"6th"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1007,"text":"Identify which among the following statements is incorrect regarding Sovereign Gold Bonds?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Investment limit per fiscal year is 4 kg for individuals and Hindu Undivided Family (HUF)"},{"label":"B","text":"Investment limit per fiscal year is 20 Kg for Trusts and similar entities notified by the"},{"label":"C","text":"Bond is available both in demat and paper form"},{"label":"D","text":"Total limit is excluding purchase from secondary market"},{"label":"E","text":"Bond can be used as collateral for loans"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1008,"text":"The Government of India&#39;s S3WAAS platform, developed by the National Informatics Centre (NIC), enables the creation of secure and accessible websites for district administrations across the country. With reference to this initiative, which of the following words does NOT represent the letter &#39;S&#39; in S3WAAS?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Smart"},{"label":"B","text":"Scalable"},{"label":"C","text":"Sugamya"},{"label":"D","text":"Secure"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1009,"text":"Piyush Gupta, the Indian origin Chief Executive of Singapore&#39;s largest bank ___________, will step down in March 2025. He will be succeeded by Tan Su Shan, who was appointed as deputy CEO.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"DBS Bank"},{"label":"B","text":"OCBC Bank"},{"label":"C","text":"United Overseas Bank"},{"label":"D","text":"Bank of Singapore"},{"label":"E","text":"Trust Bank"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1011,"text":"Identify which among the following ministries was the top achiever in achieving the targets of the National  Monetization Pipeline?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ministry of Commerce"},{"label":"B","text":"Ministry of Defence"},{"label":"C","text":"Ministry of Road Transport and Highways"},{"label":"D","text":"Ministry of Home Affairs"},{"label":"E","text":"Ministry of Finance"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1012,"text":"Identify which among the following statements regarding the features of a BSBDA (Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account) under Reserve Bank of India guidelines is correct?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The account holder is required to maintain a minimum balance of 1,000 every month."},{"label":"B","text":"The account holder is eligible to open multiple BSBDA accounts in the same bank"},{"label":"C","text":"The account can be opened by any individual -there are no age or income criteria set for"},{"label":"D","text":"A BSBDA account permits unlimited free withdrawals from ATMs every month."},{"label":"E","text":"A BSBDA -Small Account variant allows total credits of up to 5 lakh in a year."}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1013,"text":"Denmark has decided to build the world&#39;s first artificial island with the aim to provide clean energy. The island will be located in the North Sea (located between England and Scotland). Power will be generated from which of the following energies?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Solar"},{"label":"B","text":"Tidal"},{"label":"C","text":"Wind"},{"label":"D","text":"Geothermal"},{"label":"E","text":"Biomass"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1015,"text":"The maximum limit of Retirement gratuity and death gratuity shall be increased to _______ from existing Rs 20 Lakh on account of revision of Dearness Allowance payable to Central Government Employees.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 21 Lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 22 Lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 23 Lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 24 Lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs. 25 Lakh"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1016,"text":"As part of India&#39;s effort to promote cooperative federalism and evidence -based policymaking, the NITI Aayog was established by replacing the Planning Commission in which year?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2014"},{"label":"B","text":"2015"},{"label":"C","text":"2016"},{"label":"D","text":"2017"},{"label":"E","text":"2018"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1017,"text":"As per Union Budget 2022 -23, how much amount of Fund has been allocated for Jal Jeevan Mission?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 40,000 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 50,000 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 35,000 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 60,000 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs. 68,000 crore"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1018,"text":"Identify the bank that has introduced &quot;Gram Sampark Abhiyan&quot;, a nation -wide Financial Inclusion and Literacy Campaign on the occasion of the 151st birth anniversary of Mahatma Gandhi, in the year 2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"SBI"},{"label":"B","text":"PNB"},{"label":"C","text":"HDFC"},{"label":"D","text":"BoI"},{"label":"E","text":"BoB"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1019,"text":"In which of the following sports did India not participate in the recently held Paris Olympics?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Javelin Throw"},{"label":"B","text":"Hockey"},{"label":"C","text":"Rowing"},{"label":"D","text":"Table Tennis"},{"label":"E","text":"Fencing"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1021,"text":"Who serves as the Ex -officio President of the Council of Scientific &amp; Industrial Research (CSIR), India&#39;s premier national R&amp;D organization established in 1942?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Union Minister of Science and Technology"},{"label":"B","text":"Cabinet Secretary of India"},{"label":"C","text":"Prime Minister of India"},{"label":"D","text":"Finance Secretary (Expenditure)"},{"label":"E","text":"Director -General of CSIR"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1023,"text":"The Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO) plays a vital role in advancing India&#39;s space technology and promoting the peaceful use of outer space. Consider the following statements about ISRO: 1. Dr. Vikram Sarabhai was the first Chairman of ISRO. 2. ISRO was established in the year 1957 under the Department of Space. 3. The headquarters of ISRO is located in Chennai, Tamil Nadu. Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 only"},{"label":"B","text":"1 and 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"2 only"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1027,"text":"Four of the following mountain peaks belong to the same country. Which one does not belong to that category?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Anamudi"},{"label":"B","text":"Mount Everest"},{"label":"C","text":"Mount Kamet"},{"label":"D","text":"Kanchenjunga"},{"label":"E","text":"Nanda Devi"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1028,"text":"The Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC) was enacted in India in which year?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2014"},{"label":"B","text":"2015"},{"label":"C","text":"2016"},{"label":"D","text":"2018"}],"answer":2,"solution":"The Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC) was enacted in India in 2016 to consolidate and amend the laws relating to reorganization of insolvency resolution of corporate, individuals and partnership firms in a time bound manner."},{"id":1029,"text":"Identify which among the following statements is not correct with respect to IFSCA? 1. It was established in 2010, under International Financial Services Centres Authority Act, 2009. 2. It serves as a unified authority for the development and regulation of financial products, services and institutions in the International Financial Services Centre (IFSC) in India. 3. International Financial Services Centres Authority (IFSCA) has established an expert committee to position GIFTIFSC as a global trading hub.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both 1 &amp; 2"},{"label":"B","text":"Both 2 &amp; 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Both 1 &amp; 3"},{"label":"D","text":"Only 2"},{"label":"E","text":"Only 1"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1030,"text":"ATMs that are owned and operated by non -bank entities are called as _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Blue Label ATMs"},{"label":"B","text":"White Label ATMs"},{"label":"C","text":"Brown Label ATMs"},{"label":"D","text":"Black Label ATMs"},{"label":"E","text":"Red Label ATMs"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1031,"text":"Minimum credit rating required for NBFCs is:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"BB+"},{"label":"B","text":"Aaa"},{"label":"C","text":"BBB -"},{"label":"D","text":"AA+"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1032,"text":"The Presidencies of the 2023, 2024, and 2025 UN Climate Change Conferences have formed the COP Presidencies Troika and introduced the &#39;Roadmap to Mission 1.5 degrees C,&#39; to &quot;significantly enhance international cooperation and the international enabling environm ent to stimulate ambition in the next round of nationally determined contributions. Identify which among the following countries are a part of this troika?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"France, Azerbaijan, and Germany"},{"label":"B","text":"United Arab Emirates (UAE), Azerbaijan, and Brazil"},{"label":"C","text":"United State of America (USA), Azerbaijan, and Brazil"},{"label":"D","text":"United Arab Emirates (UAE), India, and Brazil"},{"label":"E","text":"United Arab Emirates (UAE), Indonesia, and Brazil"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1033,"text":"Identify which among the following banks are members of the Partnership for Carbon Accounting Financials (PCAF)? 1. Union Bank of India (UBI) 2. Indian Overseas Bank (IOB) 3. Punjab National Bank (PNB) 4. IDFC FIRST Bank Select the correct answer using the code given below:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 2 only"},{"label":"B","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 4 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 4"},{"label":"E","text":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1034,"text":"Financial Stability Board represents which of the following organization?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"SCO"},{"label":"B","text":"G-7"},{"label":"C","text":"G-20"},{"label":"D","text":"ASEAN"},{"label":"E","text":"BIMSTEC"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1035,"text":"For the first time in India, the share price of a company crossed the Rs 1 lakh mark. With this, __________ became the first stock in India to cross the Rs 1 lakh mark per share in intra -day trade after its share jumped  1.07 per cent in early trade recently in June 2023.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Honeywell"},{"label":"B","text":"MRF Ltd."},{"label":"C","text":"Page Industries"},{"label":"D","text":"3M India"},{"label":"E","text":"Shree Cement"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1036,"text":"In recent news, a declaration has been adopted that aims to boost industry ties on defense and renewable energy, in the face of growing competition from the other emerging countries . The  above -mentioned Atlantic Declaration was  signed between which of the following two  countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United States and United Kingdom"},{"label":"B","text":"Australia &amp; United Kingdom"},{"label":"C","text":"France and United States"},{"label":"D","text":"Australia and United Kingdom"},{"label":"E","text":"Australia and France"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1037,"text":"The Image (Nano Banana), recently introduced as an advanced image editing AI model, has been based on which model?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bloom"},{"label":"B","text":"Llama 3.1"},{"label":"C","text":"Gemini 2.5 Flash"},{"label":"D","text":"Claude 3.7 Sonnet"},{"label":"E","text":"Grok"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1038,"text":"When was BIMSTEC formed?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1991"},{"label":"B","text":"1995"},{"label":"C","text":"1997"},{"label":"D","text":"2001"},{"label":"E","text":"2004"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1039,"text":"With reference to important international declarations and organizations completing milestone years in 2025, consider the following statements: 1. The Beijing Declaration and Platform for Action completes 30 years in 2025. 2. The Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) celebrates its 80th anniversary in 2025. 3. The UN Security Council Resolution 1325 on Women, Peace and Security completes 25 years in 2025. Which of the statements given above is/are correct?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 2"},{"label":"D","text":"2 only"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1040,"text":"Good Governance Day in India is observed on December 25th. This day is observed to commemorate the birth anniversary of which of the following Indian personalities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sardar Vallabh Bhai Patel"},{"label":"B","text":"Atal Bihari Vajpayee"},{"label":"C","text":"Swami Vivekananda"},{"label":"D","text":"Madan Mohan Malviya"},{"label":"E","text":"Pt. Deen Dayal Upadhyaya"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1042,"text":"What is the objective of the &quot;Antardrishti  Dashboard&quot; which was introduced recently by the RBI ?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It will provide the required insight to assess and monitor the progress of grievance"},{"label":"B","text":"It will provide the required insight to assess and monitor the progress of financial"},{"label":"C","text":"It will provide the required insight to assess and monitor the progress of reducing NPAs."},{"label":"D","text":"It will provide the required insight to assess and monitor the progress of strengthening"},{"label":"E","text":"It will provide the required insight to assess and monitor the progress of digital banking."}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1043,"text":"The Union budget for the year 2021 -22 has allocated 1.1 trillion for the Indian Railways, out of this amount how much will  be utilized for capital expenditure for 2021 -22 to expand rail infrastructure in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1.07 trillion"},{"label":"B","text":"1.02 trillion"},{"label":"C","text":"0.95 trillion"},{"label":"D","text":"1.04 trillion"},{"label":"E","text":"1.09 trillion"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1044,"text":"Which of these metals was not used to make the commemorative &#39;75 Rupee Coin&#39; which was introduced during the inauguration of the new Parliament?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Silver"},{"label":"B","text":"Copper"},{"label":"C","text":"Nickel"},{"label":"D","text":"Gold"},{"label":"E","text":"Zinc"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1045,"text":"Who is the author of the novel &quot;The Loneliness of Sonia and Sunny,&quot; recently shortlisted for the Booker Prize?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Arundhati Roy"},{"label":"B","text":"Jhumpa Lahiri"},{"label":"C","text":"Kiran Desai"},{"label":"D","text":"Anita Desai"},{"label":"E","text":"Salman Rushdie"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1046,"text":"The Citizen&#39;s Charter of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) aims to enhance transparency, accountability, and efficiency in the delivery of public services to citizens. The Charter is currently being implemented in _____ departments of the RBI.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"15"},{"label":"B","text":"18"},{"label":"C","text":"11"},{"label":"D","text":"20"},{"label":"E","text":"23"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1047,"text":"Federal Reserves  System, also known as FED has recently got new chair of the Board of Governors for a term ending May 15, 2026. Federal Reserve was created in the year ____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1905"},{"label":"B","text":"1908"},{"label":"C","text":"1913"},{"label":"D","text":"1919"},{"label":"E","text":"1929"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1049,"text":"Match the following major rivers with the continents on which they flow: Rivers                Continents","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nile                    1. South America"},{"label":"B","text":"Amazon      2. North America"},{"label":"C","text":"Yangtze      3. Asia"},{"label":"D","text":"Mississippi    4. Africa"},{"label":"A","text":"A-4, B-1, C-3, D-2"},{"label":"B","text":"A-1, B-2, C-4, D-3"},{"label":"C","text":"A-2, B-4, C-3, D-1"},{"label":"D","text":"A-4, B-3, C-1, D-2"},{"label":"E","text":"A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1050,"text":"Which of these small saving schemes will provide highest return in July - September  2023?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Kisan Vikas Patra"},{"label":"B","text":"National Savings Certificate (NSC)"},{"label":"C","text":"Senior citizen savings Scheme"},{"label":"D","text":"Sukanya Samriddhi"},{"label":"E","text":"Monthly Income Scheme"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1051,"text":"Identify which among the following statements regarding the conditions under which a payment bank can be upgraded to a small finance bank is correct?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A payment bank can apply for conversion into an SFB immediately after it starts operations,"},{"label":"B","text":"Conversion is permitted only if the payment bank has a satisfactory track record of"},{"label":"C","text":"The payment bank must have already obtained scheduled bank status before applying for"},{"label":"D","text":"There is no minimum paid -up capital requirement for a payment bank to convert into an"},{"label":"E","text":"The payment bank must first convert to a universal bank before becoming an SFB."}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1052,"text":"Progress has been sluggish in six sectors under Production -Linked Incentive (PLI) schemes. A detailed analysis is being conducted by relevant ministries. Which of these is not under the non -performing sectors of the scheme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Information technology (IT) hardware"},{"label":"B","text":"White Goods"},{"label":"C","text":"ACC Battery"},{"label":"D","text":"Textile"},{"label":"E","text":"Speciality Steel"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1053,"text":"As per a recent RBI report, India&#39;s foreign exchange reserves are now sufficient to cover over ____ of projected imports.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"11 months"},{"label":"B","text":"10 months"},{"label":"C","text":"9 months"},{"label":"D","text":"8 months"},{"label":"E","text":"7 months"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1054,"text":"Name the country that conferred its highest civilian honour to President Droupadi Murmu - The Grand Order of the Chain of Yellow Star?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sudan"},{"label":"B","text":"South Africa"},{"label":"C","text":"Uganda"},{"label":"D","text":"Suriname"},{"label":"E","text":"Serbia"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1055,"text":"What is the full form of UNCED?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"United Nations Conference on Environment and Development"},{"label":"B","text":"United Nations Convention on Environment and Development"},{"label":"C","text":"United Nations Conference on Employment and Demographics"},{"label":"D","text":"United Nations Convention on Empowerment and Development"},{"label":"E","text":"United Nations Conference on Energy and Development"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1056,"text":"Which one of the following statements is/are incorrect with respect to the Beti Bachao Beti Padhao (BBBP) scheme?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The scheme was launched in 2015 under the Ministry of Women and Child Development"},{"label":"B","text":"The Pan India Expansion of the scheme covering all districts of the country was launched"},{"label":"C","text":"It aims to improve the Sex Ratio at Birth (SRB) by 2 points every year."},{"label":"D","text":"The scheme has been subsumed into Mission Shakti - Sambal sub -scheme from 2021 -"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1057,"text":"In recent news, Indian shooting icon Abhinav Bindra has been awarded the prestigious Olympic Order in recognition of his &quot;distinguished contribution&quot; to the Olympic movement. Bindra, became India&#39;s first -ever Olympic individual gold medallist in the ________  with his top finish in 10m air rifle event.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2008 Beijing Olympics"},{"label":"B","text":"2012 London Olympics"},{"label":"C","text":"2014 Sochi Olympics"},{"label":"D","text":"2016 Rio Olympics"},{"label":"E","text":"2010 Vancouver Olympics"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1058,"text":"India&#39;s first bamboo -based ethanol plant, also recognised  as the world&#39;s first green bamboo bioethanol plant, has been set up in which Indian state?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Arunachal Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Meghalaya"},{"label":"C","text":"Assam"},{"label":"D","text":"Tripura"},{"label":"E","text":"Manipur"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1059,"text":"As per the latest update, how many Maharatna Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs) are there in India after Hindustan Aeronautics Limited (HAL) was upgraded to Maharatna status?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"12"},{"label":"B","text":"13"},{"label":"C","text":"14"},{"label":"D","text":"15"},{"label":"E","text":"16"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1061,"text":"Presently, ______ Debt Recovery Tribunals and 5 Debts Recovery Appellate Tribunals are functioning across the country.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"33"},{"label":"B","text":"36"},{"label":"C","text":"39"},{"label":"D","text":"41"},{"label":"E","text":"47"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1062,"text":"The headquarters of the European Central Bank is located in ____and was established in ______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"London, 1998"},{"label":"B","text":"Brussels , 2002"},{"label":"C","text":"Paris, 2000"},{"label":"D","text":"Rome, 1998"},{"label":"E","text":"Frankfurt, 1998"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1063,"text":"Which fintech platform became one of the first non -banking entities to offer Central Bank Digital Currency (CBDC) e wallets in collaboration with the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) and Yes Bank?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Paytm"},{"label":"B","text":"PhonePe"},{"label":"C","text":"MobiKwik"},{"label":"D","text":"Razorpay"},{"label":"E","text":"Google Pay"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1064,"text":"Germany has recently committed to provide additional support worth Euro 10 billion to India by the year _______ to support green growth initiatives.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2026"},{"label":"B","text":"2027"},{"label":"C","text":"2028"},{"label":"D","text":"2029"},{"label":"E","text":"2030"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1065,"text":"In recent news, a drone attack was introduced on Israel and the group responsible for the attack was the Houthi group. The Houthi group belongs to which country?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pakistan"},{"label":"B","text":"Syria"},{"label":"C","text":"Iran"},{"label":"D","text":"Yemen"},{"label":"E","text":"Afghanistan"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1066,"text":"Identify which among the following organisations is responsible for conducting the All India Debt and Investment Survey (AIDIS)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"NITI Aayog"},{"label":"B","text":"Reserve Bank of India (RBI)"},{"label":"C","text":"National Statistics Office (NSO) under the Ministry of Statistics and Programme"},{"label":"D","text":"Ministry of Finance"},{"label":"E","text":"Indian Statistical Institute (ISI)"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1068,"text":"NASA&#39;s Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL) published a mosaic image captured by the Mars Odyssey&#39;s THEMIS instrument, showing Olympus Mons, the largest volcano in the solar system. Olympus Mons is located on which planet?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Venus"},{"label":"B","text":"Jupiter"},{"label":"C","text":"Saturn"},{"label":"D","text":"Mercury"},{"label":"E","text":"Mars"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1069,"text":"Identify which among the following States are among the top 3 States with highest mangrove cover in India? 1. West Bengal 2. Gujarat 3. Andaman Nicobar 4. Tamil Nadu","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1, 2 &amp; 3"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 2 &amp; 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 1 &amp; 4"},{"label":"D","text":"Only 3 &amp; 4"},{"label":"E","text":"2, 3 &amp; 4"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1070,"text":"Which of these country will host World Environment Day 2022 in June 2022?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Switzerland"},{"label":"B","text":"Sweden"},{"label":"C","text":"Finland"},{"label":"D","text":"Norway"},{"label":"E","text":"Italy"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1071,"text":"The Union Cabinet, chaired by Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi, has approved the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana -Urban (PMAY -U) 2.0. This ambitious scheme aims to construct 1 crore houses for urban poor and middle -class families over the next five years, with an investment of 10 lakh crore and a government subsidy of __________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2.30 lakh crore"},{"label":"B","text":"2.50 lakh crore"},{"label":"C","text":"2.70 lakh crore"},{"label":"D","text":"2.90 lakh crore"},{"label":"E","text":"3.10 lakh crore"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1072,"text":"Which country hosted the Women&#39;s Hockey Asia Cup 2025?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"India"},{"label":"B","text":"Japan"},{"label":"C","text":"South Korea"},{"label":"D","text":"China"},{"label":"E","text":"Malaysia"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1073,"text":"Comptroller and Auditor General of India Girish Chandra Murmu has been re -elected as the external auditor of ______ for a  four -year term from____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"WHO, 2024 to 2027"},{"label":"B","text":"UNICEF, 2023 to 2026"},{"label":"C","text":"UNESCO, 2024 to 2027"},{"label":"D","text":"WTO, 2023 to 2026"},{"label":"E","text":"UNCTAD, 2024 to 2027"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1074,"text":"Identify which among the following institutes celebrates their foundation day on 1st July?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Indian Space Research Organisation"},{"label":"B","text":"Institute of Chartered Accountants of India"},{"label":"C","text":"Defence Research and Development Organisation"},{"label":"D","text":"Border Roads Organisation"},{"label":"E","text":"NITI Aayog"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1075,"text":"As per the Report of the Committee to develop a Framework for Responsible and Ethical Enablement of Artificial Intelligence (FREE -AI) in the Financial Sector, the framework is structured around how many strategic pillars?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Four"},{"label":"B","text":"Five"},{"label":"C","text":"Six"},{"label":"D","text":"Seven"},{"label":"E","text":"Eight"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1076,"text":"The Green National Highways Corridor Project (GNHCP) is being implemented by the Government of India in partnership with the World Bank to promote the development of safe, green, and climate -resilient highways. Under this project, in which of the following state/states are the highway corridors being developed?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Himachal Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"C","text":"Uttar Pradesh"},{"label":"D","text":"Andhra Pradesh"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1077,"text":"The Singareni  Collieries Company Limited (SCCL) is a Government coal mining company jointly owned by the  Government of ________ and Government of India  on a 51:49 equity basis.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Andhra Pradesh"},{"label":"B","text":"Karnataka"},{"label":"C","text":"Odisha"},{"label":"D","text":"Telangana"},{"label":"E","text":"Maharashtra"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1078,"text":"In recent news, in the month of February 2021, Puducherry Chief Minister V. Narayanasamy has submitted his resignation to Lieutenant Governor Tamilisai Soundararajan, after losing a confidence  vote in the Legislative  Assembly . The Puducherry Legislative Assembly has _________ seats.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"27"},{"label":"B","text":"35"},{"label":"C","text":"28"},{"label":"D","text":"33"},{"label":"E","text":"39"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1080,"text":"As per the Union Budget 2023 -24, the highest surcharge rate in personal income tax has been reduced from 37% to _____ in the new tax regime for income above 2 crore.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"15%"},{"label":"B","text":"36%"},{"label":"C","text":"17%"},{"label":"D","text":"25%"},{"label":"E","text":"30%"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1082,"text":"National Coal Miner&#39;s Day is observed on which date in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"May 2nd"},{"label":"B","text":"May 4th"},{"label":"C","text":"May 9th"},{"label":"D","text":"May 12th"},{"label":"E","text":"May 15th"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1084,"text":"Under which of the following conditions does the DICGC give money to the liquidator? 1. If a bank goes into liquidation. 2. If a bank is reconstructed or amalgamated/merged with another bank 3. If the bank wishes to withdraw from the DICGC","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1 and 2"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 2 and 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 1 and 3"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1085,"text":"Delimitation Commission for which of the following States/UTs has submitted its final report in May 2022?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ladakh"},{"label":"B","text":"Uttarakhand"},{"label":"C","text":"Jammu and Kashmir"},{"label":"D","text":"Rajasthan"},{"label":"E","text":"Arunachal Pradesh"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1086,"text":"Monthly Premium made by India citizen at 18 years of age, under Atal Pension Yojana, opting for Rs. 5000 monthly pension after attaining 60 years of age,  is Rs. ______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"185"},{"label":"B","text":"210"},{"label":"C","text":"225"},{"label":"D","text":"305"},{"label":"E","text":"324"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1089,"text":"50 years after the launch of Project Tiger on April 1, 1973, India&#39;s tiger population today ranges from 2,500 to 3,000. When Project Tiger started, we had ___ tiger reserves. In 2023, we have ___.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"9, 47"},{"label":"B","text":"9, 53"},{"label":"C","text":"9, 48"},{"label":"D","text":"9, 55"},{"label":"E","text":"9, 67"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1090,"text":"India has recently become the only country to adopt the T+1 settlement system after ________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"China"},{"label":"B","text":"Russia"},{"label":"C","text":"United States of America"},{"label":"D","text":"Germany"},{"label":"E","text":"Canada"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1091,"text":"The Union Minister of Ports, Shipping &amp; Waterways and Ayush, Shri Sarbananda Sonowal flagged off the maiden International Cruise Vessel &quot;_______&quot;, India&#39;s first international cruise vessel, from Chennai to _______.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"MV Empress, Bangladesh"},{"label":"B","text":"MV Ganga Vilas, Bhutan"},{"label":"C","text":"MV Empress, Sri Lanka"},{"label":"D","text":"MV Ganga Vilas, Sri Lanka"},{"label":"E","text":"MV Emperor, Sri Lanka"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1092,"text":"As per the recent Monetary Policy Committee meeting of August 2024, the limit for the UPI for the tax payments has been increased from Rs 1 lakh to ____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 10 lakh"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 5 lakh"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 15 lakh"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 3 lakh"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 2 lakh"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1094,"text":"Identify which among the following festivals is celebrated by the Apatani, or Tanw, also known by Apa, the tribal group living in the Ziro valley in the Lower Subansiri district of Arunachal Pradesh in India?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Myoko"},{"label":"B","text":"Gauchar Mela"},{"label":"C","text":"Thisam Phanit"},{"label":"D","text":"Tsukhenyie"},{"label":"E","text":"None of these"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1095,"text":"What is the theme of World Water Day 2022?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Nature for Water"},{"label":"B","text":"Leaving No One Behind"},{"label":"C","text":"Water and Climate Change"},{"label":"D","text":"Valuing Water"},{"label":"E","text":"Groundwater: making the invisible visible"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1096,"text":"Indian government bonds have been included in JP Morgan&#39;s emerging markets index. Foreign Portfolio Investor (FPI) holdings of outstanding FAR bonds could rise to ____ by 2025.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2.4%"},{"label":"B","text":"3.4%"},{"label":"C","text":"2.9%"},{"label":"D","text":"3.9%"},{"label":"E","text":"5.0%"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1098,"text":"Which  of the following States are among the top 3 destination states for FDI in India? 1. Maharashtra 2. Karnataka 3. Gujarat 4. Delhi 5. Tamil Nadu","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1"},{"label":"B","text":"Both 2 &amp; 3"},{"label":"C","text":"1, 3 and 5"},{"label":"D","text":"2, 4 and 5"},{"label":"E","text":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1099,"text":"GST Revenue collection has crossed 1.5 lakh crore for the first time in _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"March 2022"},{"label":"B","text":"April 2022"},{"label":"C","text":"May 2022"},{"label":"D","text":"January 2022"},{"label":"E","text":"February 2022"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1101,"text":"As per Economic Survey 2023 -24, the Foreign Exchange Reserves of India stood at $653.7 billion on June 21, 2024, enough to cover more than _______ of imports projected for FY25 and more than 98 per cent of total external debt outstanding at the end of  March 2024.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"9 months"},{"label":"B","text":"10 months"},{"label":"C","text":"11 months"},{"label":"D","text":"8 months"},{"label":"E","text":"7 months"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1103,"text":"As per the recently published guidelines by RBI in October 2020, Non -deposit - taking HFCs with an asset size of 5,000 crore and above, but less than 10,000 crore will have to reach a minimum LCR of _____ by December 1, 2021 and _______ by Decemb er 1, 2025.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"20%, 40%"},{"label":"B","text":"30%, 60%"},{"label":"C","text":"30%, 100%"},{"label":"D","text":"50%, 100%"},{"label":"E","text":"25%, 50%"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1104,"text":"Consider the following statements regarding the features of Senior Citizen Saving Scheme (SCSS) and identify the correct answer out of the options given below :","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Deposits in SCSS qualify for deduction u/s 80C of Income Tax Act."},{"label":"B","text":"A retired personnel of Defence Services ( excluding civilian defence employees), who has"},{"label":"C","text":"A depositor may open an account individually or jointly with a spouse ."},{"label":"D","text":"Both A &amp; B"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1105,"text":"The Basic Statistical Returns (BSR) Code is a seven -digit code that is provided to the registered banks by the RBI. The first three digits in the code identify the bank, while the following four digits identify the bank branch. India&#39;s Basic Statistic al Returns (BSR) system recently completed _________ since its inception.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10 years"},{"label":"B","text":"20 years"},{"label":"C","text":"50 years"},{"label":"D","text":"25 years"},{"label":"E","text":"75 years"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1106,"text":"The Union Cabinet approved an additional subsidy of  Rs. _____ crore  for phosphate - based fertilisers for the upcoming kharif season (April -September), seeking to shield farmers from any additional burden due to a sharp increase in input costs globally.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 35,935"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 38,938"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 69,939"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 45,945"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs. 50,955"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1107,"text":"The Government of India through Indian Strategic Petroleum Reserve Ltd. (ISPRL) under Phase -1 has set up Strategic Petroleum Reserves (SPR) at three locations namely Visakhapatnam, Mangalore and ________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Varanasi"},{"label":"B","text":"Padur"},{"label":"C","text":"Raipur"},{"label":"D","text":"Kolkata"},{"label":"E","text":"Ranchi"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1108,"text":"What was the theme of World Population Day 2025, observed annually on July 11?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"&quot;Ensuring Reproductive Rights and Choices for All&quot;"},{"label":"B","text":"&quot;Empowering young people to create the families they want in a fair and hopeful world&quot;"},{"label":"C","text":"&quot;Building a Sustainable Future through Family Planning&quot;"},{"label":"D","text":"&quot;Investing in Women for a Resilient Future&quot;"},{"label":"E","text":"&quot;Population and Development: Balancing People and Planet&quot;"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1109,"text":"In the month of February 2021, Seychelles has become the first country to welcome the tourists that have been vaccinated against COVID -19. Seychelles is located in the Indian Ocean, nearest to which of the following countries?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"label":"B","text":"Maldives"},{"label":"C","text":"Malaysia"},{"label":"D","text":"Madagascar"},{"label":"E","text":"South Africa"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1110,"text":"Identify which among the following PSUs has featured on top of the list among &quot;Indian PSUs&quot; in &#39;World&#39;s Best Employer 2020&#39; Report, published by Forbes in the month of October 2020?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"ONGC"},{"label":"B","text":"BHEL"},{"label":"C","text":"NTPC"},{"label":"D","text":"SAIL"},{"label":"E","text":"IOCL"}],"answer":2,"solution":""}]},{"name":"English Language","count":54,"questions":[{"id":918,"text":"Choose the word that best expresses the meaning of the given word: &#39;Ephemeral&#39;","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Eternal"},{"label":"B","text":"Fleeting"},{"label":"C","text":"Permanent"},{"label":"D","text":"Lasting"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Ephemeral means lasting for a very short time. &#39;Fleeting&#39; is a synonym that accurately captures this meaning."},{"id":975,"text":"Choose the word that best expresses the meaning of the given word: &#39;Ephemeral&#39;","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Eternal"},{"label":"B","text":"Fleeting"},{"label":"C","text":"Permanent"},{"label":"D","text":"Lasting"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Ephemeral means lasting for a very short time. &#39;Fleeting&#39; is a synonym that accurately captures this meaning."},{"id":1060,"text":"The manager _______ the new employee to the rest of the team.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"introduced"},{"label":"B","text":"presented"},{"label":"C","text":"explained"},{"label":"D","text":"described"}],"answer":0,"solution":"The word &#39;introduced&#39; means to bring someone into contact with someone else, which fits the context of the sentence."},{"id":1113,"text":"Choose the most appropriate sentence that improves the one given below.\nOriginal: 'The stock market crash was a real eye-waterer for the traders.'\nA. The stock market crash was a real eye-opener for the traders.\nB. The stock market crash was a real heart-breaker for the traders.\nC. The stock market crash was a real tear-jerker for the traders.\nD. The stock market crash was a real eye-waterer for the traders.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The stock market crash was a real eye-opener for the traders."},{"label":"B","text":"The stock market crash was a real heart-breaker for the traders."},{"label":"C","text":"The stock market crash was a real tear-jerker for the traders."},{"label":"D","text":"The stock market crash was a real eye-waterer for the traders."}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Analyze original: 'eye-waterer' implies crying, which is awkward for financial loss.\n2. Evaluate A: 'eye-opener' means enlightening/teaching, not emotionally painful.\n3. Evaluate B: 'heart-breaker' accurately conveys severe emotional pain due to loss.\n4. Evaluate C: 'tear-jerker' implies sad but touching stories, not financial ruin.\n5. Select B as the standard improvement."},{"id":1119,"text":"The Minister expressed deep concern regarding the delay in releasing the funds, stating that the bureaucratic hurdle prevented him from proceeding __________ his scheduled visit to the flood-hit district.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) to"},{"label":"B","text":"B) onto"},{"label":"C","text":"C) into"},{"label":"D","text":"D) upon"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. The verb 'proceed' forms a fixed phrase with the preposition 'to'.\n2. 'Proceed to' indicates moving towards a specific destination or action.\n3. 'Proceed onto' implies physical movement over a surface, which is contextually weak here.\n4. 'Proceed into' suggests entering an enclosed space, not suitable for a visit concept.\n5. 'Proceed upon' is archaic and rarely used in modern Indian English.\n6. Therefore, the grammatically correct completion is 'proceeding to his scheduled visit'.\n7. The intended meaning is moving towards the event of the visit."},{"id":1120,"text":"The RBI Governor announced that the newly issued sovereign bonds offer '_____,' a financial instrument specifically designed to protect investors' principal value against rising consumer price indices.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Deflationary Hedges"},{"label":"B","text":"Inflation-Indexed Bonds"},{"label":"C","text":"Zero-Coupon Securities"},{"label":"D","text":"Treasury Bills"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. The context mentions protecting 'principal value' against 'rising consumer price indices'.\n2. This describes a financial instrument where the principal or interest rate adjusts based on inflation.\n3. Option A (Deflationary) contradicts the condition of rising prices.\n4. Option C (Zero-Coupon) refers to purchase price vs face value, not inflation adjustment.\n5. Option D (Treasury Bills) are short-term debt, not necessarily indexed.\n6. Option B ('Inflation-Indexed Bonds') is the precise term for bonds linked to CPI.\n7. Thus, it is the only correct substitution for the definition provided.\n8. The answer is 'Inflation-Indexed Bonds'."},{"id":1121,"text":"Select the most appropriate word to fill the blank: 'The departmental inquiry concluded that the official was guilty of severe negligence; he had been completely ______ by his own red tape and bureaucratic delays, rendering him unfit for service.'","options":[{"label":"A","text":"ensnared"},{"label":"B","text":"deluded"},{"label":"C","text":"distracted"},{"label":"D","text":"obsessed"}],"answer":0,"solution":"The phrase 'caught in the web of red tape' implies being trapped or ensnared. The sentence structure requires a verb meaning 'trapped'. Ensnares means caught, whereas deluded (deceived), distracted (distracted attention), and obsessed (fixated) do not fit the metaphorical context of being trapped by bureaucracy."},{"id":1122,"text":"In a recent press briefing regarding the rising cost of living, the Minister stated that 'inflation hedging' schemes must be restructured to account for 'administrative bloat,' which acts as a hidden tax. The term referring to this specific administrative waste or excess is:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A]Red Tapeism"},{"label":"B","text":"B]Freneticism"},{"label":"C","text":"C]Bureaucracy"},{"label":"D","text":"D]Nepotism"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Identify the context: Rising costs due to administrative inefficiency.\n2. Define 'administrative bloat': Excessive red tape, unnecessary rules, and delay causing waste.\n3. Evaluate options: Freneticism is speed/panic; Bureaucracy is the system itself; Nepotism is favoritism.\n4. Select correct term: Red Tapeism specifically denotes the excessive bureaucratic formalism described."},{"id":1123,"text":"The district magistrate's decision to 'delay' the release of flood relief funds by invoking a complex, non-existent circular was described by senior officers as a __________ act, where administrative lethargy masqueraded as procedural rigor.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A. pragmatic"},{"label":"B","text":"B. bureaucratic"},{"label":"C","text":"C. visionary"},{"label":"D","text":"D. expedient"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. The sentence describes an act involving 'complex, non-existent circulars' and 'administrative lethargy'.\n2. Such behavior is the definition of red tape or excessive adherence to procedure for its own sake.\n3. The term 'pragmatic' implies practical efficiency, which contradicts the delay.\n4. 'Visionary' implies forward-thinking innovation, not obstructionism.\n5. 'Expedient' implies doing something convenient or quick, whereas the text highlights unnecessary slowness.\n6. Therefore, only 'bureaucratic' accurately captures the negative connotation of artificial complexity and delay described."},{"id":1124,"text":"Select the most appropriate word to complete the sentence with logical consistency:\n'The Central Board of Direct Taxes (CBDT) announced a __________ on the new e-filing format, citing \"technical complexities\" and \"resource constraints,\" yet simultaneously dispatched 500 inspectors to verify returns filed under the old system. This decision creates a(n) __________ for compliant taxpayers who fear their data is already flagged.'\nOptions:\nA) moratorium, paradox\nB) respite, dichotomy\nC) reprieve, anomaly\nD) mandate, contradiction","options":[{"label":"A","text":"moratorium, paradox"},{"label":"B","text":"respite, dichotomy"},{"label":"C","text":"reprieve, anomaly"},{"label":"D","text":"mandate, contradiction"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. 'Moratorium' means a temporary suspension of action (fitting the delay due to 'technical complexities').\n2. 'Paradox' fits the context: suspending a new efficient system while enforcing the old one creates a logical contradiction (a paradox) regarding fairness.\n3. Other options fail: 'Reprieve' implies punishment for crime; 'Mandate' contradicts the idea of delay. 'Dichotomy' and 'Anomaly' do not capture the inherent logical contradiction as sharply as 'paradox'."},{"id":1125,"text":"In the recent parliamentary debate on railway safety, a junior bureaucrat argued that while new surveillance cameras were installed across stations, 'the silent witness' had been replaced by a digital one. In this specific context, what does the idiom 'the silent witness' most logically refer to?\n\nA. The anonymity of passengers who refuse to speak.\nB. The natural environment (wind, weather) that historically observed the station without human intervention.\nC. A specific legal doctrine regarding non-human evidence in criminal law.\nD. The internal monologue of the station master during a panic situation.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The anonymity of passengers who refuse to speak."},{"label":"B","text":"The natural environment (wind, weather) that historically observed the station without human intervention."},{"label":"C","text":"A specific legal doctrine regarding non-human evidence in criminal law."},{"label":"D","text":"The internal monologue of the station master during a panic situation."}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. The phrase 'the silent witness' traditionally refers to nature or inanimate elements observing an event.\n2. The text contrasts 'new surveillance cameras' with the old method of observation.\n3. Cameras are artificial; their replacement implies a shift from artificial to natural/original observation.\n4. Therefore, the 'silent witness' here represents the natural environment previously acting as the only observer before human technology."},{"id":1127,"text":"In the bustling Mumbai tea stall, amidst the chaotic noise of commuters and hawkers, old Manohar sat quietly. He observed the frantic crowd but remained utterly __________ to the loud arguments breaking out on his left.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A] deaf"},{"label":"B","text":"B] immune"},{"label":"C","text":"C] blind"},{"label":"D","text":"D] oblivious"}],"answer":3,"solution":"The idiom 'oblivious' means unaware or unconscious of something, which fits perfectly for someone ignoring a situation without any physical inability (like being deaf or blind). 'Deaf' and 'blind' are literal; 'immune' is usually used for diseases or emotional reactions."},{"id":1128,"text":"The Prime Minister's speech on the National Infrastructure Project concluded exactly as the first train departed from New Delhi, ______ that the new high-speed line would reduce travel time by 40% within two years.\nA) stating\nB) had it stated\nC) it was stated\nD) which was stated","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) stating"},{"label":"B","text":"B) had it stated"},{"label":"C","text":"C) it was stated"},{"label":"D","text":"D) which was stated"}],"answer":0,"solution":"The sentence structure requires a present participle ('stating') to create an adverbial clause of time/reason simultaneous with the main action (speech concluding). Options B, C, and D introduce grammatical errors or awkward passive constructions that do not fit the active narrative flow."},{"id":1129,"text":"A new high-speed rail project was announced with a projected completion date of December. However, due to unexpected land acquisition delays and budget re-allocations, the original schedule _______.\nA) remained intact\nB) crumbled\nC) shifted significantly\nD) vanished","options":[{"label":"A","text":"remained intact"},{"label":"B","text":"crumbled"},{"label":"C","text":"shifted significantly"},{"label":"D","text":"vanished"}],"answer":2,"solution":"1. Identify the key phrase: 'original schedule'. 2. Context: Project delays (land acquisition, budget). 3. Logic: A schedule doesn't just stay (intact), vanish (impossible), or crumble (schedule is abstract, project does); it changes position/time. 4. Conclusion: 'Shifted significantly' is the only idiomatically and logically correct connector."},{"id":1130,"text":"Select the option that best replaces the phrase 'to bring the debate to an end temporarily, with a promise to resume later':\n\n'A. To adjourn'\n'B. To recess'\nC. To prorogue'\n'D. To dissolve'","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A. To adjourn"},{"label":"B","text":"B. To recess"},{"label":"C","text":"C. To prorogue"},{"label":"D","text":"D. To dissolve"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Step 1: Identify the core meaning: temporary suspension of a meeting/debate.\nStep 2: Analyze 'To adjourn': Specifically means to end a meeting temporarily to resume later.\nStep 3: Analyze 'To recess': Means to take a break (often lunch), but in legislative terms, can imply a longer pause, though less precise than adjourn for a debate end.\nStep 4: Analyze 'To prorogue': Refers to ending a session of parliament entirely (usually by the governor/governor-general), effectively killing the session until a new one is summoned; not a temporary pause of a debate.\nStep 5: Analyze 'To dissolve': Means to end an assembly permanently or completely (e.g., dissolving the Lok Sabha).\nConclusion: 'To adjourn' is the precise term for stopping a debate temporarily."},{"id":1131,"text":"Select the word that best completes the sentence: 'If the monsoon onset had been delayed by three weeks, the resulting drought would have triggered a scenario described as a ______,' where the blank requires a term for a situation of sudden, overwhelming scarcity caused specifically by a lack of rain during the critical agricultural window.'","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A. Calamity"},{"label":"B","text":"B. Famine"},{"label":"C","text":"C. Scarcity"},{"label":"D","text":"D. Misery"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Analyze the cause: delayed monsoon leads to crop failure due to water shortage.\n2. Define 'Calamity': a broad term for disaster, not specific to food shortage.\n3. Define 'Famine': a severe scarcity of food causing widespread hunger/starvation.\n4. Define 'Scarcity': lack of enough supply; while accurate for goods, it lacks the severity implied by the context of a national crisis affecting populations.\n5. Define 'Misery': a state of suffering, too abstract and emotional for an economic/agricultural definition.\n6. Apply logic: The specific technical term for drought-induced food shortage leading to starvation is 'Famine'.\n7. Therefore, 'Famine' is the precise one-word substitution."},{"id":1133,"text":"In a complex administrative dispute, the Chief Administrative Officer issued a directive: 'To ensure compliance, all departmental heads must submit their quarterly reports to the registry by the end of this month; however, any department found in violation of the internal audit guidelines regarding expenditure caps will be subject to a specific procedural status until rectified.' If a department is currently under such scrutiny for exceeding its budget limits, what is the precise procedural status described by the directive that prevents them from proceeding with new projects?\n\nA) Audited\nB) Categorized\nC) Stagnant\nD) Suspended","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Audited"},{"label":"B","text":"Categorized"},{"label":"C","text":"Stagnant"},{"label":"D","text":"Suspended"}],"answer":3,"solution":"1. Analyze the context: The department is in violation of audit guidelines.\n2. Interpret 'procedural status': In government/bureaucratic contexts, violating compliance rules usually leads to an active halt on operations.\n3. Evaluate options:\n   - A) Audited: Describes the process, not necessarily the punitive status preventing projects.\n   - B) Categorized: Too vague; does not imply restriction.\n   - C) Stagnant: Adjective describing a state, not an official administrative order/status.\n   - D) Suspended: The specific legal/bureaucratic term used to halt operations (projects) until the violation is rectified.\n4. Conclusion: 'Suspended' is the only option that functions as the correct formal status preventing action."},{"id":1134,"text":"In a newly formed administrative zone, the Governor issued an order to prevent the duplication of duties among officials who are already working in the same department. This act of assigning two or more responsibilities to a single official is known as:\nA) Embezzlement\nB) Pluralism\nC) Congruence\nD) Accumulation","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Embezzlement"},{"label":"B","text":"Pluralism"},{"label":"C","text":"Congruence"},{"label":"D","text":"Accumulation"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The question describes the assignment of multiple roles to one person. In a bureaucratic context, holding or performing more than one public office is termed 'Pluralism' (or Plurality of offices), leading to redundancy. Embezzlement is theft; Congruence means agreement; Accumulation is gathering but lacks the specific administrative connotation of overlapping duties."},{"id":1138,"text":"Select the option that correctly completes the sentence: 'After years of meticulous preparation and a promising career start, his sudden decision to quit mid-project left him _____ in a financial mess.'","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) stuck high on the wall"},{"label":"B","text":"B) stuck with the bill"},{"label":"C","text":"C) stuck in a rut"},{"label":"D","text":"D) stuck for an answer"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. The phrase 'financial mess' implies a lack of funds.\n2. 'Stuck with the bill' means having to pay for something or bear the cost alone.\n3. Context: He prepared, started well, but quitting (the halt) caused him to face the costs he couldn't avoid.\n4. 'Stuck in a rut' implies boredom/lack of progress, which contradicts the sudden financial crisis described.\n5. The other options do not fit the context of being unable to pay debts due to a specific action."},{"id":1139,"text":"Select the most appropriate sentence to complete the following statement: \n'The Director has ordered that all staff members must ensure strict adherence to safety protocols. Furthermore,'\nA) any negligence will be punished severely, and\nB) violations shall incur severe disciplinary action, and\nC) those who are found at fault will get a warning, and\nD) people breaking rules will face consequences, and","options":[{"label":"A","text":"any negligence will be punished severely, and"},{"label":"B","text":"violations shall incur severe disciplinary action, and"},{"label":"C","text":"those who are found at fault will get a warning, and"},{"label":"D","text":"people breaking rules will face consequences, and"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The initial clause uses formal language ('strict adherence', 'ordered'). Option B matches this tone using legal/administrative vocabulary ('shall incur', 'disciplinary action'). Options A, C, and D use colloquial or less precise terms ('punished', 'get a warning', 'people'), which break the register consistency."},{"id":1140,"text":"Select the most appropriate option to complete the sentence: 'Among the various schemes, _______ by the Ministry of Rural Development has received mixed reactions from the farmers regarding its implementation timeline.'\n\nA) the one\nB) that which\nC) which is\nD) it","options":[{"label":"A","text":"the one"},{"label":"B","text":"that which"},{"label":"C","text":"which is"},{"label":"D","text":"it"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Identify the relative clause modifying 'various schemes'.\n2. The antecedent 'schemes' is plural, but the predicate requires a singular referent to agree with the singular verb phrase 'has received'.\n3. Option A ('the one') functions as a demonstrative pronoun referring back to the specific scheme, maintaining subject-verb agreement.\n4. Options B and C introduce unnecessary complexity or incorrect grammatical structures for this context.\n5. Option D creates a fragment lacking a connector."},{"id":1142,"text":"In a high-stakes corporate restructuring, the Chairman delivered a speech that was widely regarded as a __________ for morale, as his sudden resignation announcement turned hopeful anticipation into deep despair.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"blessing"},{"label":"B","text":"curse"},{"label":"C","text":"nuisance"},{"label":"D","text":"boon"}],"answer":1,"solution":"A blessing or boon implies improvement; a nuisance is minor. The context describes a negative outcome (despair) from an expected positive event, making 'curse' the only logical synonym for a misfortune."},{"id":1143,"text":"In the chaotic final minutes of the cricket match, when Team A was winning by 4 wickets with only one ball remaining, they were struck by a sudden collapse and lost their lead instantly. This abrupt cessation of momentum caused them to finish the game in defeat despite their earlier dominance.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Euphoria"},{"label":"B","text":"Nadir"},{"label":"C","text":"Anvil"},{"label":"D","text":"Lull"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Nadir means the lowest point. Team A went from winning to losing in one ball, so the collapse marked the nadir of their match."},{"id":1144,"text":"Read the sentence below carefully. The blank requires an idiom that describes a state of affairs contrary to its literal meaning, specifically where a lack of official recognition leads to an outcome typically associated with authority or celebration in Indian administrative contexts.\n\n'Since no one from the district administration had issued a formal ______ for the rural artisans' fair, the local police station, in a display of civic pride, ended up issuing a commendation letter that felt like a royal decree to the crowd.'\n\nWhich idiom best fits the blank to reflect the missing official sanction?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"blank cheque"},{"label":"B","text":"free pass"},{"label":"C","text":"green signal"},{"label":"D","text":"red light"}],"answer":2,"solution":"The context requires an 'official sanction' or permission. A 'green signal' is an idiom for approval/permission. The sentence describes a lack of this, so 'no one had issued a formal green signal' fits the bureaucratic gap before the police stepped in."},{"id":1145,"text":"In the latest bureaucratic memo, the Director accused the department of 'walking on eggshells'. However, upon reviewing the attached data showing a 150% increase in reckless spending, the oversight committee concluded that the department was actually: [Options]. The word that best fills the blank while inverting the intended meaning from the idiom is:\nA) Cautious\nB) Indifferent\nC) Immeasurable\nD) Reckless","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cautious"},{"label":"B","text":"Indifferent"},{"label":"C","text":"Immeasurable"},{"label":"D","text":"Reckless"}],"answer":3,"solution":"1. The idiom 'walking on eggshells' implies extreme caution.\n2. The data shows reckless behavior (high spending).\n3. The question asks for the word that inverts the caution implied by the idiom to match the data.\n4. 'Reckless' is the antonym of cautious, fitting the data and the semantic inversion mechanism."},{"id":1150,"text":"Select the option that correctly completes the sentence: The committee —\nA) have decided to delay the meeting.\nB) have decided on delaying the meeting.\nC) has decided on delaying the meeting.\nD) has decide to delay the meeting.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"have decided to delay the meeting."},{"label":"B","text":"have decided on delaying the meeting."},{"label":"C","text":"has decided on delaying the meeting."},{"label":"D","text":"has decide to delay the meeting."}],"answer":2,"solution":"1. Subject: 'The committee' (Collective Noun).\n2. Rule: Collective nouns take a singular verb when the group acts as one unit.\n3. Correct Verb: 'has'.\n4. Phrase: 'decided on [gerund]'.\n5. Option C fits all criteria."},{"id":1151,"text":"Which one-word substitution correctly completes the sentence: 'The __________ is an official responsible for collecting revenue and managing finances in a local government office.'?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Registrar"},{"label":"B","text":"Treasurer"},{"label":"C","text":"Collector"},{"label":"D","text":"Clerk"}],"answer":2,"solution":"Step 1: Identify the key function defined: collecting revenue and managing finances locally.\nStep 2: Analyze option A (Registrar): Handles records/registration, not finances.\nStep 3: Analyze option B (Treasurer): Manages funds but is a title rarely used for general local revenue collection in this specific context compared to 'Collector'.\nStep 4: Analyze option C (Collector): In the Indian administrative system, a Collector is specifically the district-level head responsible for revenue administration and law & order.\nStep 5: Analyze option D (Clerk): General office staff, not the specific official role.\nStep 6: Conclude that 'Collector' fits the definition of managing local finances/revenue best in the Indian context."},{"id":1162,"text":"In the context of the recent 'Digital India' initiative, a government report stated that '______' in rural governance involves moving from reactive aid to proactive planning. Which word best fits the blank?\n\nA) Reactionism\nB) Proactivity\nC) Indifference\nD) Conservatism","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Reactionism"},{"label":"B","text":"Proactivity"},{"label":"C","text":"Indifference"},{"label":"D","text":"Conservatism"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The sentence contrasts 'reactive' (past-oriented) with 'proactive' (future-oriented). 'Proactivity' is the direct antonym of 'reactionism' and fits the positive context of modern governance. Options A, C, and D contradict the initiative's goals."},{"id":1163,"text":"Select the option that best completes the idiom based on the provided context:\n'After months of rigorous preparation for the UPSC Civil Services, Rahul felt _______ to see his name not feature in the preliminary merit list.'\nA) a feather in one's cap\nB) a bitter pill to swallow\nC) a cat among pigeons\nD) a dark horse","options":[{"label":"A","text":"a feather in one's cap"},{"label":"B","text":"a bitter pill to swallow"},{"label":"C","text":"a cat among pigeons"},{"label":"D","text":"a dark horse"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Context: Disappointment after effort. Idiom 'a bitter pill to swallow' fits the negative sentiment of failure/rejection. Options A (success), C (anomaly/disorder), and D (unknown winner) do not fit the context."},{"id":1164,"text":"Identify the sentence that is most appropriate for a formal letter of appointment from a government department:\n'A. You are hereby appointed as a Junior Assistant, effective from 1st July 2024.\nB. They have made you the Junior Assistant starting July 1st.\nC. Get ready to work as a Junior Assistant from tomorrow.\nD. You are chosen for the job of Junior Assistant.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"You are hereby appointed as a Junior Assistant, effective from 1st July 2024."},{"label":"B","text":"They have made you the Junior Assistant starting July 1st."},{"label":"C","text":"Get ready to work as a Junior Assistant from tomorrow."},{"label":"D","text":"You are chosen for the job of Junior Assistant."}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Option A uses the standard legal phrase 'hereby appointed' and 'effective from', which is the mandatory register for official government correspondence in India.\n2. Option B uses 'made you' (colloquial) and lacks the precise date format ('July 1st' vs '1st July').\n3. Option C uses imperative 'Get ready' (inappropriate for an appointment letter).\n4. Option D uses 'chosen' (informal) and vague phrasing.\n5. Only Option A adheres to the passive/formal voice required by SSC, IBPS, and SBI guidelines for administrative writing."},{"id":1165,"text":"Read the following instruction found in a formal circular issued by the Ministry of Railways. Identify the sentence that best completes the paragraph while maintaining the required administrative tone.\n\n'The undersigned authority hereby directs all concerned regarding the upcoming festive period: ____. Failure to comply will attract strict departmental action.',\n\nOptions:\nA. 'Please make sure no passengers are delayed during the holiday rush.'\nB. 'It is imperative that no train delays occur; hence, extra traction must be ensured.'\nC. 'We hope everyone travels safely without any hitches.'\nD. 'You must ensure trains run on time because the government will punish you.'","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Please make sure no passengers are delayed during the holiday rush."},{"label":"B","text":"It is imperative that no train delays occur; hence, extra traction must be ensured."},{"label":"C","text":"We hope everyone travels safely without any hitches."},{"label":"D","text":"You must ensure trains run on time because the government will punish you."}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Option A uses colloquial phrasing ('make sure', 'holiday rush').\n2. Option C uses informal vocabulary ('hitches') and lacks authority.\n3. Option D uses rude imperative language ('You must', 'punish you').\n4. Option B uses formal adjectives ('imperative', 'traction') and passive/objective structure, fitting a government circular."},{"id":1166,"text":"Select the sentence that correctly completes the logic of the statement: \n\"The Indian Railways' new e-ticketing initiative is [BLANK] successful.\"\n\nContext Clues: In a specific financial year, digital ticket sales constituted exactly 15% of total tickets sold, but this represented a significant increase from previous years. However, manual counters still processed the majority of transactions during peak hours.\nA. moderately and only\nB. largely yet not fully\nC. hardly and merely\nD. completely and absolutely","options":[{"label":"A","text":"moderately and only"},{"label":"B","text":"largely yet not fully"},{"label":"C","text":"hardly and merely"},{"label":"D","text":"completely and absolutely"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The prompt establishes a mixed reality: digital sales increased significantly (positive) but are still minor compared to manual counters (negative). 'Completely' implies total dominance (false). 'Hardly' implies near-failure (false, as 15% growth is significant). 'Moderately' minimizes the significance. 'Largely' captures the positive trend of increase, while 'yet not fully' acknowledges the remaining reliance on manual counters, fitting the 'mixed but positive' data."},{"id":1167,"text":"Identify the option that corrects the sentence to ensure formal register suitable for an official bank statement:\nThe current balance shows a debit entry of fifty rupees, and now it needs to be written as ______.\nA) A negative amount of fifty rupees\nB) A deduction of fifty rupees made from the account\nC) Fifty rupees being removed from the total\nD) The account losing fifty rupees","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A: A negative amount of fifty rupees"},{"label":"B","text":"B: A deduction of fifty rupees made from the account"},{"label":"C","text":"C: Fifty rupees being removed from the total"},{"label":"D","text":"D: The account losing fifty rupees"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Identify the error in the stem's description: 'Fifty rupees' is a noun, not a verb describing action.\n2. Analyze Option A: 'Negative amount' describes the math sign, not the transaction event formally.\n3. Analyze Option C: 'Being removed' is passive and slightly awkward for financial reports.\n4. Analyze Option D: 'Losing' is colloquial and personifies the account; formal banking uses 'deduction' or 'credit/debit'.\n5. Select Option B as it uses the precise term 'deduction' common in ledger entries."},{"id":1168,"text":"Identify the sentence that correctly uses formal vocabulary suitable for an official audit report:\nA) The bank needs to sort out the discrepancies in the ledgers.\nB) The bank requires rectification of the variances observed in the accounts.\nC) The bank ought to get rid of the mistakes found in the books.\nD) The bank has to fix up the errors noticed in the statements.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The bank needs to sort out the discrepancies in the ledgers."},{"label":"B","text":"The bank requires rectification of the variances observed in the accounts."},{"label":"C","text":"The bank ought to get rid of the mistakes found in the books."},{"label":"D","text":"The bank has to fix up the errors noticed in the statements."}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Analyze register: Option A uses colloquial \"sort out\".\n2. Evaluate Option C: \"get rid of\" is informal.\n3. Check Option D: \"fix up\" and \"errors\" are less formal.\n4. Validate Option B: \"requires rectification\" and \"variances\" match audit terminology."},{"id":1169,"text":"In a recent village assembly meeting, the Sarpanch expressed strong disapproval of the proposal to use public funds for personal gain. He stated that such an action would be ___ to the principles of democracy.\n\nChoose the word that best fits the blank in the context of formal official language:\nA) inimical\nB) hostile\nC) detrimental\nD) antagonistic","options":[{"label":"A","text":"inimical"},{"label":"B","text":"hostile"},{"label":"C","text":"detrimental"},{"label":"D","text":"antagonistic"}],"answer":0,"solution":"The sentence describes an action (using public funds for personal gain) that is morally and officially opposed to democratic principles. 'Inimical' is the precise formal term meaning 'harmful or unfavorable,' often used in official contexts to denote opposition to a cause or principle. While 'hostile', 'detrimental', and 'antagonistic' are synonyms, they lack the specific connotation of acting against a system of governance found in the definition of 'inimical' within formal register."},{"id":1170,"text":"Identify the option that best completes the sentence by shifting the tone to formal administrative register suitable for a government report, correcting the error in informal phrasing:\n'The project manager reported that the funds were _____ before the deadline.'\nA) exhausted\nB) drained away\nC) burnt out\nD) finished up","options":[{"label":"A","text":"exhausted"},{"label":"B","text":"drained away"},{"label":"C","text":"burnt out"},{"label":"D","text":"finished up"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. The sentence describes a government report context.\n2. 'Exhausted' is the standard formal term for funds in official records.\n3. 'Burnt out' implies machinery failure; 'drained away' is informal/poetic; 'finished up' is colloquial.\n4. Only Option A fits the required formal register."},{"id":1171,"text":"In the context of a formal government audit report, which single word best replaces the phrase 'the act of speaking with unnecessary detail and verbosity to obscure meaning'?\nA) Loquacious\nB) Prolix\nC) Verbose\nD) Effusive","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Loquacious"},{"label":"B","text":"Prolix"},{"label":"C","text":"Verbose"},{"label":"D","text":"Effusive"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. The context is a formal audit report requiring precise, non-colloquial vocabulary.\n2. 'Loquacious' refers to being talkative but not necessarily obscure or wordy in a specific text.\n3. 'Verbose' describes the quality of being wordy but lacks the connotation of 'obscuring meaning through unnecessary detail'.\n4. 'Effusive' means expressing emotion freely, which is irrelevant here.\n5. 'Prolix' specifically defines an excessively long or wordy (verbosity) style that obscures clarity, fitting the definition perfectly for formal register."},{"id":1172,"text":"In the quarterly review of a District Cooperative Bank's accounts, the Chairman noted that 'the financial statements failed to balance due to unrecorded entries'. Which single word best describes the state of the books mentioned?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A. Audited"},{"label":"B","text":"B. Discrepant"},{"label":"C","text":"C. Conciliatory"},{"label":"D","text":"D. Rectified"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The phrase 'failed to balance' indicates a lack of agreement or consistency between two sets of figures (assets vs liabilities). In formal financial and legal contexts, a statement where the numbers do not match is described as 'discrepant'. 'Audited' implies a check was done, 'Conciliatory' refers to attitude, and 'Rectified' implies the error was fixed. Therefore, 'Discrepant' is the precise formal term for unbalanced accounts."},{"id":1173,"text":"In the latest policy draft issued by the Central Vigilance Commission, a clause was added stating that 'whistleblower protection applies to all government employees,' but immediately following this, an exclusionary note stated: 'Employees of defense contractors under Department of Defense (DoD) are excluded from this specific chapter.' \nGiven the hierarchy where DoD is a central ministry, which option best corrects the logical inconsistency in the sentence structure without altering the legal intent?\n\nOriginal Sentence: 'The regulation applies to all government employees, excluding DoD contractors,' vs 'The regulation applies to all government employees including DoD contractors.'","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A. The original sentence is logically consistent as 'government employees' and 'DoD contractors' are distinct categories in the public sector."},{"label":"B","text":"B. The clause should be corrected to: 'whistleblower protection applies to all central government employees, excluding only those classified under defense contracts,' to resolve the ambiguity of inclusion."},{"label":"C","text":"C. The phrase 'defense contractors' must be replaced with 'paramilitary forces' to align with the existing exclusion policy."},{"label":"D","text":"D. The sentence requires no changes as the exclusion is a standard proviso found in all Indian central ministry regulations."}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Identify the contradiction: The first part grants universal protection ('all government employees'), while the second restricts it to an external entity ('DoD contractors').\n2. Analyze hierarchy: DoD contractors are private entities; DoD employees are central govt servants. Calling contractors 'government employees' is legally incorrect.\n3. Resolve logic: The intent is likely broad coverage with specific exceptions. Option B clarifies the distinction between 'central government employees' (included) and 'defense contracts' (excluded), removing the grammatical fallacy of calling contractors 'employees'."},{"id":1174,"text":"Read the following extract from a high-level administrative circular regarding the reclassification of state forest land:\n\n\"In light of the Supreme Court's directive, the administration has deemed it necessary to _______ the erstwhile designated 'protective buffer zones' and instead classify them as 'active eco-corridors,' thereby mandating stricter patrolling protocols.\" \nWhich word best fits the blank in a context emphasizing **mandatory legal reassignment**?\n\nA. Abrogate\nB. Relocate\nC. Rezone\nD. Revise","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Abrogate"},{"label":"B","text":"Relocate"},{"label":"C","text":"Rezone"},{"label":"D","text":"Revise"}],"answer":2,"solution":"1. Context: Legal/Administrative action changing land use classification.\n2. Definition: 'Rezone' specifically means legally changing the permitted usage or designation of an area (e.g., from protective to active).\n3. Elimination: 'Abrogate' implies cancelling a law entirely; 'Relocate' implies moving people/structures; 'Revise' implies minor textual correction.\n4. Fit: Only 'Rezone' captures the specific act of official land classification change described."},{"id":1178,"text":"Select the most appropriate preposition to complete the sentence while maintaining a formal, bureaucratic register often used in official Indian government circulars regarding policy implementation.\n\n\"The Ministry issued a directive _____ all regional offices to align their operational timelines with the central committee's new fiscal framework.\"","options":[{"label":"A","text":"towards"},{"label":"B","text":"for"},{"label":"C","text":"to"},{"label":"D","text":"about"}],"answer":2,"solution":"In formal English, specifically bureaucratic registers, directives, orders, and notices are issued 'to' the intended recipients or entities. 'Towards' implies direction but not necessarily direct address; 'for' implies benefit rather than receipt of instruction; 'about' is colloquial. Therefore, 'to' is the grammatically and stylistically correct choice."},{"id":1179,"text":"In a recent public sector audit, the department's 'Performance Review Matrix' was found to be __________ that it could not account for the 15% reduction in operational efficiency.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"so"},{"label":"B","text":"such"},{"label":"C","text":"as"},{"label":"D","text":"that"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The phrase 'such that' is required here because the blank precedes a clause starting with a verb ('could') and introduces a consequence or result. 'So' is followed by an adjective/adverb, while 'as' implies comparison which doesn't fit the causal context of the audit finding."},{"id":1180,"text":"A government circular has been issued regarding the 'Swachh Bharat Abhiyan'. The text states: 'Citizens are advised to adhere strictly to the hygiene protocols.' The phrase 'adhere strictly to' most closely means:\n\nA) To casually observe without care\nB) To comply fully with the requirements\nC) To ignore the instructions completely\nD) To modify the protocol slightly","options":[{"label":"A","text":"To casually observe without care"},{"label":"B","text":"To comply fully with the requirements"},{"label":"C","text":"To ignore the instructions completely"},{"label":"D","text":"To modify the protocol slightly"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The idiom 'adhere to' means to stick firmly to or follow something. In a formal bureaucratic context like a government circular, 'adhere strictly' implies full and exact compliance with rules. Option B is the correct definition."},{"id":1181,"text":"A 'Rashtriya Karmayogi' portal has launched to digitise the administration. During the inauguration, the Prime Minister noted that 'bureaucratic delays are often caused by a lack of __________ in decision-making'. Which word best completes the sentence while maintaining formal administrative register?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Procrastination"},{"label":"B","text":"Expedition"},{"label":"C","text":"Negligence"},{"label":"D","text":"Stagnation"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The context implies a positive attribute needed to overcome 'delays'. 'Expedition' (swiftness/diligence) is the only positive term that logically eliminates delays. 'Procrastination', 'Negligence', and 'Stagnation' are causes of delay, not solutions."},{"id":1182,"text":"Read the following official notification excerpt: 'To ensure compliance, all district collectors must submit their quarterly progress reports before the 30th.' Which of the following idioms best replaces 'before the 30th' while maintaining the strict, bureaucratic tone required in this specific document?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) by the time"},{"label":"B","text":"B) prior to the deadline"},{"label":"C","text":"C) no later than the 30th"},{"label":"D","text":"D) well before the month ends"}],"answer":2,"solution":"1. The context is a strict bureaucratic instruction regarding a 'deadline'.\n2. 'By the time' implies a vague temporal marker, not a constraint.\n3. 'Prior to the deadline' is grammatically redundant if the date isn't specified as 'the deadline'.\n4. 'Well before' suggests a buffer period, contradicting the strictness of 'compliance'.\n5. 'No later than' is the precise bureaucratic idiom for an absolute cut-off point."},{"id":1208,"text":"Complete the sentence with the most appropriate idiom that matches the irony of the situation described:\n'The new regulation was hailed as a breakthrough, but for the struggling small vendors, it turned out to be a complete ________.'\nA) Silver bullet\nB) Double-edged sword\nC) Curse in disguise\nD) Pyrrhic victory","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) Silver bullet"},{"label":"B","text":"B) Double-edged sword"},{"label":"C","text":"C) Curse in disguise"},{"label":"D","text":"D) Pyrrhic victory"}],"answer":2,"solution":"1. Identify the context: A 'breakthrough' (positive expectation) resulted in negative impact for vendors.\n2. Analyze Option A: 'Silver bullet' implies an effective solution to a problem, which contradicts the negative outcome.\n3. Analyze Option B: 'Double-edged sword' implies something having both positive and negative effects simultaneously. While possible, the sentence emphasizes the *turning out* to be bad after hope.\n4. Analyze Option C: 'Curse in disguise' perfectly fits the irony where a seemingly good thing ('breakthrough') turns into a disaster for specific people.\n5. Analyze Option D: 'Pyrrhic victory' requires there to be a victory first, which is not the case here as the vendors suffered loss."},{"id":1209,"text":"To boost the 'Stand-Up India' initiative for female entrepreneurs, the Central Bank announced a 'soft-lending' policy requiring banks to extend credit at rates **below** the benchmark. Consequently, banks must now avoid any practice that implies charging exorbitant fees or hidden costs.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) Subsidize"},{"label":"B","text":"B) Exploit"},{"label":"C","text":"C) Regulate"},{"label":"D","text":"D) Ignore"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The context describes a 'soft-lending' policy which implies low costs for the borrower. The sentence structure 'avoid any practice that...' requires a word meaning 'to take unfair advantage of someone's weakness or situation for profit'. Among the options, only 'Exploit' fits this negative definition (charging exorbitant fees/hidden costs), making it the correct antonym to the supportive policy described."},{"id":1210,"text":"In a frantic rush to fix the broken bridge before the monsoon, the village engineer shouted at the contractors, 'Stop! You are trying to ___________ by using these temporary bamboo poles!' He believed they were attempting to make the river flow through a solid wall of wood.\nWhich idiom best completes the engineer's frustrated outburst?\nA. paint the town red\nB. build castles in the air\nC. count chickens before they hatch\nD. throw good money after bad","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A. paint the town red: Celebrate wildly."},{"label":"B","text":"B. build castles in the air: Engage in unrealistic planning or hope."},{"label":"C","text":"C. count chickens before they hatch: Expect results prematurely."},{"label":"D","text":"D. throw good money after bad: Persist in a failing course despite losses."}],"answer":1,"solution":"The engineer is frustrated because the contractors are using temporary, flimsy bamboo poles to solve a structural crisis that requires permanent concrete foundations. They are relying on an illusion of strength (a 'castle') built on an unstable foundation ('in the air'). Option A refers to celebration. Option C refers to premature expectation of profit. Option D refers to financial persistence. Only Option B captures the essence of constructing something grand or functional based on a delusion or insufficient means."},{"id":1211,"text":"Even though the committee members insisted that the report ______ before the monsoon floods submerged the village, no one could decide which of them ______ to sign first.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"was finished / dared"},{"label":"B","text":"be finished / dared"},{"label":"C","text":"is finished / dares"},{"label":"D","text":"were finished / dare"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. The main clause subject is 'no one' (singular), so the second blank must take a singular verb: 'dared'. \n2. This eliminates options C and D immediately.\n3. For the first blank, we have an embedded clause within a 'that-clause' functioning as the object of 'insisted'. \n4. In formal exam grammar (like IBPS/SSC), when the main verb is in the past tense ('insisted'), the subordinate clause typically maintains past tense consistency or uses the subjunctive if hypothetical.\n5. 'Insisted that X was done' implies a specific state of completion demanded at that time.\n6. 'Be finished' (subjunctive) is grammatically possible but less common in standard Indian competitive exams unless the context explicitly demands a hypothetical ('insisted that he be present').\n7. Here, the focus is on the factual report status relative to the past timeline of the flood threat; thus, simple past 'was finished' fits the narrative flow better than subjunctive 'be finished'.\n8. Option A provides the standard past tense agreement for both clauses."},{"id":1212,"text":"Read the following sentence and identify the part containing the error (marked as A, B, C, D). If no error is found, select E.\n\n'The project manager decided to launch the initiative next week after the stakeholders had already signed the agreement.'\n(A) The project manager decided to launch the initiative next week\n(B) after the stakeholders had already signed the agreement\n(C) (No error)\n(D) if any\n(E) None of these","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A"},{"label":"B","text":"B"},{"label":"C","text":"C"},{"label":"D","text":"D"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. The phrase 'had already signed' implies the action was completed in the past.\n2. The phrase 'next week' implies a future time relative to now.\n3. An agreement cannot be 'already signed' before the project manager decides to launch it 'next week' unless there is a specific timeline context missing.\n4. The error is the tense contradiction: 'had already signed' (Past Perfect) vs 'decided... next week' (Future). The sequence is illogical without rephrasing B to 'sign' or changing 'next week'.\n5. Option B contains the logical flaw regarding time sequence."},{"id":1213,"text":"Read the following sentence and select the most appropriate idiom to fill the blank, ensuring the phrase's figurative meaning aligns with the context of a sudden financial collapse:\n\"After years of steady growth, the startup's value crashed overnight when the market ____, leaving investors in deep trouble.\"\nA) blew up\nB) folded its tents\nC) hit bottom\nD) turned sour","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) blew up"},{"label":"B","text":"B) folded its tents"},{"label":"C","text":"C) hit bottom"},{"label":"D","text":"D) turned sour"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Analyze the context: A sudden financial collapse or withdrawal of investment.\n2. Evaluate Option A ('blew up'): Means an explosion or angry outburst; implies destruction but not retreat.\n3. Evaluate Option C ('hit bottom'): Refers to a low point in value, not a departure.\n4. Evaluate Option D ('turned sour'): Refers to deteriorating quality or attitude, not leaving.\n5. Evaluate Option B ('folded its tents'): Originating from travelers setting up camp and packing away tents to leave quickly; metaphorically means to retreat or withdraw suddenly.\n6. Conclusion: 'Folded its tents' fits the context of investors withdrawing their capital abruptly."},{"id":1214,"text":"In the context of a heated debate on urban planning where architects insisted that 'greenery should be treated as concrete infrastructure' to ensure survival, which idiom best captures the speaker's view that nature is not just decorative but essential for structural stability?\n\nA) Green is green\nB) It's the little things\nC) The grass is always greener\nD) A bird in the hand","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) Green is green"},{"label":"B","text":"B) It's the little things"},{"label":"C","text":"C) The grass is always greener"},{"label":"D","text":"D) A bird in the hand"}],"answer":0,"solution":"The phrase 'Green is green' is a metaphorical literalism implying that something fundamental (like nature/greenery) retains its intrinsic value and necessity regardless of external opinions or trends, mirroring the speaker's insistence on treating greenery as essential infrastructure. Option C implies envy of others' better situations, B suggests minor details are important but not foundational, and D advises against taking unnecessary risks; none capture the 'essential nature' concept as directly as the literal metaphor."},{"id":1215,"text":"In a hypothetical economic scenario where the government's primary goal is to maximize rural employment immediately following a drought, which phrase best completes the sentence: 'The administration decided that ______ the monsoon forecasts remain uncertain, the public works department would prioritize local labor allocation over automated machinery deployment.'?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A] as long as"},{"label":"B","text":"B] even if"},{"label":"C","text":"C] provided that"},{"label":"D","text":"D] unless"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The stem describes a situation requiring action (prioritizing labor) despite a negative condition (uncertain monsoon). 'Even if' introduces the concession that the uncertainty exists, making the decision valid regardless of it. 'As long as', 'provided that', and 'unless' imply conditions that must be met or avoided, which contradicts the logic of acting *despite* the risk mentioned in the context."},{"id":1216,"text":"Select the option that best completes the sentence: \n'The new government policy is a __________ for small businesses, as it provides essential financial support to keep them from collapsing during the economic downturn.'\nOptions:\nA) A lifeline\nB) A tightrope\nC) A stepping-stone\nD) A dead-end","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) A lifeline"},{"label":"B","text":"B) A tightrope"},{"label":"C","text":"C) A stepping-stone"},{"label":"D","text":"D) A dead-end"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. The sentence describes a policy providing 'essential financial support' to prevent collapse.\n2. 'Lifeline' metaphorically means a line thrown to someone in peril, fitting the context of saving businesses.\n3. 'Tightrope' implies danger and balance, contradicting the supportive nature of the aid.\n4. 'Stepping-stone' suggests moving forward/upward, not necessarily preventing collapse from below.\n5. 'Dead-end' implies a negative outcome or lack of progress, which is incorrect.\n6. Only 'lifeline' logically fits the metaphor of saving something drowning (collapsing).\n7. Therefore, Option A is the correct choice."}]},{"name":"Reasoning","count":52,"questions":[{"id":885,"text":"The National Institutional Ranking Framework (NIRF) was approved by the MHRD and introduced by the Honourable Minister of Human Resource Development on 29th September 2015. As per the NIRF&#39;s &quot;India Rankings 2023&quot;, which one of the following has been mat ched incorrectly: 1. Top performing University: IISc Bengaluru 2. Top performing College: St. Stephens 3. Top performing institute in Overall Category: IIT Madras","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2 only"},{"label":"B","text":"1 and 2 only"},{"label":"C","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":886,"text":"Identify which among the following statement is/are correct about interest rate and bond price? 1. Interest rate is negatively related to bond prices. 2. If interest rate and yield is rising bond prices will fall. 3. Interest rate positively related to bond prices.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 1 and 2"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 2 and 3"},{"label":"D","text":"All 1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":904,"text":"NTPC Limited, India&#39;s largest power generation company, has climbed 52 positions to secure the 433rd rank in Forbes&#39; “The Global 2000” List for 2023. Which of these is/are not the parameters taken into account for determining Forbes 2000 ranking of the top public companies in the world?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Goodwill"},{"label":"B","text":"Sales"},{"label":"C","text":"Profits"},{"label":"D","text":"Assets"},{"label":"E","text":"Market value"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":928,"text":"Consider the following statements about the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBS) 2016, and find out the correct statement – 1. These Regulations shall apply to the corporate insolvency resolution process. 2. An insolvency professional shall be eligible to be appointed as a resolution professional for a corporate insolvency resolution process of a corporate debtor. 3. A resolution professional shall make disclosures at the time of his appointment and thereafter in accordance with the Code of Conduct.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 2"},{"label":"B","text":"2 and 3"},{"label":"C","text":"1 and 2"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":987,"text":"In a certain code, &#39;FLOWER&#39; is written as &#39;649537&#39; and &#39;WONDER&#39; is written as &#39;539278&#39;. How is &#39;REFLOW&#39; coded?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"729645"},{"label":"B","text":"785649"},{"label":"C","text":"789645"},{"label":"D","text":"789465"}],"answer":2,"solution":"By comparing the letters and their corresponding codes in &#39;FLOWER&#39; and &#39;WONDER&#39;, we can deduce the code for each letter. R=7, E=8, F=6, L=4, O=9, W=5. Therefore, &#39;REFLOW&#39; would be coded as 789645."},{"id":999,"text":"Which of these statement is/are correct about the PM SVANidhi scheme? 1. The Scheme has been extended till 2024. 2. The approval is expected to benefit nearly 1.2 crore citizens of Urban India. 3. The loan amount under the scheme has increased the loan amount to Rs. 10000 crore","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1 and 2 only"},{"label":"B","text":"1 and 3 only"},{"label":"C","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1001,"text":"TRAI in its endeavor to curb menace of spams through Unsolicited Commercial Communication (UCC) has taken various measures in the recent past. In recent news, (June 2023), TRAI has now issued a Direction to all the Access Providers to develop and deploy the DCA facility for creating a unified platform and process to register customers consent digitally across all service providers and Principal Entities. What does &quot;DCA&quot; stand for?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Digital Consent Acquisition"},{"label":"B","text":"Data Consent Acquisition"},{"label":"C","text":"Digital Content Acquisition"},{"label":"D","text":"Data Content Acquisition"},{"label":"E","text":"Digital Communication Acquisition"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1014,"text":"The World Bank has scrapped Ease of Doing Business and declared a new replacement annual series which will reflect a more balanced and transparent approach toward evaluating a country&#39;s business and investment climate. What is the name of the new rep lacement annual series?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ease Business"},{"label":"B","text":"Business PRO"},{"label":"C","text":"Easy Business"},{"label":"D","text":"Business Ready"},{"label":"E","text":"Business PORT"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1022,"text":"A bat and a ball together cost Rs. 100. The bat costs Rs. 20 more than the ball. How much does the ball cost?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 40"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 50"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 60"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 70"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Let&#39;s say the ball costs x. The bat costs x + 20. The total cost is x + (x + 20) = 100. Simplifying the equation, we get 2x + 20 = 100. Subtracting 20 from both sides, we get 2x = 80. Dividing both sides by 2, we get x = 40."},{"id":1025,"text":"NTPC Limited, India&#39;s largest power generation company, has climbed 52 positions to secure the 433rd rank in Forbes&#39; &quot;The Global 2000&quot; List for 2023. Which of these is/are not the parameters taken into account for determining Forbes 2000 ranking of the top public companies in the world?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Goodwill"},{"label":"B","text":"Sales"},{"label":"C","text":"Profits"},{"label":"D","text":"Assets"},{"label":"E","text":"Market value"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1079,"text":"The National Institutional Ranking Framework (NIRF) was approved by the MHRD and introduced by the Honourable Minister of Human Resource Development on 29th September 2015. As per the NIRF&#39;s &quot;India Rankings 2023&quot;, which one of the following has been mat ched incorrectly: 1. Top performing University: IISc Bengaluru 2. Top performing College: St. Stephens 3. Top performing institute in Overall Category: IIT Madras","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2 only"},{"label":"B","text":"1 and 2 only"},{"label":"C","text":"2 and 3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1081,"text":"Identify which among the following statement is/are correct about interest rate and bond price? 1. Interest rate is negatively related to bond prices. 2. If interest rate and yield is rising bond prices will fall. 3. Interest rate positively related to bond prices.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1 and 3"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 1 and 2"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 2 and 3"},{"label":"D","text":"All 1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1087,"text":"In a certain code, &#39;FLOWER&#39; is written as &#39;649537&#39; and &#39;WONDER&#39; is written as &#39;539278&#39;. How is &#39;REFLOW&#39; coded?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"729645"},{"label":"B","text":"785649"},{"label":"C","text":"789645"},{"label":"D","text":"789465"}],"answer":2,"solution":"By comparing the letters and their corresponding codes in &#39;FLOWER&#39; and &#39;WONDER&#39;, we can deduce the code for each letter. R=7, E=8, F=6, L=4, O=9, W=5. Therefore, &#39;REFLOW&#39; would be coded as 789645."},{"id":1093,"text":"If it takes 5 machines 5 minutes to make 5 widgets, how long would it take 100 machines to make 100 widgets?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5 minutes"},{"label":"B","text":"50 minutes"},{"label":"C","text":"100 minutes"},{"label":"D","text":"500 minutes"}],"answer":0,"solution":"If 5 machines can make 5 widgets in 5 minutes, then 1 machine can make 1 widget in 5 minutes. Therefore, 100 machines can make 100 widgets in 5 minutes."},{"id":1112,"text":"In a family, A is the father of B. C is the brother of D. E is the sister of F. G is the son of H. If A, B, and C are all deceased, and only their direct descendants (children) remain alive to inherit from them, who among F or G stands in a relationship with D such that they could be considered 'siblings' to each other under this specific inheritance scenario? (Note: Assume standard biological relations unless implied otherwise by the death conditions).","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A. F and D are half-siblings."},{"label":"B","text":"B. G and D are full siblings."},{"label":"C","text":"C. F and G are step-siblings."},{"label":"D","text":"D. Neither F nor G is a sibling of D."}],"answer":3,"solution":"1. Identify family unit 1: A (Father) -> B (Child). C is not explicitly linked to A/B, so they are distinct unless stated. C and D are siblings.\n2. Identify family unit 2: E and F are sisters.\n3. Identify family unit 3: G is the son of H.\n4. Analyze links: There is no information linking A's line with C's line or E/F's line or H's line.\n5. The condition 'A, B, C deceased' affects inheritance distribution within their lines but does not create biological relations between distinct family groups described separately.\n6. Therefore, F (sister of E) and G (son of H) have no defined connection to D (sibling of C).\n7. Without a connecting parent figure shared by these groups, no sibling relationship exists between F or G and D."},{"id":1115,"text":"Identify the next number in the series: 2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"42"},{"label":"B","text":"44"},{"label":"C","text":"46"},{"label":"D","text":"48"}],"answer":0,"solution":"The differences between consecutive terms are 4, 6, 8, 10. The next difference should be 12. Adding 12 to the last term (30) gives 42."},{"id":1116,"text":"Arrange the following words in dictionary order: 1. Apple, 2. Apricot, 3. Ant, 4. Arm.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"3, 1, 2, 4"},{"label":"B","text":"3, 4, 1, 2"},{"label":"C","text":"1, 3, 4, 2"},{"label":"D","text":"2, 3, 1, 4"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Comparing first letters: 'Ant' (A-n), 'Apple' (A-p), 'Apricot' (A-p-r). 'n' comes before 'p', so Ant is first. Between Apple and Apricot, 'pp' vs 'pr', 'p' comes before 'r'. So Apple then Apricot. Then Arm. Order: Ant, Apple, Apricot, Arm."},{"id":1117,"text":"Identify the odd one out:","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Breeze"},{"label":"B","text":"Storm"},{"label":"C","text":"Hurricane"},{"label":"D","text":"Gale"}],"answer":0,"solution":"'Breeze', 'Storm', 'Hurricane', and 'Gale' are types of winds. However, a 'Breeze' is a light wind, while the others (Storm, Hurricane, Gale) are strong or violent winds causing significant weather disturbance."},{"id":1118,"text":"A spy starts at a secure point 'X' facing North. His mission requires him to execute the following sequence of commands relative to his CURRENT direction, where every command rotates his internal compass by 90 degrees clockwise AFTER execution:\n1. Move forward 5 units.\n2. Turn Left (relative to current face) and move forward 5 units.\n3. Turn Right (relative to current face) and move forward 5 units.\n4. Turn Left (relative to current face) and move forward 5 units.\n\nHowever, due to a magnetic anomaly affecting Sector X, every time the spy executes a command that involves turning LEFT, his body rotates an additional 90 degrees clockwise immediately after the turn but BEFORE moving. If he turns RIGHT normally, no such rotation occurs.\n\nAfter completing all 4 steps, in which cardinal direction is the spy facing?\nA) North\nB) South\nC) East\nD) West","options":[{"label":"A","text":"North"},{"label":"B","text":"South"},{"label":"C","text":"East"},{"label":"D","text":"West"}],"answer":2,"solution":"Start: Facing North. Step 1 (Forward): Still facing North. Step 2 (Turn Left relative to North -> West; Magnetic anomaly adds +90 deg clockwise due to 'Left' turn command). New orientation: West rotated by +90 deg = North. Move 5 units while facing North. Step 3 (Turn Right relative to current North -> East). No anomaly for 'Right'. Orientation remains East. Move 5 units while facing East. Step 4 (Turn Left relative to East -> North; Magnetic anomaly adds +90 deg clockwise due to 'Left' turn command). New orientation: North rotated by +90 deg = East. Move 5 units. Final Facing Direction: East."},{"id":1136,"text":"In a family, A is the brother of B. C is the father of A and D. If E is the daughter of D, who is the grandfather of E?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A"},{"label":"B","text":"C"},{"label":"C","text":"B"},{"label":"D","text":"D"}],"answer":1,"solution":"C is the father of A and D, so C is D's father. E is D's daughter, so C is E's grandfather."},{"id":1141,"text":"In a specific code language used for railway signaling, the position of letters in a word is shifted based on their distance from the center. For words with an even number of letters (4 letters), the letter at index 1 moves to index 4, and the letter at index 2 moves to index 3 (swapping the first pair). The second pair (indices 3 and 4) also swaps places (index 3 goes to 4, index 4 goes to 3). This creates a mirror swap across the vertical midline. Using this 'Inverse-Coordinate Flip' logic for 4-letter words, if 'TRAIN' becomes 'NARIT', how is 'MADRAS' coded?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"ATAD"},{"label":"B","text":"DAT A"},{"label":"C","text":"ADTA"},{"label":"D","text":"TADA"}],"answer":0,"solution":"The rule reverses a four-letter word: positions 1 and 4 swap, and positions 2 and 3 swap. DATA becomes ATAD."},{"id":1146,"text":"If today is Monday, what was the day 473 days ago?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Wednesday"},{"label":"B","text":"Thursday"},{"label":"C","text":"Tuesday"},{"label":"D","text":"Monday"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Divide the total days (473) by 7 to find full weeks.\n2. Calculation: 473 ÷ 7 = 67 weeks with a remainder of 4 days.\n3. Since we are going backwards, subtract the remainder from 'Monday'.\n4. Monday - 1 day = Sunday; - 2 days = Saturday; - 3 days = Friday; - 4 days = Thursday.\n5. The year's leap status does not affect day calculation as it depends purely on the modulo arithmetic of 7."},{"id":1148,"text":"Point A is at 12 o'clock on a clock face. If you start walking from the center towards A, then make a sharp 'Right' turn (90 degrees), which direction are you now facing relative to the clock's frame?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"3 o'clock position"},{"label":"B","text":"6 o'clock position"},{"label":"C","text":"9 o'clock position"},{"label":"D","text":"12 o'clock position"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Initial movement is from center towards 12 o'clock (North). 2. A 'Right' turn of 90 degrees rotates the heading 90 degrees clockwise. 3. North + 90 deg Right = East. 4. On a clock face, East corresponds exactly to the 3 o'clock position."},{"id":1149,"text":"Find the missing term in the series: 10, 23, 46, 87, ?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"154"},{"label":"B","text":"171"},{"label":"C","text":"189"},{"label":"D","text":"188"}],"answer":2,"solution":"Each term is doubled and the sum of its digits is added: 10 x 2 + (1 + 0) = 23; 23 x 2 + (2 + 3) = 46; 46 x 2 + (4 + 6) = 87; 87 x 2 + (8 + 7) = 189."},{"id":1152,"text":"Find the next term in the series: 5, 9, 13, 17, ?, 25 (where digits are values in base-10, but the pattern follows Base-12 arithmetic rules where any digit exceeding 9 wraps around to letters A-E representing 10-14).","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) 21"},{"label":"B","text":"B) 21A"},{"label":"C","text":"C) 21E"},{"label":"D","text":"D) 21F"}],"answer":0,"solution":"The series is an arithmetic progression starting at 5 with a common difference of 4: 5, 9 (5+4), 13 (9+4), 17 (13+4). The next term is 17 + 4 = 21. Although the prompt mentions Base-12 rules as a potential trap, standard integer addition applies here as no digit exceeds 9 in the sequence up to this point."},{"id":1153,"text":"In a certain community, all 'Kartars' are also 'Yogis'. No 'Yogi' is a 'Vedantist'. Some 'Vedantists' are 'Brahmins'. What must be true?\nI. All Kartars are Brahmins.\nII. No Kartar is a Vedantist.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only I follows"},{"label":"B","text":"Only II follows"},{"label":"C","text":"Both I and II follow"},{"label":"D","text":"Neither I nor II follows"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Draw circle 'Kartar' entirely inside 'Yogi'.\n2. Draw circle 'Vedantist' entirely outside 'Yogi' (since no Yogi is Vedantist).\n3. Conclude: Since Kartar is a subset of Yogi, and Yogi excludes Vedantist, Kartar must exclude Vedantist. Thus II follows.\n4. There is no relationship defined between 'Kartar' and 'Brahmin' directly; the link is broken by 'Vedantist'.\n5. Therefore, statement I cannot be deduced as necessarily true."},{"id":1154,"text":"In a certain code language, words are encoded based on the sum of their digits. The rule is: If a number's digit-sum (repeatedly adding digits until a single digit is obtained) is odd, write the letter corresponding to that sum (A=1, B=2... Z=26). If even, write the word 'EVE'.\nExample: \n'7' -> 7 (Odd) -> G\n'8' -> 8 (Even) -> EVE\n'5' -> 5 (Odd) -> E\n'4' -> 4 (Even) -> EVE\nWhat is the code for the number 29?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A"},{"label":"B","text":"I"},{"label":"C","text":"EVE"},{"label":"D","text":"K"}],"answer":2,"solution":"Step 1: Sum digits of 29 = 2 + 9 = 11.\nStep 2: Since 11 > 9, repeat process: 1 + 1 = 2.\nStep 3: Final single digit is 2.\nStep 4: 2 is Even.\nStep 5: Apply rule for even -> Code is 'EVE'."},{"id":1157,"text":"Complete the series: 24, 36, 54, 81, 121.5, ?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"160"},{"label":"B","text":"170"},{"label":"C","text":"180"},{"label":"D","text":"182.25"}],"answer":3,"solution":"Each term is multiplied by 1.5: 24 x 1.5 = 36, 36 x 1.5 = 54, 54 x 1.5 = 81, 81 x 1.5 = 121.5, 121.5 x 1.5 = 182.25."},{"id":1159,"text":"A spy, Agent X, starts at point O facing North. He moves 20m forward, turns 90° Left, walks 15m, then turns 90° Left again and walks 20m. Finally, he turns 90° Left one more time and walks 15m to reach a hidden vault. If the Sun is at his back as he enters the vault, in which cardinal direction did Agent X originally face while walking along the LAST segment of his path?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) North"},{"label":"B","text":"B) South"},{"label":"C","text":"C) West"},{"label":"D","text":"D) East"}],"answer":3,"solution":"1. Start facing North. 2. Move 20m forward (Path 1). 3. Turn 90° Left -> Face West. Walk 15m (Path 2). 4. Turn 90° Left -> Face South. Walk 20m (Path 3). 5. Turn 90° Left -> Face East. Walk 15m (Path 4, the last segment). 6. Therefore, Agent X was facing East while walking along the last segment."},{"id":1161,"text":"In a specific code language used for railway safety alerts, dates are encoded such that the letter corresponds to the sum of the Day's position in the month and its alphabetical value (A=1, B=2...), then converted back to a single letter based on the remainder when divided by 26. If the sum is > 26, subtract 26 once. Note: Only dates where the resulting letter is 'M' or later are considered valid alerts. On 10th March, an alert code is generated as 'L'. What date generates the alert code 'Q' under the same rules?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) 13th April"},{"label":"B","text":"B) 20th May"},{"label":"C","text":"C) 17th June"},{"label":"D","text":"D) 15th July"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Let day = d, month position in year (Jan=1...Mar=3). \nCode Letter Q is the 17th letter of alphabet.\nFormula: (d + Month_Pos) % 26 = Q_Val. If result > 26, subtract 26.\nCheck Option A (13th April): April is month 4. Day=13.\nSum = 13 + 4 = 17.\nLetter for 17 is 'Q'. Matches."},{"id":1175,"text":"In a secret code used by the Railway Safety Wing, words are encoded based on their reverse causal function. For example: 'Stop' is encoded as 'Go' (the opposite action), 'Dark' is encoded as 'Light', and 'Win' is encoded as 'Lose'. Using this logic, how would 'Sleep' be encoded?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rest"},{"label":"B","text":"Wake"},{"label":"C","text":"Tiredness"},{"label":"D","text":"Bed"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The pattern is strictly Anti-Synonym (Action) reversal. Stop <-> Go, Dark <-> Light, Win <-> Lose. The word 'Sleep' describes a state of rest; its direct functional opposite action is to 'Wake'. Options A and C are states related to sleep, while D is the object."},{"id":1176,"text":"In a rural village of Madhya Pradesh, the community council maps social connections as directional vectors relative to the Village Hall (Origin). Known relations:\n1. Ramu is 40 meters EAST of the Hall.\n2. Meera is 30 meters NORTH of Ramu.\n3. Aarav stands exactly midway between Ramu and Meera.\n\nLater, a storm forces everyone to walk along the line connecting their current position and the Village Hall in a straight path (shortest route). After walking this shortest distance, who will be standing closest to the Village Hall?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Meera"},{"label":"B","text":"Aarav"},{"label":"C","text":"Ramu"},{"label":"D","text":"None of them"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Plot positions: Ramu (40E), Meera (40E, 30N). \n2. Aarav is midway: Pos = (40/2, 30/2) = (20E, 15N). \n3. Calculate shortest path to Hall (0,0) as distance: \n   - Ramu distance = sqrt(40² + 0²) = 40m.\n   - Meera distance = sqrt(40² + 30²) = 50m.\n   - Aarav distance = sqrt(20² + 15²) = sqrt(400+225) = sqrt(625) = 25m.\n4. Shortest path implies walking directly to origin. \n5. Comparison: 25m < 40m < 50m. Aarav is closest."},{"id":1177,"text":"In a corporate hierarchy where rank is determined by strict rules: (1) No employee of 'Grade X' can supervise an employee of 'Grade Y' unless they are in the same department. (2) An employee of 'Grade X' and an employee of 'Grade Y' are never in the same department if they work on different projects. (3) Supervision implies a direct project linkage. If it is known that Employee A supervises Employee B, and both have ranks corresponding to Grade X and Grade Y respectively, which of the following conclusions about their working conditions must be true?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are in the same department and work on the same project."},{"label":"B","text":"They are in different departments but work on the same project."},{"label":"C","text":"They are in the same department and work on different projects."},{"label":"D","text":"They are in different departments and work on different projects."}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Condition (1) requires them to be in the same department for A to supervise B.\n2. Condition (3) states supervision implies a direct project linkage, meaning they must share the same project.\n3. Condition (2) creates a hypothetical constraint: if they were on different projects, they could not be in the same department. Since we established they are in the same department from step 1, the premise of condition (2) regarding 'different projects' must be false for them to remain in the same department.\n4. Therefore, to satisfy all conditions while maintaining the supervision hierarchy, they must be in the same department and working on the same project."},{"id":1185,"text":"In a specific cipher code, words are mapped to their directional 'Shadow Codes'. The rule is derived from the first letter of the word: if the first letter is in the set {A, B, C}, the shadow points North-East (NE); if in {D, E, F}, South-West (SW); if in {G, H, I}, South-East (SE); and so on, repeating this cycle every three letters. Additionally, words with exactly 3 vowels are appended with 'Long', those with 4 vowels with 'Short', and others get the suffix '-'. Given: 'CART' -> NE-Long, 'BIRD' -> NE-Low, 'POTATO' -> SW-Swift. What is the code for the word 'GARDEN'?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"SE-Swift"},{"label":"B","text":"SE-Long"},{"label":"C","text":"SW-Swift"},{"label":"D","text":"NE-Swift"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Check first letter of 'GARDEN': 'G'. 2. Map 'G' to direction cycle: A,B,C=NE; D,E,F=SW; G,H,I=SE. Thus, Direction = SE. 3. Count vowels in 'GARDEN' (A, E, E) = 3 vowels. 4. Rule for 3 vowels is suffix 'Swift'. 5. Combine: SE-Swift."},{"id":1186,"text":"In a specific logic-gate language, the symbols represent operations as follows:\n'+' means 'is less than or equal to'\n'-\nmeans 'is greater than'\n'*' means 'is not equal to'\n'/\nmeans 'is exactly equal to'\n'The statements below are true in this language:\nI. A + B (A <= B)\nII. B - C (B > C)\nIII. D / B\nIV. E * A (E != A)\nGiven these, which of the following conclusions MUST be true?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A < C and D < E"},{"label":"B","text":"D > C and E < A"},{"label":"C","text":"D >= C and E != A"},{"label":"D","text":"Data Inadequate"}],"answer":2,"solution":"1. Translate statements: I(A<=B), II(B>C), III(D=B), IV(E!=A).\n2. Combine I & II via B: Since A<=B and B>C, we have A<=B>C. No direct relation between A and C.\n3. Substitute III into chain: D=B. Thus A<=D>C. Therefore D>=C is logically valid (since B>=C implies D>=C).\n4. Analyze IV with substitution: E!=A. No fixed inequality exists between E and A, so 'E < A' or 'E > A' cannot be determined.\n5. Evaluate options: Option C states 'D >= C and E != A'. This matches our derived facts perfectly."},{"id":1188,"text":"In the formal register of Indian Bureaucracy, specific verbs denote official actions with strict procedural connotations: 'Sanction' is to approval as 'Cognizance' is to …?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"a) Accepting a legal case for trial"},{"label":"B","text":"b) Issuing a travel pass"},{"label":"C","text":"c) Denying a leave application"},{"label":"D","text":"d) Filing a criminal complaint"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Analyze the first pair: 'Sanction' in bureaucracy strictly means granting official approval.\n2. Identify the register of the second word: 'Cognizance' is a technical term used by courts/police.\n3. Apply the meaning: To 'take cognizance' means a court formally acknowledges receipt of a case and accepts jurisdiction over it.\n4. Compare options: Option (a) defines accepting a legal case, matching the formal definition of taking cognizance."},{"id":1189,"text":"A train engineer observes a specific rule for speed adjustments based on the type of station passed: If the station has an odd number of platforms, add 10 km/h; if even, subtract 5 km/h. Starting at Station X (3 platforms) traveling at 60 km/h, the train passes 4 subsequent stations before reaching the final destination. The sequence of platform counts is 2, 5, 4, and 3 respectively. What is the speed of the train upon reaching the final destination?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) 65 km/h"},{"label":"B","text":"B) 50 km/h"},{"label":"C","text":"C) 70 km/h"},{"label":"D","text":"D) 85 km/h"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Start: 60 km/h. Station 1 (2 platforms, even): -5 -> 55. Station 2 (5 platforms, odd): +10 -> 65. Station 3 (4 platforms, even): -5 -> 60. Station 4 (3 platforms, odd): +10 -> 70. Destination reached at 70 km/h."},{"id":1191,"text":"Identify the next term in the series: 15, 22, 33, 48, 67, ?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"88"},{"label":"B","text":"90"},{"label":"C","text":"92"},{"label":"D","text":"95"}],"answer":0,"solution":"The differences between terms are 7, 11, 15, 19 (increasing by 4). The next difference is 23. 67 + 23 = 88."},{"id":1192,"text":"A and B are siblings. C is the father of B. D is the mother of A. E is the son of D. Who is E to C?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Son"},{"label":"B","text":"Grandson"},{"label":"C","text":"Brother"},{"label":"D","text":"Nephew"}],"answer":0,"solution":"D is the mother of A, so D is also the mother of B (since A and B are siblings). C is the father of B, so C is married to D. E is the son of D, which makes E the son of C."},{"id":1194,"text":"In a certain code language, 'CAT' is written as '3120'. What is the code for 'DOG'?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"4157"},{"label":"B","text":"4150"},{"label":"C","text":"3157"},{"label":"D","text":"4158"}],"answer":0,"solution":"C=3, A=1, T=20. D=4, O=15, G=7. So DOG is 4157."},{"id":1196,"text":"If you walk 10 km North, turn left and walk 5 km, then turn right and walk 10 km, how far are you from the starting point?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5 km"},{"label":"B","text":"10 km"},{"label":"C","text":"15 km"},{"label":"D","text":"20 km"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Start North 10. Left is West 5. Left is South 10. Net displacement is 5 km West. Distance from start is 5 km."},{"id":1198,"text":"Arrange the following words in a logical sequence: 1. Egg, 2. Chicken, 3. Bird, 4. Baby","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1, 2, 4, 3"},{"label":"B","text":"1, 4, 2, 3"},{"label":"C","text":"4, 1, 2, 3"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 3, 4, 2"}],"answer":1,"solution":"An egg hatches into a baby chicken (chick), which grows into a chicken, which is a type of bird. Sequence: 1, 4, 2, 3."},{"id":1205,"text":"In the village of Panchavati, a peculiar inheritance rule dictates that property passes NOT to the son, but to the maternal aunt of the heir. Consider the family: A is B's brother. C is D's daughter. E is F's only child and E is also the maternal aunt of G. If the property owner is H, who is J's son, and we know that I is H's wife and K is L's mother, identify the relationship between M (who is N's only daughter) and H, given that M is the one who inherits from H. How is M related to H?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"M is H's daughter."},{"label":"B","text":"M is H's sister."},{"label":"C","text":"M is H's maternal aunt."},{"label":"D","text":"M is H's wife."}],"answer":2,"solution":"1. M inherits from H, so M must be H's maternal aunt per the rule.\n2. The rule defines 'maternal aunt' as the mother of H's mother.\n3. Therefore, M is the sister of H's mother.\n4. This makes M the maternal aunt of H."},{"id":1207,"text":"In the city of Varanasi, a new digital tax rule applies to vehicle license numbers: for any digit in the even positions (2nd, 4th, etc.) that is greater than 5, swap it with its mirror image across 5 (e.g., 6 becomes 4, 7 becomes 3). However, if the sum of digits in positions 1 and 3 equals 8, this rule does not apply to those specific digits. What is the resulting sequence after applying these rules to the number 5274?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5274"},{"label":"B","text":"5474"},{"label":"C","text":"5234"},{"label":"D","text":"5276"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Identify positions: Pos1=5, Pos2=2, Pos3=7, Pos4=4.\n2. Check swap condition for even positions (Pos2, Pos4).\n3. Pos2=2 (<=5), no swap needed.\n4. Pos4=4 (<=5), no swap needed.\n5. Check exception: Sum of Pos1 and Pos3 = 5+7=10.\n6. Since sum is not 8, the rule applies generally to even positions.\n7. However, since neither 2 nor 4 are >5, no swaps occur regardless.\n8. The number remains 5274."},{"id":1219,"text":"A person stands at the center of a circular plaza. At 12:00 PM, their shadow falls exactly towards the East, indicating the Sun is in the West (Southwest quadrant logic for this specific exam universe). They walk 5 meters North-East, turn right and walk 5 meters, then turn left and walk 5 meters. If they return to the center by walking due South-East, what was their initial facing direction relative to the clock face numbers?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) Facing 10"},{"label":"B","text":"B) Facing 2"},{"label":"C","text":"C) Facing 4"},{"label":"D","text":"D) Facing 8"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Initial Shadow East implies Sun West (Person faces North by standard assumption unless twisted).\n2. Walk NE: Position shifts NE.\n3. Turn Right (NE->SE), Walk SE: Position shifts SE relative to start.\n4. Turn Left (SE->SW), Walk SW: Position shifts SW.\n5. Return path is South-East, meaning the displacement was North-West.\n6. Net displacement from 1st leg must be cancelled by last two legs + return.\n7. The only valid configuration for the 'Return' vector to be SE implies the starting orientation relative to the shadow logic aligns with option A."},{"id":1220,"text":"A transparent sheet has a 3x3 grid of cells. The pattern inside is: Cell(1,1) has a circle; Cell(2,2) has a square; Cell(3,3) has a triangle. If you fold this flat sheet along the diagonal from top-left to bottom-right (bringing corners (1,2)-(3,4) together) and then view the front face of the resulting 3D structure, which symbol is visible in the geometric center of the front face? Options: A) Circle B) Square C) Triangle D) Empty.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Circle"},{"label":"B","text":"Square"},{"label":"C","text":"Triangle"},{"label":"D","text":"Empty"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Map grid coordinates (row, col): Circle=(1,1), Square=(2,2), Triangle=(3,3). 2. Fold along diagonal y=x (top-left to bottom-right). 3. The fold brings the upper-right half onto the lower-left half. 4. The 'front' of the folded object corresponds to the original lower-left triangle area. 5. However, the question asks for the symbol visible in the *geometric center* of the resulting face after folding. 6. When a square sheet is folded along its main diagonal, the point originally at (2,2) - the exact center of the 3x3 grid - remains exactly on the fold line and becomes the central point of the new 2D projection's surface. 7. The symbol located at (2,2) is the Square."},{"id":1222,"text":"In a specific government office protocol, the code for an action is derived by taking the literal physical direction mentioned in the sentence and applying it to the 'position' of the word 'Office' within the alphabet sequence (A=1st, B=2nd, ..., Z=26th). \n\nProtocol Rule: If a word implies a movement towards North, move the letter 'O' backward by 4 positions. If South, move forward by 4. If East, move backward by 3. If West, move forward by 5.\n\nBased on this protocol, what is the code for the phrase: 'The official must walk straight ahead'? (Note: In a standard map orientation where North is Up and South is Down, 'straight ahead' implies a neutral vertical alignment relative to the observer's view from the bottom looking up, effectively pointing 'North'.)","options":[{"label":"A","text":"K"},{"label":"B","text":"Q"},{"label":"C","text":"O"},{"label":"D","text":"R"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Step 1: Identify the key directional instruction in the phrase: 'walk straight ahead'.\nStep 2: Interpret direction: Relative to an observer facing North (standard map convention), 'straight ahead' points North.\nStep 3: Apply Protocol Rule for 'North': Move backward by 4 positions.\nStep 4: Take the target letter 'O' (15th letter).\nStep 5: Calculate new position: 15 - 4 = 11.\nStep 6: Identify the 11th letter of the alphabet: K."},{"id":1223,"text":"In a standard Cartesian grid where North is up, imagine a 'Magic Mirror' placed at the diagonal line y = -x. This mirror swaps coordinates such that any point (x, y) reflects to (-y, -x). If you stand at Point A (coordinates 3, 2) and walk towards Point B (coordinates -1, 5), then step onto the mirror exactly halfway between them, which direction does your shadow face relative to the original North-East reference frame?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"North-West"},{"label":"B","text":"South-West"},{"label":"C","text":"North-East"},{"label":"D","text":"South-East"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Calculate midpoint of A(3,2) and B(-1,5): M = ((3-1)/2, (2+5)/2) = (1, 3.5).\n2. Reflect M across y=-x using rule (-y, -x): New Pos = (-3.5, -1).\n3. Original displacement vector A->B is (-4, +3). This is North-West.\n4. Reflection of vector (-4, 3) across y=-x: Swap and negate -> (-3, 4).\n5. Vector (-3, 4) points West (negative x) and North (positive y), which is North-West."},{"id":1199,"text":"Statement: 'All employees must submit their project reports by Friday to avoid penalty.' Assumptions: I. Employees currently have pending project reports. II. Friday is the deadline for submission. Which is/are implicit?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only I"},{"label":"B","text":"Only II"},{"label":"C","text":"Both"},{"label":"D","text":"Neither"}],"answer":2,"solution":"Correct answer: Both."},{"id":1200,"text":"Situation: The city has seen a sharp rise in road accidents in the past year. Course of Action: I. Install speed cameras at all major intersections. II. Ban all private vehicles in the city. Which course(s) of action is/are appropriate?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only I"},{"label":"B","text":"Only II"},{"label":"C","text":"Both"},{"label":"D","text":"Neither"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Correct answer: Only I."},{"id":1201,"text":"Statement: 'The government should increase spending on public healthcare to improve health outcomes.' Which of the following is the strongest argument in favour?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Increased spending always leads to better outcomes"},{"label":"B","text":"Many countries with higher healthcare spending have better health indicators"},{"label":"C","text":"Private hospitals are too expensive for most people"},{"label":"D","text":"The current government has a surplus budget"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Correct answer: Many countries with higher healthcare spending have better health indicators."},{"id":1202,"text":"Passage: 'Studies show that students who participate in extracurricular activities perform better academically. Therefore, schools should mandate participation in at least one extracurricular activity.' Which of the following, if true, weakens the argument?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Extracurricular activities teach teamwork and leadership"},{"label":"B","text":"Students with better time management skills tend to join more activities"},{"label":"C","text":"Many schools lack adequate sports facilities"},{"label":"D","text":"Some students dislike extracurricular activities"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Correct answer: Students with better time management skills tend to join more activities."}]},{"name":"Quantitative Aptitude","count":48,"questions":[{"id":888,"text":"A train travels from City A to City B at a speed of 60 km/hr and returns from City B to City A at a speed of 90 km/hr. What is the average speed of the train for the entire journey?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"70 km/hr"},{"label":"B","text":"72 km/hr"},{"label":"C","text":"75 km/hr"},{"label":"D","text":"80 km/hr"}],"answer":1,"solution":"The average speed is calculated using the harmonic mean formula for two speeds over the same distance: Average Speed = 2 * (Speed1 * Speed2) / (Speed1 + Speed2). Plugging in the values: Average Speed = 2 * (60 * 90) / (60 + 90) = 2 * 5400 / 150 = 10800 / 150 = 72 km/hr."},{"id":893,"text":"The Securities and Exchange Board of India has proposed that the government should allow tax benefits to companies investing in zero coupon zero principal bonds issued by non-profit organisations listed on the Social Stock Exchange. Under this, the in vestors or donors purchasing these bonds will receive tax benefits under Section _____ of Income Tax rules.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"80D"},{"label":"B","text":"80E"},{"label":"C","text":"80F"},{"label":"D","text":"80G"},{"label":"E","text":"80H"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":898,"text":"The Securitisation and Reconstruction of Financial Assets and Enforcement of Security Interest (SARFAESI) Act, 2002 provides for the establishment of a particular type of institution to acquire and manage non -performing assets (NPAs) of banks and finan cial institutions. Which one of the following types of entities has been established under the provisions of this Act?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Asset Reconstruction Company (ARC)"},{"label":"B","text":"Asset Management Company (AMC)"},{"label":"C","text":"Asset Securitisation Fund (ASF)"},{"label":"D","text":"Debt Recovery Tribunal (DRT)"},{"label":"E","text":"Credit Information Company (CIC)"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":924,"text":"In recent news, (August 2024), the Indian government has reinstated interest subsidy under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban) 2.0 and allocated _____________ for the Credit Linked Subsidy Scheme (CLSS). The scheme, which provides subsidized home loans ba sed on income, is being implemented through three verticals: Beneficiary Led Construction/Enhancement, Affordable Housing in Partnership, and In -situ Slum Redevelopment.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 3,000 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 5,000 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 6,000 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 7,000 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 4,000 crore"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":957,"text":"Ministry of Labour and Employment has published 4 labour codes in the year 2020. These codes are aimed at protecting the interest of workers and will provide them social security, protection, safe working  environment and effective conciliation, mechanism for their grievances. Which one of the following is not one these four labour codes published by the Labour Ministry?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Code on Wages, 2019"},{"label":"B","text":"Code on Migrant Laborers , 2020"},{"label":"C","text":"Industrial Relations Code, 2020"},{"label":"D","text":"Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code, 2020"},{"label":"E","text":"Code on Social Security, 2020"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":960,"text":"Identify which among the following Scheduled Commercial Banks have recorded the highest number of new branch additions  in the financial year ended on 31st March 2023?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Yes Bank"},{"label":"B","text":"Axis Bank"},{"label":"C","text":"Bank of Baroda"},{"label":"D","text":"HDFC Bank"},{"label":"E","text":"ICICI Bank"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":967,"text":"Identify which among the following parameters has/have increased in the ASUSE Report published recently? 1. Number of establishments 2. Number of workers 3. GVA added","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both 1 &amp; 2"},{"label":"B","text":"2 only"},{"label":"C","text":"3 only"},{"label":"D","text":"Both 1 &amp; 3 only"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":968,"text":"As per the Financial Stability Report, SCBs&#39; gross non -performing assets (GNPA) ratio continued  its downtrend and fell to a __________ year low to 3.9% in March 2023 and the net non -performing assets (NNPA) ratio declined to __________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"8, 0.5%"},{"label":"B","text":"10, 1%"},{"label":"C","text":"13, 1.5%"},{"label":"D","text":"10, 1.5%"},{"label":"E","text":"8, 1%"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":971,"text":"As per the Union Budget 2023, Government has decided to continue the 50 -year interest free loan to state governments for one more year to spur capital investment and, with a significantly enhanced outlay of Rs 1.3 lakh crore, from ___________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2021 -22"},{"label":"B","text":"2025 -26"},{"label":"C","text":"2024 -25"},{"label":"D","text":"2022 -23"},{"label":"E","text":"2023 -24"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":979,"text":"There has been great excitement and a rush of positive sentiment among members of the fintech community (digital lenders), regulated lenders, and investors about the recently (June 2023) published Guidelines on Default Loss Guarantee (DLG) in Digital L ending  which were issued by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI). The Guidelines on Default Loss Guarantee (DLG) in Digital Lending is not applicable on which of the following  entities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Payment Banks"},{"label":"B","text":"Small Finance Banks"},{"label":"C","text":"State Co -operative Banks"},{"label":"D","text":"NBFC"},{"label":"E","text":"Commercial Banks"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":984,"text":"Ministry of Labour and Employment has published 4 labour codes in the year 2020. These codes are aimed at protecting the interest of workers and will provide them social security, protection, safe working  environment and effective conciliation, mechanism for their grievances. Which one of the following is not one these four labour codes published by the Labour Ministry?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Code on Wages, 2019"},{"label":"B","text":"Code on Migrant Laborers , 2020"},{"label":"C","text":"Industrial Relations Code, 2020"},{"label":"D","text":"Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code, 2020"},{"label":"E","text":"Code on Social Security, 2020"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1003,"text":"The Reserve Bank has declared a hike in cash reserve ratio (CRR) by 50 basis points to 4.5 per cent. It has been effective from _____.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"May 05, 2022"},{"label":"B","text":"May 14, 2022"},{"label":"C","text":"May 18, 2022"},{"label":"D","text":"May 21, 2022"},{"label":"E","text":"May 23, 2022"}],"answer":3,"solution":""},{"id":1010,"text":"The Securitisation and Reconstruction of Financial Assets and Enforcement of Security Interest (SARFAESI) Act, 2002 provides for the establishment of a particular type of institution to acquire and manage non -performing assets (NPAs) of banks and finan cial institutions. Which one of the following types of entities has been established under the provisions of this Act?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Asset Reconstruction Company (ARC)"},{"label":"B","text":"Asset Management Company (AMC)"},{"label":"C","text":"Asset Securitisation Fund (ASF)"},{"label":"D","text":"Debt Recovery Tribunal (DRT)"},{"label":"E","text":"Credit Information Company (CIC)"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1020,"text":"There has been great excitement and a rush of positive sentiment among members of the fintech community (digital lenders), regulated lenders, and investors about the recently (June 2023) published Guidelines on Default Loss Guarantee (DLG) in Digital L ending  which were issued by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI). The Guidelines on Default Loss Guarantee (DLG) in Digital Lending is not applicable on which of the following  entities?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Payment Banks"},{"label":"B","text":"Small Finance Banks"},{"label":"C","text":"State Co -operative Banks"},{"label":"D","text":"NBFC"},{"label":"E","text":"Commercial Banks"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1024,"text":"As per a new report by UN body World Intellectual Property Organisation (WIPO), which one of the following countries has filed the maximum number of GenAI patents?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"China"},{"label":"B","text":"South Korea"},{"label":"C","text":"Thailand"},{"label":"D","text":"Nepal"},{"label":"E","text":"South Africa"}],"answer":0,"solution":""},{"id":1026,"text":"As per the National Family Health Survey (NFHS) conducted in 2019 -21, India&#39;s sex ratio in urban areas is _____ females per every 1,000 males and  ______ females per every 1,000 males in rural areas.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"958, 984"},{"label":"B","text":"967, 997"},{"label":"C","text":"985, 1037"},{"label":"D","text":"979, 1019"},{"label":"E","text":"972, 1026"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1041,"text":"In recent news, (August 2024), the Indian government has reinstated interest subsidy under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban) 2.0 and allocated _____________ for the Credit Linked Subsidy Scheme (CLSS). The scheme, which provides subsidized home loans ba sed on income, is being implemented through three verticals: Beneficiary Led Construction/Enhancement, Affordable Housing in Partnership, and In -situ Slum Redevelopment.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 3,000 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 5,000 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 6,000 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 7,000 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 4,000 crore"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1048,"text":"As per the Union Budget 2023, Government has decided to continue the 50 -year interest free loan to state governments for one more year to spur capital investment and, with a significantly enhanced outlay of Rs 1.3 lakh crore, from ___________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2021 -22"},{"label":"B","text":"2025 -26"},{"label":"C","text":"2024 -25"},{"label":"D","text":"2022 -23"},{"label":"E","text":"2023 -24"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1067,"text":"A person invests Rs. 1000 in a savings account that earns an annual interest rate of 5%. How much will the person have in the account after 2 years?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 1102.50"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 1105"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 1110"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 1120"}],"answer":0,"solution":"The interest earned in the first year is Rs. 1000 * 5% = Rs. 50. The total amount after the first year is Rs. 1000 + Rs. 50 = Rs. 1050. The interest earned in the second year is Rs. 1050 * 5% = Rs. 52.50. The total amount after the second year is Rs. 1050 + Rs. 52.50 = Rs. 1102.50."},{"id":1083,"text":"As per the Ministry of Agriculture &amp; Farmers Welfare Annual Report 2024 -25, which of the following statements is/are correct? 1. Net sown area in India is more than half of the total geographical area. 2. Sugarcane occupies a significant area among commercial crops. 3. A major share of irrigation in India is done using tubewells.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Only 1 and 2"},{"label":"B","text":"Only 2 and 3"},{"label":"C","text":"Only 1 and 3"},{"label":"D","text":"1, 2 and 3"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1088,"text":"As per the Migration &amp; Development brief Report, in the fourth quarter of 2023, the global average costs of sending USD 200 continued to be high at 6.4 per cent, 0.2 percentage points higher than the previous year. SDG 10.C underscores the commitment of countries to reducing the transaction costs associated with migrant remittances to less than _____. This target aims to establish a global average for sending USD 200.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"5%"},{"label":"B","text":"3.5%"},{"label":"C","text":"3%"},{"label":"D","text":"2.5%"},{"label":"E","text":"1%"}],"answer":2,"solution":""},{"id":1097,"text":"As per the Financial Stability Report, SCBs&#39; gross non -performing assets (GNPA) ratio continued  its downtrend and fell to a __________ year low to 3.9% in March 2023 and the net non -performing assets (NNPA) ratio declined to __________.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"8, 0.5%"},{"label":"B","text":"10, 1%"},{"label":"C","text":"13, 1.5%"},{"label":"D","text":"10, 1.5%"},{"label":"E","text":"8, 1%"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1100,"text":"Ministry of Labour and Employment has published 4 labour codes in the year 2020. These codes are aimed at protecting the interest of workers and will provide them social security, protection, safe working  environment and effective conciliation, mechanism for their grievances. Which one of the following is not one these four labour codes published by the Labour Ministry?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Code on Wages, 2019"},{"label":"B","text":"Code on Migrant Laborers , 2020"},{"label":"C","text":"Industrial Relations Code, 2020"},{"label":"D","text":"Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code, 2020"},{"label":"E","text":"Code on Social Security, 2020"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1102,"text":"Which of these telecommunication company has joined the SEA -ME-WE- 6 undersea cable consortium to scale up its high -speed global network capacity and serve India&#39;s fast growing digital economy?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Reliance Jio"},{"label":"B","text":"Bharti Airtel"},{"label":"C","text":"Vodafone -Idea"},{"label":"D","text":"BSNL"},{"label":"E","text":"None of the above"}],"answer":1,"solution":""},{"id":1111,"text":"RBI has published a bulk  deposit limit for scheduled commercial banks, regional rural banks, small finance banks and local area banks. What is the minimum limit of the bulk deposit for the local area banks?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs 5 crore"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs 4 crore"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs 3 crore"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs 2 crore"},{"label":"E","text":"Rs 1 crore"}],"answer":4,"solution":""},{"id":1114,"text":"A shopkeeper sells a cricket bat with a marked price of ₹5,000. He offers two alternatives: Scheme A: 15% discount followed by a further 10% discount on the reduced price. Scheme B: A single flat discount of x%. To make the final selling price identical in both schemes, what is the value of x?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"25%"},{"label":"B","text":"23.5%"},{"label":"C","text":"22.5%"},{"label":"D","text":"24%"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Discount A = 15%. Remaining = 85%.\nDiscount B = 10%. Remaining = 90%.\nCombined Remaining = 85% x 90% = 0.85 x 0.90 = 0.765.\nTotal Discount = 1 - 0.765 = 0.235.\nx = 23.5%."},{"id":1126,"text":"A bank offers a special 'Festival Savings Scheme' where the interest rate for the first year is 5% per annum on the principal. However, the interest earned in the first year is added to the principal at the end of the year. If a customer deposits ₹10,000 and closes the account after exactly one year, what is the total amount received?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A) ₹10,500"},{"label":"B","text":"B) ₹10,525"},{"label":"C","text":"C) ₹10,600"},{"label":"D","text":"D) ₹10,400"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Simple Interest = (P * R * T) / 100.\nSubstituting values: P = 10000, R = 5%, T = 1 year.\nSI = (10000 * 5 * 1) / 100.\nSI = 500.\nTotal Amount = Principal + Interest = 10000 + 500 = 10500."},{"id":1132,"text":"A retailer marks up a commodity by 25% above its cost price. He then offers a discount of x% on this marked price. If the final selling price equals the original cost price plus half of the initial profit he would have made had there been no discount, what is the value of x?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10"},{"label":"B","text":"12"},{"label":"C","text":"15"},{"label":"D","text":"20"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Let Cost Price (CP) = Rs. 100.\nInitial Profit (if no discount) = Marked Price - CP = 125 - 100 = 25.\nHalf of this initial profit = 25 / 2 = 12.5.\nTarget Selling Price = CP + Half Initial Profit = 100 + 12.5 = 112.5.\nMarked Price (MP) = 125.\nDiscount Amount = MP - SP = 125 - 112.5 = 12.5.\nDiscount Percentage (x) = (Discount / MP) * 100 = (12.5 / 125) * 100 = 10%."},{"id":1135,"text":"A suburban train covers a distance of 120 km in 2 hours at its scheduled speed. On the return journey, due to signal disruptions at exactly 5 platforms encountered, the train incurs a fixed 'delay penalty' of 4 minutes for every platform passed. If the train maintains the exact same average speed between these platforms as it did on the outbound journey, how much total time is required for the entire return trip?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2 hours"},{"label":"B","text":"2 hours 10 minutes"},{"label":"C","text":"2 hours 20 minutes"},{"label":"D","text":"2 hours 30 minutes"}],"answer":2,"solution":"1. Outbound average speed = 120 km / 2 hrs = 60 km/hr.\n2. Return journey distance is also 120 km.\n3. Ideal time for return trip at 60 km/hr = 120/60 = 2 hours (120 mins).\n4. Delay penalty = 4 minutes per platform * 5 platforms = 20 minutes.\n5. Total time = Ideal time + Penalty = 120 mins + 20 mins = 140 mins."},{"id":1137,"text":"A fixed deposit scheme offers Simple Interest (SI) calculated on a daily basis. If the interest for one full year is Rs. 4,800, what will be the interest earned if the money is withdrawn after exactly one-third of that year? Assume a non-leap year.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹1,600"},{"label":"B","text":"₹2,400"},{"label":"C","text":"₹3,200"},{"label":"D","text":"₹4,800"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Total annual SI = ₹4,800. Since it is Simple Interest, the rate is constant per unit time. 1/3rd of a year yields 1/3rd of the total annual interest. Calculation: (1/3) * 4,800 = 1,600."},{"id":1147,"text":"In a government procurement tender for 'Project Yogi', the contractor declares that the total estimated Cost Price (CP) for a batch of uniforms was calculated as 80% of the total Selling Price (SP). If the final SP for the batch was Rs. 240,000, and the actual expenses incurred were: Materials (40% of CP), Labor (35% of CP), and Overheads (25% of CP), what is the amount spent on Overheads? \n\n**Note:** The 'Materials' expense was found to be under-estimated by Rs. 5,000 in the initial draft, but the question asks for the **calculated** Overhead based on the declared percentages and the given SP.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 48,000"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 53,000"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 52,000"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 60,000"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Calculate Total CP: SP (240,000) * 80% = Rs. 192,000.\n2. Identify Overhead component: Given as 25% of CP.\n3. Calculate Overhead Amount: 25% of 192,000 = (192,000 / 4) = Rs. 48,000.\n4. Note: The under-estimation info is a distractor for the specific question asking for calculated overhead."},{"id":1155,"text":"A retailer marks up a festive gift item by 40% over its cost price to sell it at a premium. However, due to post-festival inflation and supply chain delays, the final selling price ends up being exactly equal to what it would have been if the item were sold at a 15% profit on the original cost price WITHOUT any markup. What is the Cost Price of the item if the Final Selling Price was Rs. 230?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 186.50"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 200.00"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 192.40"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 210.00"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Let Cost Price = x.\nOriginal Selling Price (with 40% markup) = 1.4x.\nAlternative Selling Price (with 15% profit) = 1.15x.\nThe problem states the Final SP equals the Alternative SP, so Final SP = 1.15x.\nWe are given Final SP = Rs. 230.\nEquation: 1.15x = 230.\nCalculation: x = 230 / 1.15.\nDivision: 230 / 1.15 = 200."},{"id":1156,"text":"A trader marks up the Cost Price (CP) of a commodity by 25% to get the Marked Price (MP). He then offers a 10% discount on this MP. If the final Selling Price (SP) is Rs. 270, what is the trader's profit percentage on the CP?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"15%"},{"label":"B","text":"12.5%"},{"label":"C","text":"10%"},{"label":"D","text":"8%"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Let CP = 100.\nMP = 100 + 25% = 125.\nSP = 125 - 10% = 125 * 0.9 = 112.5.\nProfit = SP - CP = 112.5 - 100 = 12.5.\nProfit % = (12.5 / 100) * 100 = 12.5%."},{"id":1158,"text":"A confectioner sells 'Assorted Box' X (cost ₹220/kg) and 'Premium Box' Y (cost ₹320/kg). To reduce inventory of Y, he mixes 2 kg of X with 1 kg of Y to create 'Box Z'. If Box Z is sold at a 10% profit on its cost price, what is the profit percentage earned on the original cost of the 3 kg ingredients?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A: 13.33%"},{"label":"B","text":"B: 10%"},{"label":"C","text":"C: 6.67%"},{"label":"D","text":"D: 5%"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Cost of 2 kg X = 2 x 220 = 440.\nCost of 1 kg Y = 1 x 320 = 320.\nTotal Cost Price (CP) of 3 kg = 440 + 320 = 760.\nSelling Price (SP) of 3 kg = 760 x 1.10 = 836.\nProfit = SP - CP = 836 - 760 = 76.\nProfit % = (76 / 760) x 100 = 10%."},{"id":1160,"text":"In a government office, there are 5 files of 'Pending Cases' and 3 files of 'Closed Cases'. A junior officer must select exactly two files for review. The rule is: if the first file selected is 'Pending', the second MUST be 'Closed'; if the first is 'Closed', the second can be anything. If the officer picks a 'Pending' file first, what is the probability that the SECOND file selected turns out to be 'Pending' as well?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"0"},{"label":"B","text":"1/4"},{"label":"C","text":"3/8"},{"label":"D","text":"5/12"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Let P1 = Pending, C1 = Closed. Total = 8.\nP(Case 1 is P) * P(Case 2 is P | Case 1 is P) = Probability of two P.\nThe rule states: If 1st is P, 2nd MUST be C.\nTherefore, given 1st is P, probability 2nd is P is 0.\nTotal probability of (P then P) = P(P1)*0 = 0."},{"id":1183,"text":"A retailer purchases a smartwatch with a Manufacturer's List Price (MLP) of Rs. 2,000. He receives a 'trade discount' of 12% on the MLP. He then marks the price at 25% above his cost price. During a 'festival sale', he offers a 'cash discount' of 10% on the marked price. If the retailer declares that his 'net profit percentage' is calculated on the 'final selling price' rather than the cost price, what is his net profit percentage (rounded to the nearest integer)?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"11%"},{"label":"B","text":"12%"},{"label":"C","text":"13%"},{"label":"D","text":"14%"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Cost Price (CP) = 2000 * (1 - 0.12) = Rs. 1760.\n2. Marked Price (MP) = 1760 * 1.25 = Rs. 2200.\n3. Final Selling Price (SP) = 2200 * (1 - 0.10) = Rs. 1980.\n4. Profit = SP - CP = 1980 - 1760 = Rs. 220.\n5. Net Profit % on SP = (220 / 1980) * 100.\n6. 220 / 1980 = 22 / 198 = 1 / 9.\n7. (1 / 9) * 100 = 11.11%.\n8. Rounded to nearest integer = 11%."},{"id":1184,"text":"A prudent investor splits a total sum of Rs. 20,000 into two parts. Part A is invested at 6% simple interest per annum, and Part B is invested at 8% simple interest per annum. If the combined annual interest earned from both parts is exactly equal to the simple interest on the entire Rs. 20,000 invested at a blended rate of 7% per annum for one year, what is the amount invested at 6%?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 10,000"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 15,000"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 8,000"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 12,000"}],"answer":0,"solution":"1. Total Sum = Rs. 20,000.\n2. Target Interest (Target Rate) = 7% of 20,000 = Rs. 1,400.\n3. Let Part A = x (at 6%) and Part B = 20,000 - x (at 8%).\n4. Equation: 0.06x + 0.08(20,000 - x) = 1,400.\n5. Simplify: 0.06x + 1,600 - 0.08x = 1,400.\n6. Rearrange: -0.02x = -200.\n7. Solve: x = 200 / 0.02 = 10,000."},{"id":1187,"text":"An Indian Railways employee saves for a new ticket reservation system upgrade by depositing ₹2,000 at the end of each month into a Public Provident Fund (PPF) account. The bank announces an annual compound interest rate of 7.2% compounded annually. Assuming the standard PPF calculation where monthly deposits are treated as a lump sum deposited half-yearly for approximation in simplified exams, which is closest to the total maturity value after 2 years?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹48,500"},{"label":"B","text":"₹51,200"},{"label":"C","text":"₹49,300"},{"label":"D","text":"₹47,600"}],"answer":2,"solution":"1. Total principal (24 months * 2000) = ₹48,000.\n2. Simplified Interest for 2 years on recurring deposits in simplified exams approximates to roughly 2.5% of the principal over the period.\n3. Calculation: 48,000 + (48,000 * 0.025) = 48,000 + 1,200 = ₹49,200.\n4. Rounding to nearest option gives ₹49,300."},{"id":1190,"text":"A shopkeeper buys a table for ₹4,200. He spends 10% on transportation and 5% on repairs. If he sells the table at a profit of 12% on the total cost, what is his selling price?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"₹4,998"},{"label":"B","text":"₹4,830"},{"label":"C","text":"₹5,010"},{"label":"D","text":"₹4,750"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Total cost = 4200 + (10% of 4200) + (5% of 4200) = 4200 + 420 + 210 = ₹4830. Selling price at 12% profit = 4830 * 1.12 = ₹4,998."},{"id":1193,"text":"A train crosses a pole in 18 seconds. The train's speed is 72 km/h. If the train's length is increased by 120 meters, how long will it take to cross the pole?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"24 seconds"},{"label":"B","text":"30 seconds"},{"label":"C","text":"35 seconds"},{"label":"D","text":"40 seconds"}],"answer":0,"solution":"72 km/h = 72 x 5/18 = 20 m/s. In 18 s the train covers its own length: 20 x 18 = 360 m. After adding 120 m the length is 480 m, so time = 480 / 20 = 24 seconds. The other options ignore the correct speed conversion or the added length."},{"id":1195,"text":"Find the value of x if 3x + 7 = 22.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"3"},{"label":"B","text":"5"},{"label":"C","text":"7"},{"label":"D","text":"9"}],"answer":1,"solution":"3x = 22 - 7 = 15. x = 15 / 3 = 5."},{"id":1197,"text":"A basket contains 50 apples. If 20% are rotten, how many good apples are left?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"30"},{"label":"B","text":"40"},{"label":"C","text":"50"},{"label":"D","text":"20"}],"answer":1,"solution":"Rotten apples = 20% of 50 = 10. Good apples = 50 - 10 = 40."},{"id":1203,"text":"A contractor promises to complete a project in 40 days. He employs 60 men. However, due to supply shortages, the work rate of every single man drops by 25% immediately after day 20. If he wants to finish the job exactly on day 40 regardless of this slowdown, how many additional men must he hire at that moment?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"10"},{"label":"B","text":"15"},{"label":"C","text":"20"},{"label":"D","text":"25"}],"answer":2,"solution":"Initial plan: 60 men complete work in 40 days. Halfway (day 20), half the total required work is done. Remaining work needs to be done in remaining 20 days. At day 20, efficiency of each man drops by 25% (becomes 75% of original). Let original rate be R. New rate = 0.75R. Effective men count available remains 60, but their total output is 0.75 * 60 * R = 45R equivalent to 45 normal-men-days per day. Remaining work for 20 days with full efficiency would need (Total Work / 2) / 20 days? No. Original plan: Total Work W = 60 men * 40 days * R = 2400 man-days. Half done in 20 days = 1200 man-days. Remaining 1200 man-days must be done in 20 days. Current effective capacity per day with 60 men at 75% efficiency = 60 * 0.75 * R = 45R (where 1R=1 normal man-day). Days needed for current 60 men = 1200 / 45 = 26.67 days. We have only 20 days left. Deficit = 6.67 days worth of work. Required capacity per day = 1200 / 20 = 60R (equivalent to 60 normal men). Current effective capacity is 45R. Need additional 15R. Since each new man adds 0.75R efficiency, let x be number of men. Total capacity = (60 + x) * 0.75R = 60R => 45R + 0.75xR = 60R => 0.75x = 15 => x = 20."},{"id":1204,"text":"A train covers a distance of 480 km at a uniform speed. If the train had traveled 12 km/hr faster, it would have taken 4 hours less for the same journey. However, in reality, due to mechanical issues, the train stopped for 'x' minutes for every 'y' kilometers traveled, where x/y = 1/30 (i.e., 1 minute per 30 km). If the effective speed reduced by 25% because of these stops, what was the original scheduled time of the journey in hours?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"6.4"},{"label":"B","text":"7.2"},{"label":"C","text":"8.0"},{"label":"D","text":"9.6"}],"answer":2,"solution":"1. Let original speed be v km/hr. New speed = v+12. Time diff equation: 480/v - 480/(v+12) = 4.\n2. Solving gives v=60 km/hr (original speed) and new speed=72 km/hr.\n3. Original scheduled time = Distance/Speed = 480/60 = 8 hours.\n4. The problem states effective speed is reduced by 25% due to stops, making actual time longer, but the question asks for the 'original scheduled time' based on the uniform speed scenario described in the first half."},{"id":1206,"text":"A financial scheme offers a simple interest rate of $r\text{\textperthousand}$ per annum for the first $T$ years and switches to a compound interest mechanism (compounded annually) at a rate of $(20-r)\text{\textperthousand}$ for the subsequent period. A principal amount is invested such that the total interest earned over 12 years exactly equals Rs. 6480.\n\nIt is known that if the initial simple interest rate had been increased by 2 units (to $r+2$) and the switching point delayed by 1 year, while maintaining the same final compound rate logic relative to the new switch point, the total interest would remain exactly Rs. 6480.\n\nGiven that the principal amount is an integer, find the value of $T$ (the number of years for simple interest).","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A: 4"},{"label":"B","text":"B: 5"},{"label":"C","text":"C: 6"},{"label":"D","text":"D: 7"}],"answer":1,"solution":"1. Let Principal = P. Simple Rate = r%, Compound Rate = (20-r)%.\n2. Scenario 1 (Original): SI for T years + CI for (12-T) years = 6480.\n3. Scenario 2 (Perturbed): New SI Rate = (r+2)%. New Switch point = (T+1). New Comp Rate = (20 - (r+2))% = (18-r)%.\n4. Note the symmetry: The sum of rates in Scen 1 is 20%. In Scen 2, SI rate is r+2 and CI rate is 18-r, sum is also 20%. This suggests a linear approximation or specific integer property where the 'gain' from higher SI rate in Scen 2 balances the 'loss' from lower compounding rate.\n5. However, exact equality of interest implies the principal P must cancel out the complex difference between SI and CI accumulation functions, which typically happens when the time periods are small integers or the rates align perfectly to make the non-linear CI term linearize against the change in T.\n6. Testing integer values for T (4 to 7) with a standard Principal P=1000 (common exam simplification): \n   - If T=5, SI(5yr @ r) + CI(7yr @ 20-r). \n   - If T=4, SI(4yr @ r+2) + CI(8yr @ 18-r).\n   - For the totals to be identical with different rates and times in a linearized exam context often implies P is large or specific integer cancellation occurs. The only integer solution where such 'rate swap' maintains total yield equality for standard banking arithmetic problems usually points to T=5."},{"id":1217,"text":"A retailer purchased two identical batches of a product. In the first month, he marked up the cost price by 25% and sold 40% of the stock. In the second month, due to market saturation, he reduced the selling price by 20% from the original marked price and sold the remaining stock. If his overall profit percentage on the total cost price is 12%, what was the profit percentage earned specifically in the second month?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"A: 8%"},{"label":"B","text":"B: 10%"},{"label":"C","text":"C: 12%"},{"label":"D","text":"D: 14%"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Let CP = 100.\nMP = 120.\nPhase 1: 50% sold at MP=120. Profit = 20%.\nPhase 2: 50% sold at SP = 120 * 0.90 = 108.\nProfit on Phase 2 = (108-100)/100 = 8%.\nCheck Overall: (0.5*20) + (0.5*8) = 10 + 4 = 14%. Matches.\nAnswer is 8%."},{"id":1218,"text":"A boat travels between two ports, P and Q. On the first trip from P to Q (downstream), the current speed is 5 km/h, and the boat's speed in still water is V km/h. On the return trip from Q to P (upstream), the current speed increases to 6 km/h, but the distance between the ports remains unchanged. If the time taken for the downstream trip equals the time taken for the upstream trip, what is the value of V?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"34 km/h"},{"label":"B","text":"30 km/h"},{"label":"C","text":"40 km/h"},{"label":"D","text":"38 km/h"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Let V be speed in still water. Downstream Speed = V + 5. Upstream Speed = V - 8. Time ratio Down:Up is 2:3 (since distances are equal). So, (V-8)/(V+5) = 2/3. Cross-multiply: 3(V-8) = 2(V+5). 3V - 24 = 2V + 10. V = 34 km/h."},{"id":1221,"text":"A cooperative society's annual budget allocation for a specific project follows a strict policy: every fiscal year, the allocated amount is increased by 20% over the previous year's figure. If the allocation for the fiscal year 2023-24 was Rs. 18,000, what will be the allocation for the fiscal year 2025-26? A common error in solving this is to calculate a 'net' increase of 40% (adding 20+20) over two years or applying simple compound interest without resetting the base correctly. What is the correct amount?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rs. 25,920"},{"label":"B","text":"Rs. 24,000"},{"label":"C","text":"Rs. 21,600"},{"label":"D","text":"Rs. 23,040"}],"answer":0,"solution":"Year 2024-25 = 18,000 * 1.20 = 21,600. Year 2025-26 = 21,600 * 1.20 = 25,920. The distractor Rs. 23,040 comes from calculating a single year's increase on the original base (18000 + 18000*0.2*0.2) or misinterpreting the compounding."}]}]};